{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DSnsCQfL9uHa5GnBdbAtpH","type":"tool_result","content":"1620\t| spider | Brass Spider | 2 | M | 22 | 13 | +4 | 1d6 | 1.5 | 0.6 | 5 | 110 | 30% of hits poison | 25% potionAntidote |\n1621\t| sentinel | Clockwork Sentinel | 2 | L | 50 | 16 | +5 | 2d6 | 2.8 | 1.6 | 5 | 350 | construct: immune to Sleep, Hold, Poison and Turn; lightning does ×1.5; 0.8 s wind-up | ringOfWarding, potionGreaterHealing |\n1622\t| hound | Lidless Hound | 3 | M | 20 | 13 | +5 | 1d8 | 1.3 | 0.5 | 6 (hearing) | 120 | always aware within 6 cells | — |\n1623\t| seer | Gloam Seer | 3 | M | 18 | 12 | +3 | 1d4 | 2.2 | 1.0 | 6 | 180 | casts a **Locking Bolt** (projectile, 2d6, 6 cells) every 6 s in line; a **Hold** (1 member, 6 s, save) every 12 s; keepAway at 3 | 30% staff; 20% potionHealing; 15% elixirClarity |\n1624\t| warden | Gloam Warden | 3 | M | 26 | 15 | +6 | 1d10 | 2.2 | 0.9 | 5 | 150 | reach: strikes from 2 cells in a clear line | 25% glaive; 15% studdedLeather |\n1625\t| gazer | Gazer | 3, 4 | S | 10 | 14 | +4 | 1d3 | 2.0 | 0.8 | 5 | 90 | flies; **Spark Gaze** (1d6, ranged, line of 3 or less) every 3 s | — |\n1626\t| golem | Lockjaw Golem | 4 | L | 60 | 17 | +7 | 2d8 | 3.0 | 1.8 | 5 | 400 | construct; lightning ×1.5, blunt ×1.25 | golemA: potionGreaterHealing |\n1627\t| boltholder | The Bolt-Holder | 4 | L | 320 | 15 | +8 | see §4.7.4 | 3.5 / 2.8 / 2.2 | drift 4 s | all | 3000 | phases, locks, absorbs lightning | — |\n1628\t\n1629\t**Balance targets** (the bot measures them, §14). On Normal, with the premade party plus the NPCs:\n1630\t- a single Drain Rat dies to one or two hits;\n1631\t- a fresh party survives the first Rat Channel fight above 60% HP;\n1632\t- Snick takes 20 to 40 s and is the first time a member is likely to go Down;\n1633\t- the Sentinel takes 30 to 60 s;\n1634\t- the boss takes 2.5 to 5 minutes.\n1635\t- The party should use 1 to 3 potions and 1 to 2 rests per floor.\n1636\t\n1637\t### 7.7 Items\n1638\t\n1639\tSpeed is the cooldown in seconds. Classes are F (Fighter), P (Paladin), R (Ranger), C (Cleric), M (Mage) and T (Thief). Two-handed is 2H. Defense values are \"+n\".\n1640\t\n1641\t**Weapons:**\n1642\t\n1643\t| Id | Name | Stats | Classes | Found | Description |\n1644\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1645\t| rustyDagger | Rusty Dagger | 1d3, 1.2, throwable | all | f1 (2,13) | \"Pitted and dull, but sharper than your fingernails.\" |\n1646\t| dagger | Dagger | 1d4, 1.2, throwable | all | Mage start, drops | \"A plain blade. It goes where you put it.\" |\n1647\t| shortSword | Short Sword | 1d6, 1.6 | F P R T | f1 (3,2); Ranger and Thief start | \"Short enough for a drain, long enough for a rat.\" |\n1648\t| longSword | Long Sword | 1d8, 2.0 | F P R | Fighter and Paladin start | \"Hasp steel, with a lockwright's mark on the tang.\" |\n1649\t| wardensBlade | Warden's Blade | 1d8+2, 2.0, +2 to-hit | F P R | f3 (22,11) | \"Black as wet slate. It never seems to dull.\" |\n1650\t| handAxe | Hand Axe | 1d6, 1.8, throwable | F P R | skeleton drops | \"Balanced for splitting kindling, or Latchkins.\" |\n1651\t| lockbreaker | Lockbreaker | 1d10+1, 3.0, 2H, +1 to-hit | F P | f2 (13,5) | \"A guild axe made for doors that would not open. It does not argue.\" |\n1652\t| mace | Mace | 1d6+1, 2.0, blunt | F P R C | Cleric start | \"Flanged iron on an oak haft. Honest work.\" |\n1653\t| copperhandsMaul | Copperhand's Maul | 1d8+1, 2.4, blunt | F P C | Durgan's | \"Dwarf-forged. The copper bands are for luck, and for weight.\" |\n1654\t| warhammer | Warhammer | 1d6+1, 2.4, blunt | F P R C | f2 (11,3) | \"Half tool, half argument.\" |\n1655\t| staff | Quarterstaff | 1d6, 1.8, 2H, blunt | all | Seer drops; Veil's | \"Ash, iron-shod at both ends.\" |\n1656\t| spear | Spear | 1d6, 2.2, **reach**, throwable | F P R T | Latchkin drops (10%) | \"Long enough to reach past a friend.\" |\n1657\t| glaive | Glaive | 1d10, 2.8, 2H, **reach** | F P R | Warden drops | \"A Warden's polearm, its blade etched with a shut eye.\" |\n1658\t| tumblersPick | Tumbler's Pick | 1d6+1, 1.8, ×2 vs constructs | F P R T | f2 (9,15) | \"A locksmith's pick-hammer. Clockwork hates it.\" |\n1659\t\n1660\t**Missile weapons and ammo:**\n1661\t\n1662\t| Id | Name | Stats | Classes | Found | Description |\n1663\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1664\t| sling | Sling | 1d4, 2.0, ammo slingStones | all | f1 (1,5) | \"Leather and string. Older than locks.\" |\n1665\t| shortBow | Short Bow | 1d6, 1.8, ammo arrows, 2H | F P R T | Ranger start (in pack) | \"Elf-made, light as a thought.\" |\n1666\t| lightCrossbow | Light Crossbow | 1d8, 2.6, ammo bolts, 2H | F P R T | f1 (20,1) | \"Wound by a crank. Someone loved this, before the Latchkins.\" |\n1667\t| heavyCrossbow | Heavy Crossbow | 1d10+1, 3.4, ammo bolts, 2H | F P R | f3 (13,7) | \"It punches through mail, and patience.\" |\n1668\t| darts | Darts | 1d3, 1.2, thrown, stack | all | f1 (5,1); Thief start | \"Little iron wasps.\" |\n1669\t| slingStones / arrows / bolts | ammo | stack 30 | — | f1 (1,5) ×12; Ranger ×20; f1 (20,2) ×12, f3 (17,7) ×10 | \"Bolts: the city's other export.\" |\n1670\t\n1671\t**Armour and wearables:**\n1672\t\n1673\t| Id | Name | Stats | Classes | Found | Description |\n1674\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1675\t| travellersRobe | Traveller's Robe | body +0 | M | Mage start | \"Many pockets, all of them full of crumbs.\" |\n1676\t| paddedJerkin | Padded Jerkin | body +1 | all | Latchkin drops (5%); Veil's | \"Quilted, and quietly proud of it.\" |\n1677\t| leatherArmor | Leather Armour | body +2 | F P R C T | starts; f1 (13,1) | \"Boiled, stitched and smelling of both.\" |\n1678\t| studdedLeather | Studded Leather | body +3 | F P R T | Warden drops (15%) | \"Leather with ambitions.\" |\n1679\t| chainShirt | Chain Shirt | body +4 | F P R C | Paladin start; f2 (17,15) | \"Ten thousand little rings, all of them cold.\" |\n1680\t| scaleMail | Scale Mail | body +5 | F P C | Durgan's | |\n1681\t| robeOfTheLintel | Robe of the Lintel | body +2, +1 INT, +1 level-1 slot | M | f3, SQ3 | \"Embroidered with doors. Every door is open.\" |\n1682\t| buckler | Buckler | shield +1 | F P R C T | Durgan's | |\n1683\t| woodenShield | Wooden Shield | shield +1 | F P C | Fighter and Paladin start | |\n1684\t| ironShield | Iron Shield | shield +2 | F P C | f2 (13,15) | |\n1685\t| leatherCap | Leather Cap | head +1 | F P R C T | f1 (3,8) | |\n1686\t| ironHelm | Iron Helm | head +1 | F P R C | Durgan's | |\n1687\t| ratKingsCrown | Rat King's Crown | head +1 | all | f1 lair | \"Twisted tin, worn by something with too many tails.\" |\n1688\t| tumblerwrightsGoggles | Tumblerwright's Goggles | head +0; always **Seeing** (secrets and traps glint) | all | f2, SQ2 | \"The world's seams show plainly through them.\" |\n1689\t| lidlessWard | Lidless Ward | neck: immune to Hold and Gaze | all | f3, Veil | \"Shaped like a shut eye. What it cannot see cannot hold you.\" |\n1690\t| amuletOfVigor | Amulet of Vigor | neck: +1 CON | all | f1, Snick | |\n1691\t| bracersOfDefense | Bracers of Defense | arms +2 | all | f3 (22,13) | |\n1692\t| ringOfMending | Ring of Mending | 1 HP every 30 s | all | f1, SQ1 | \"Warm, as if someone just took it off.\" |\n1693\t| ringOfWarding | Ring of Warding | +1 Def, +1 saves | all | f2, Sentinel | |\n1694\t| quickstepBoots | Quickstep Boots | cooldowns −10% | all | f3 (13,10) | |\n1695\t\n1696\t**Consumables and readables:**\n1697\t\n1698\t| Id | Name | Effect | Found |\n1699\t|---|---|---|---|\n1700\t| ration | Ration | +50 food | 14 placed (f1: 4, f2: 5, f3: 5), plus one each at the start and rat drops |\n1701\t| ironRation | Iron Ration | +100 food | 4 placed: f1 (20,12), f2 (14,5), f3 (13,1), f3 (21,14) |\n1702\t| potionHealing | Potion of Healing | 2d4+2 | 6 placed (f1 (8,3), (19,10); f2 (20,3); f3 (15,1), (16,10) ×2), plus Seer drops |\n1703\t| potionGreaterHealing | Potion of Greater Healing | 4d4+4, wakes a Down member | f2 (6,10); the Sentinel's and golemA's drops |\n1704\t| potionAntidote | Antidote | cures poison | f3 (4,8) and drops |\n1705\t| elixirClarity | Elixir of Clarity | restores 1 spent slot of the highest level | Seer drops (15%) |\n1706\t| scroll ×9 | Scroll of *spell* | a mage casts it or scribes it | §7.4 |\n1707\t| scrollRaising | Scroll of Raising | a cleric or paladin reads it: Raise from Rest | f2 (11,5), f3 (20,14) |\n1708\t| wandUnlatching | Wand of Unlatching | Unlatch, 3 charges, anyone | f2 (1,7) |\n1709\t| wandSparks | Wand of Sparks | Spark Dart (2 darts), 8 charges | f3 (13,1) |\n1710\t\n1711\t**Tools, keys, wards, quest items, lore and junk:**\n1712\t\n1713\t| Id | Name | Effect | Found |\n1714\t|---|---|---|---|\n1715\t| lockpicks | Lockpicks | 6 uses; a failed pick snaps one | Thief start, Tamsin |\n1716\t| holySymbol | Key of the Threshold | a cleric's holy symbol | Cleric start |\n1717\t| veilsLantern | Veil's Lantern | a holy symbol | Veil's |\n1718\t| spellbook | Spellbook | holds known spells | Mage start |\n1719\t| ironKey / drainwardensKey / gearKey / boneKey / bentKey | keys | as wired | §7.4 |\n1720\t| copperWard / brassWard / ironWard | the Three Wards | the Undergate | §7.4 |\n1721\t| tumblerGear (I–IV) | Tumbler Gear | the clock deed | f2 |\n1722\t| tornPage / guildLedger / seersPsalm | notes | lore and hints (§7.9) | f1 (6,14), f2 (10,3), f3 (5,4) |\n1723\t| rock / ironIngot / bone | junk | heavy things for plates | §7.4 |\n1724\t| ratCrown | Rat Crown (coin) | race score | race |\n1725\t\n1726\t### 7.8 Spells\n1727\t\n1728\tArcane spells come from the spellbook and its scrolls. Prayers are to the Warder of Thresholds, the city's god of doors. The numbers are × ★spell power.\n1729\t\n1730\t| Id | Name | Kind and level | Target | Effect | Look |\n1731\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1732\t| sparkDart | Spark Dart | arcane 1 | line | 1 + ⌊lvl/2⌋ darts (3 at most), each 1d4+1, always hitting the first monster within 6 cells | violet-white glows, sparks |\n1733\t| wardOfBrass | Ward of Brass | arcane 1 | member | +3 Def until it absorbs 8 + lvl damage, or until rest | brass shimmer on the card |\n1734\t| findSeams | Find Seams | arcane 1 | party | 90 s of Seeing | gold outlines |\n1735\t| slumber | Slumber | arcane 1 | front | sleep 20 s: living S and M monsters, an HP pool of 10 + 3×lvl, lowest first | drifting z's |\n1736\t| unlatch | Unlatch | arcane 2 | door | opens a magic seal or a simple lock | a ghost key turns |\n1737\t| frostbite | Frostbite | arcane 2 | front | 2d6 cold to all in the front cell, and Slowed 10 s | blue shards, a frost ring |\n1738\t| featherStep | Feather Step | arcane 2 | party | 120 s of Floating | the view rises 3 units; wind |\n1739\t| forkedLightning | Forked Lightning | arcane 3 | line | 3d6 (+1d6 per level above 5) to every monster along 5 cells; it bounces back once off a near wall and never hurts the party; **it heals the Bolt-Holder** | jagged cyan bars, a flash |\n1740\t| blazingOrb | Blazing Orb | arcane 3 | line | at the first monster cell or wall: 3d6 + lvl fire to all there, half to the 4 neighbouring cells' monsters | an orange orb, an explosion, a light flash |\n1741\t| mend | Mend | prayer 1 | member | heals 1d8 + 1 + ⌊lvl/2⌋; wakes a Down member | green glints |\n1742\t| steadyHand | Steady Hand | prayer 1 | party | +1 to-hit and saves, 60 s | a golden hand icon |\n1743\t| turnDead | Turn the Dead | prayer 1 | front | undead flee 12 s; undead with HP ≤ 2×lvl crumble | a white flare |\n1744\t| purge | Purge Venom | prayer 2 | member | cures poison and heals 1d4 | |\n1745\t| holdFast | Hold Fast | prayer 2 | front | humanoids are Held 10 s (25% save) | golden chains |\n1746\t| loaves | Loaves of the Hearth | prayer 2 | party | all food to 100 | bread, a warm glow |\n1747\t| greaterMend | Greater Mend | prayer 3 | member | heals 3d8 + lvl; wakes Down | |\n1748\t| raise | Raise from Rest | prayer 3 | dead member | back at 1 HP | a rising light |\n1749\t| freeHinge | Free Hinge | prayer 3 | party | cures Held; immune to Hold and Gaze for 120 s | a hinge sigil on the cards |\n1750\t\n1751\t### 7.9 The party, the NPCs and their scripts\n1752\t\n1753\t**The premade party** (Quick Start; also the Rat Run's at level 2):\n1754\t\n1755\t| Place | Name | Race and class | STR DEX CON INT WIS | HP | Gear | Prepared |\n1756\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1757\t| 1 | Brannoc Ironside | Human Fighter | 17 12 16 9 10 | 12 | longSword, woodenShield, leatherArmor, ration | — |\n1758\t| 2 | Ysa Thornfeather | Elf Ranger | 14 17 12 12 13 | 8 | shortSword ×2, leatherArmor, shortBow and arrows ×20 (pack), ration | — |\n1759\t| 3 | Father Cobb | Dwarf Cleric (beard) | 13 9 16 10 16 | 10 | mace, holySymbol, leatherArmor, ration | Mend ×2 |\n1760\t| 4 | Odelia Fenn | Human Mage | 8 14 11 17 11 | 4 | dagger, spellbook (Spark Dart, Find Seams, Slumber), travellersRobe, darts ×4, ration | Spark Dart, Slumber |\n1761\t\n1762\t**The NPCs:**\n1763\t\n1764\t| Name | Race and class, level | STR DEX CON INT WIS | HP | Gear | Prepared |\n1765\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1766\t| Tamsin Pell | Halfling Thief 2 | 10 17 13 13 9 | 12 | dagger, darts ×6, leatherArmor, lockpicks | — |\n1767\t| Durgan Copperhand | Dwarf Fighter 3 | 17 10 17 11 10 | 28 | copperhandsMaul, buckler, ironHelm, scaleMail | — |\n1768\t| Sister Veil | Human Cleric 4 | 10 13 12 14 17 | 23 | staff, veilsLantern, paddedJerkin | Mend ×3, Steady Hand, Purge ×2, Hold Fast |\n1769\t\n1770\t**Scripts** (E.Story nodes; the choices are in brackets):\n1771\t- **tamsin** (after LV2; she steps out of the cage):\n1772\t  - \"Took you long enough! Three days in a birdcage, and the little latch-thieves poking me with forks.\"\n1773\t  - \"Tamsin Pell, journeywoman of the Lockwrights. Or I was, before the locks went mad.\"\n1774\t  - \"You're going down, aren't you? Toward the thing that's doing this. Take me along. I open what your keys can't.\"\n1775\t  - **[Join us]** \"Then let's go and annoy something big.\" She joins.\n1776\t  - **[Go home, Tamsin]** \"Suit yourself. Take these. You'll need them more than me.\" She gives the lockpicks and leaves: \"Mind the right channel. That's where they nest.\"\n1777\t- **durgan1** (through the bars):\n1778\t  - \"Don't stand there gawping. Those levers on the wall behind you are the Tumbler Lock. My own design, and I'm locked on the wrong side of it.\"\n1779\t  - \"The creed is carved in the workshop. First falls, second rises, third falls. Can't reach the blasted things from in here.\"\n1780\t- **durgan2** (when G5 opens):\n1781\t  - \"Ha! Durgan Copperhand thanks you. The guild's dead and gone, but its halls aren't done with me yet.\"\n1782\t  - \"Whatever's below took my brothers' work and twisted it. I'd like a word with it. A hammer-shaped word.\"\n1783\t  - \"And take this gear. Found it in my cell. Looks like it belongs to the big clock.\"\n1784\t  - **[Come with us]** He joins.\n1785\t  - **[Find your own way out]** \"Hmph. Then luck to you.\" He leaves; the gear is given either way.\n1786\t- **ysolde1** (the Clock Hall):\n1787\t  - \"Living feet, in the Tumbler Halls. It has been a long time.\"\n1788\t  - \"I was Guildmistress Ysolde Vane. We forged the Watcher for the Undergate: an eye that would never close, for a lock that must never open.\"\n1789\t  - \"We gave it seven Great Bolts to hold. And it learned to love holding. Now it holds the whole city, one lock at a time.\"\n1790\t  - \"Three Wards open the Undergate: copper, brass and iron. Ours, the brass, sleeps in the Guild Vault. What is sealed by art, art unseals.\"\n1791\t  - \"And if you would do an old woman a kindness, the Great Clock has lost its four gears. Let it tell the hour once more.\"\n1792\t- **ysoldeHint** (a whisper): \"The guild hid its catches in plain sight. Look to the walls.\"\n1793\t- **ysolde2** (after the Sentinel): \"Close its eye, little keys. Close it for all of us.\" She fades.\n1794\t- **veil** (after LV3):\n1795\t  - \"Do not look at me so. Your eyes are loud, surface-folk.\"\n1796\t  - \"I am Veil, once a Seer of the Lidless. I shut my eyes to the Watcher's voice, and for that they chained me here to be… corrected.\"\n1797\t  - \"You seek the Iron Ward. The Wardens keep it in the Reliquary, past their barracks. There is another way. I know the stones that move.\"\n1798\t  - \"Take me from this place and I will show you. Leave me, and pray the Wardens are asleep.\"\n1799\t  - **[We will help you]** If a place is free: \"Then I walk with you.\" If the party is full: \"Then take this. It kept me sane.\" (the `lidlessWard`). Either way: \"Push where the moss does not grow.\" H2 opens and `veilHelped` is set.\n1800\t  - **[Stay here, seer]** \"Then go with your eyes open. It will find you.\" `veilRefused` is set.\n1801\t- **Snick's barks:**\n1802\t  - `snick1`: \"MINE! All the shiny bolts are MINE!\"\n1803\t  - `snick2`: \"Latchkins! To your king!\"\n1804\t  - `snick3`: \"…not… fair…\"\n1805\t- **The Bolt-Holder's lines:**\n1806\t  - `eye1`: \"Little keys. You have come so far, only to be turned.\"\n1807\t  - `eye2`: \"Every lock is a promise. I KEEP THEM ALL.\"\n1808\t  - `eye3`: \"You… unbolt… ME?\"\n1809\t  - `eye4`: \"Then be locked in the dark FOREVER!\"\n1810\t  - `eye5`: \"Who… will keep… the promises…?\"\n1811\t- **The notes:**\n1812\t  - **tornPage**: \"…they take the bolts, all the iron, every nail and hinge, down the right channel to HIM. Snick says HE pays in shiny. Snick says HE sees everything…\"\n1813\t  - **guildLedger**: \"Tumbler Lock, cell 4: the creed governs it. Undergate wards: copper to the Drainwarden, brass to the Vault, iron to the Lidless, who swore to keep it. Watcher: bolts tested, seven of seven. God help us if it learns to like it.\"\n1814\t  - **seersPsalm**: the candle order (§7.4.3).\n1815\t\n1816\t---\n1817\t\n1818\t## 8. Dev Mode (from the pause menu; hidden in hub sessions)\n1819\t\n1820\t- **The panel** is a 10-foot list in the game's own style.\n1821\t  - L1 and R1 switch tabs; up and down move between rows; left and right change a slider (hold to speed up).\n1822\t  - ✕ toggles or runs a row, □ resets the row, △ resets the page, ○ goes back.\n1823\t  - The mouse drags sliders and clicks toggles.\n1824\t- **Storage.** Changes apply live and persist in storage key `boltholder.dev`. **Reset to defaults** is a row at the top of Tuning.\n1825\t\n1826\t| Tab | Rows |\n1827\t|---|---|\n1828\t| **Tuning: Combat** | Party damage × (0.25–4, default 1) · Party to-hit (−5…+10, 0) · Attack cooldown × (0.25–3, 1) · Spell power × (0.25–4, 1) |\n1829\t| **Tuning: Monsters** | Monster HP × (0.25–4, 1) · Monster damage × (0.25–4, 1) · Monster interval × (0.25–3, 1) · Sight (1–10 cells, 5) · Wind-up (0.1–1.5 s, 0.5) · Re-engage delay (0–2 s, 0.6) · Boss HP × (0.25–4, 1) · Loot chance × (0–3, 1) |\n1830\t| **Tuning: Exploration** | Step time (0.05–0.6 s, 0.28) · Turn time (0.05–0.5 s, 0.2) · Throw range (1–8, 4) · Trap damage × (0–4, 1) · Button window (2–15 s, 6) |\n1831\t| **Tuning: Survival** | Hunger rate × (0–5, 1) · Rest heal × (0–5, 1) · Rest interruption (0–50%, 4) · XP gain × (0–5, 1) · Time in menus (0–1, 0.25) |\n1832\t| **Cheats** | God mode · Infinite spells · No cooldowns · No hunger · One-hit kills · Noclip · Reveal map · Show secrets · Freeze monsters · Give all keys and wards |\n1833\t| **Warp** | floor ◀ ▶, then that floor's named waypoints (data: `waypoints` in each floor, e.g. \"F1 Start\", \"F1 Latchkin Den\", \"F1 Snick's Hall\", \"F1 Cistern\", \"F2 Landing\", \"F2 Clock Hall\", \"F2 Endless Hall\", \"F2 Lock Room\", \"F2 Weight Hall\", \"F2 Vault\", \"F3 Ossuary\", \"F3 Gauntlet\", \"F3 Chapel\", \"F3 Penance\", \"F3 Barracks\", \"F3 Undergate\", \"F4 Antechamber\", \"F4 Arena\", \"Rat Run\") · Next floor · Boss · Ending |\n1834\t| **Party** | Heal all · Revive all · +1 level for everyone · Max food · Give item (by category) · Learn every spell · Fill every slot · Add NPC (Tamsin, Durgan, Veil) · Reset to the premade party |\n1835\t| **Spawn** | monster type ◀ ▶, then Spawn in front (group size ◀ ▶) · Kill all on this floor · Clear wanderers |\n1836\t| **Debug** | Overlays: cell and facing; monster AI states and timers over each monster; wiring lines on the automap; sim time per step; the last 20 events · **Auto-play to floor end** (the walkthrough bot, with or without cheats) · Start the attract mode now · Play the intro or ending · Sound test (every sfx, song and voice, with a test line) · Fake hub ghosts (2 dummies walking a loop) |\n1837\t\n1838\t---\n1839\t\n1840\t## 9. Attract mode\n1841\t\n1842\t- **The trigger.** 10.0 s with no input (§5.6) on the title or any of its menus (Load, Rat Run, About). This includes touch-only devices.\n1843\t- **The `attract` scene** runs a **director of vignettes**. Each vignette is data:\n1844\t\n1845\t  ```js\n1846\t  { name, floor, at: [x, y, dir], party: 'demo',\n1847\t    cheats: { god: true, infiniteSpells: true, noHunger: true, noclip: false },\n1848\t    steps: [ bot commands ], seconds }\n1849\t  ```\n1850\t\n1851\t  - The `demo` party is the premade four at level 5 plus Tamsin and Durgan, knowing every spell, with good gear.\n1852\t  - The steps use the same commands as players (§3.5), so the bot is the one in `72-bot.js`.\n1853\t\n1854\t| # | Vignette | What it shows | About |\n1855\t|---|---|---|---|\n1856\t| 1 | The Drains | take the dagger; LV1 and the gate rising; into the Rat Channel; Party Strike on the rats (damage pops); read N1 | 18 s |\n1857\t| 2 | Latchkins | the Den fight; LV2; Tamsin's lines typing with babble (auto-advancing) | 16 s |\n1858\t| 3 | Stones and plates | the rock put down on P1, G2 rising; walking through I1 (the dissolve) | 14 s |\n1859\t| 4 | Spellcraft | Spark Dart down a corridor, Mend on a card, Blazing Orb on skeletons (f2 Workshop) | 14 s |\n1860\t| 5 | The Party screen | it opens; the focus moves; a sword is equipped; the automap opens and closes | 12 s |\n1861\t| 6 | Clockwork | the Sentinel fight with Forked Lightning (×1.5) | 14 s |\n1862\t| 7 | The Gauntlet | ducking Seer bolts into the niches | 14 s |\n1863\t| 8 | The Bolt-Holder | a Great Lock turned, Chain Lightning dodged behind a pillar, Bolt Rain, the cage opening | 22 s |\n1864\t| 9 | Title | the logo and \"Press any button\" | 5 s |\n1865\t\n1866\t- **The loop.** After vignette 9 it starts over. A \"DEMO\" tag sits top left, and \"Press [glyph] / any key\" blinks at the bottom centre.\n1867\t- **Any input exits at once.** The input is consumed so the title menu doesn't act on it; the title scene, its music and its camera come back. The demo never writes saves, settings or dev storage, and never touches the player's party.\n1868\t- **Robustness.** Every vignette is time-boxed. If a step stalls for more than 4 s or throws, the director skips to the next vignette (and logs it in dev builds).\n1869\t\n1870\t---\n1871\t\n1872\t## 10. Multiplayer\n1873\t\n1874\t### 10.1 AI Hub session (`AIHub.active`): the Rat Run ghost race, 1 to 4 players\n1875\t\n1876\t1. **Boot. Connect first, build second.** The harness gives each copy **about 11 s to say hello** (`connect()`) and **20 s more to call `ready()`**. A 3D page reaches the game's module only after three.js and Rapier have downloaded, so:\n1877\t   - Put a tiny classic script in `<head>`, right after the session client: `window.__hubInfo = (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;`. It runs during parsing, before any module.\n1878\t   - The game module then does `const info = await window.__hubInfo`. Events that arrive before handlers attach are kept, so nothing is lost.\n1879\t   - If `info` is `null`, boot normally.\n1880\t   - In a session, build only the race world and the UI, and skip the title, attract and menus.\n1881\t2. **Seeding.** Seed every `B.rng` stream from `AIHub.rng('deal')`, so every copy deals the same monsters and rolls at the start.\n1882\t3. **Our own card** (the `hubcard` scene, drawn over the race floor's first view) shows:\n1883\t   - the logo and \"THE RAT RUN\";\n1884\t   - the goal, \"Fastest party out of the Rat Run wins\";\n1885\t   - the controls, with glyphs for this device;\n1886\t   - every player in their seat colour (`info.players[i].color`) with a ✓ when ready (`card.ready`);\n1887\t   - \"Ready ✕ / Enter · More time △\" and the countdown (`card.left`).\n1888\t\n1889\t   ✕ or Enter sends `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △ sends `AIHub.answer('more')`, and pressing it again takes it back. The card has no menus or choices, and any randomness on it comes from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n1890\t4. **Ready and start.** Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the race sim and its `World3D` exist, with no key press; `prepare()` may finish during the card's countdown. On `start`, show the countdown 3-2-1 from the negative `AIHub.time()`; input unlocks at 0. Measure this in M0 and M6 with `players=4`. On this machine's SwiftShader, aim for hello under 3 s and ready under 12 s.\n1891\t5. **During the run.**\n1892\t   - Every 100 ms, `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', area: 'race', cx, cy, dir, x, y, yaw, cp, hp }, { reliable: false })`.\n1893\t   - About once a second, `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`.\n1894\t   - **Ghosts** are the others' cloaked rigs in their seat colours, with name tags drawn with `E.font` (never as HTML). They are lerped to the reported positions, shown when the `area` matches, and never block or affect anything.\n1895\t6. **Finishing.** Reaching `>` sends `AIHub.result({ time: Math.round(AIHub.time()), stats: { Kills, Crowns } })` and `send({ t: 'done', time })`. The screen shows \"Escaped in 01:42.3. Waiting for the others.\"\n1896\t7. **A wipe** sends `result({ score })` once and shows \"Your party fell. The others run on.\"\n1897\t8. **`time-up`** sends `result({ score })` if nothing was sent yet. **`leave`** removes that ghost. **`end`** clears and locks the input, stops the music and sfx, and shows the reason; the hub draws the results.\n1898\t9. **The rules in a session.**\n1899\t   - No saves, no Dev Mode.\n1900\t   - The pause menu shows only Resume, Settings and Controls.\n1901\t   - No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open`, and no network but the hub.\n1902\t   - Options is ignored while Create is held.\n1903\t   - `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">`.\n1904\t\n1905\t### 10.2 On its own\n1906\t\n1907\t- **Rat Run from the title** is the same race, solo, on the local clock (the code is shared in `73-hub.js`, with its clock and ghost source swapped).\n1908\t- **The best-run ghost.** The best time and a 10 Hz trail of `{ t, cx, cy, dir }` are kept in storage `boltholder.ratrun`, and the trail runs beside you as a **golden ghost**.\n1909\t- **The results** show time, best, crowns and kills, with Run again and Title.\n1910\t- The campaign is single-player.\n1911\t\n1912\t---\n1913\t\n1914\t## 11. About and Credits, and the final report\n1915\t\n1916\t- **The About and Credits screen** opens from the title and the pause menu. Its pages are switched with L1 and R1 and scrolled with the d-pad:\n1917\t  1. **The game:** the title, the tagline \"A thousand locks. One eye.\", the version and the build date.\n1918\t  2. **Source Information:** every field of TASK.md's list (Date, Source, Plan, Genre and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage).\n1919\t  3. **Testing Feedback** (4 answers).\n1920\t  4. **Engine Feedback** (6 answers).\n1921\t  5. **Prompt Feedback** (4 answers).\n1922\t  6. **Credits:**\n1923\t     - the game by (your model);\n1924\t     - the engine: my-3D2dge (MIT);\n1925\t     - three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), the AI Hub session client;\n1926\t     - any store asset sets used (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG, CC0);\n1927\t     - \"Inspired by Eye of the Beholder (Westwood Associates / SSI, 1991). No names, text or assets from it are used.\"\n1928\t\n1929\t  Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n1930\t- **One source of truth.** Keep the text in `14-data-text.js` as `B.ABOUT`. `tools/build.mjs` writes `exit-interview.json` from that same object and checks that it parses. Your chat reply copies the same text.\n1931\t- **Prefilled values** (confirm or replace them with your own run's facts):\n1932\t\n1933\t  | Field | Value |\n1934\t  |---|---|\n1935\t  | Source | Eye of the Beholder (Westwood Associates / SSI, 1991; MS-DOS and Amiga) |\n1936\t  | Plan | `PLAN.md` |\n1937\t  | Genre and Perspective | real-time, first-person, grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler; a first-person party view with tweened steps and quarter turns, plus a top-down automap |\n1938\t  | Tech | my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the 2D engine from `dist/handoff`) and my-3D2dge 3D v0.85.2 (three.js r182 WebGPU / WebGL 2 and Rapier 0.19.3, via jsDelivr); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for the tests; plain JavaScript in one HTML file |\n1939\t  | Art Direction | the engine's native retro-modern look: code-drawn low-res 3D (pixel resolution, toon light, outlines, fog), rigs as pixel-art cards, procedural textures, pen-drawn creatures and mechanisms, a brass \"lockwork\" UI |\n1940\t  | Animation | the engine's procedural rigs and moves (E.Humanoid, E.Blob, E.MOVES), a tweened first-person camera, pen-animated creatures and mechanisms, first-person weapon overlays |\n1941\t  | Audio | the engine's chip synth (step-sequencer music with combat layers and stings, synthesized sfx); voices from a custom WebAudio formant babble synth (Animalese/Simlish style) |\n1942\t  | Online | AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1 to 4 players (the Rat Run); a solo time trial against the local best ghost |\n1943\t  | Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage | your run's facts (the planning research is §1 of this plan) |\n1944\t\n1945\t- **`exit-interview.json`** (in the root, exactly TASK.md's shape). The `aiHub` part:\n1946\t\n1947\t  ```json\n1948\t  \"aiHub\": { \"name\": \"Eye of the Bolt-Holder\", \"tagline\": \"A thousand locks. One eye.\",\n1949\t    \"description\": \"A real-time, first-person party dungeon crawl beneath Hasp, the City of a Thousand Locks: four floors of drains, clockwork halls and eye-cults, levers, plates and keys, spells memorized at camp, and the caged Eye that holds the city's bolts.\",\n1950\t    \"type\": \"Game\", \"genre\": \"RPG\", \"source\": \"Eye of the Beholder (1991)\", \"series\": \"Eye of the Beholder\", \"players\": \"1–4\",\n1951\t    \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD move · D-pad/Q E turn · ✕/F use · □/Space strike · L2 R2/1-6 hands · △/I party\",\n1952\t    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"first-person\", \"fantasy\", \"retro\", \"exploration\", \"boss fights\"] }\n1953\t  ```\n1954\t\n1955\t  Fill `sourceInformation`, `testingFeedback` (4), `engineFeedback` (6) and `promptFeedback` (4) as plain text. Check it with `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`.\n1956\t\n1957\t---\n1958\t\n1959\t## 12. Build order and milestones\n1960\t\n1961\tEach milestone ends **shippable**: it builds, the one command passes and nothing half-done is visible. Build floor 1 completely before starting floor 2. The percentages are the rough share of effort.\n1962\t\n1963\t| # | Milestone | Build | Exit criteria (tests in §14) |\n1964\t|---|---|---|---|\n1965\t| **M0** | Foundation and spikes (10%) | Fetch (§3.2); folder skeleton; `tools/build.mjs`; `tests/run.mjs` with the Node harness and one browser smoke; `NullView`. Spikes: (a) the bundled page boots from `file://` to a corridor of floor 1's geometry; (b) THINGS: lever, button, catch, alcove with items, keyhole, plaque, `wallBlock` (it must match the level walls) and the illusion pass-through; (c) a pen creature (the leech) and a boss sketch; (d) `babble.plan` plus a playable voice; (e) the hub harness passing against a stub page with our metas | `node tests/run.mjs` green; the bundle opens from disk with no errors; harness `__hubCheck.pass` on the stub |\n1966\t| **M1** | The dungeon (15%) | `15-data-floors.js` (all 5 maps and tables, §7.4); the floor loader; movement; every feature in §4.2 with wiring; stairs and pits between floors; the Presenter building all floors (geometry, things, lights, fog); the automap; the log; Examine; Dev Warp, Noclip and Reveal map | content lint plus the walkthrough reachability for every floor; unit tests for every feature; walking all floors by hand with Warp |\n1967\t| **M2** | The party and the fight (15%) | races, classes, stats, formation; items, inventory, equipment, the Hand (take, put down, throw, place); combat (hands, cooldowns, rows, reach, missiles, Party Strike, statuses); all 16 monster types' minds and their visuals (§6.3); the HUD (§5.2); the glyph painter and prompts; the input map for pad, keys and mouse; the Party screen with focus navigation; first-person weapon overlays | combat maths and AI unit tests; UI-flow tests (Party screen, equipping, prompts per device); a scripted floor 1 fight sequence passes |\n1968\t| **M3** | Magic, camp, progress (12%) | all 18 spells, the Cast menu and targeting; scrolls, wands, Scribe; Camp: Rest (interruptions, safe rooms), Memorize, Pray, Formation, Eat; food; XP and levels; Down, Dead, Raise; game over; saves (3 slots plus the autosave); character creation; the premade party | **floor 1 is completed by the bot with real rules on Normal**; the save and load round-trip hash; the creation flow test |\n1969\t| **M4** | Story and the deep floors (18%) | E.Story scripts for all NPCs and barks (§7.9); recruiting and dismissing; Veil's two branches; floors 2–4 content (items, monsters, events, hints, deeds); the Undergate; **the Bolt-Holder** (§4.7.4); intro and ending stages and scripts; per-floor music with fight layers; every sfx; the babble voices | **the full playthrough bot passes, start to ending, on both Veil branches**; every deed is reachable |\n1970\t| **M5** | The shell (10%) | the title (3D stage, logo, menu); the **attract mode** (§9); **Dev Mode** (§8); Settings (§4.16) including PlayStation and Xbox glyphs; the touch-only notice; About and Credits; game over and ending screens; floor cards | attract tests (start at 10 s, any input exits, every vignette runs); Dev Mode tests (a slider changes behaviour, reset works); the touch notice test |\n1971\t| **M6** | Multiplayer (8%) | the hub session flow (§10.1) with our own card, ghosts and reporting; the solo Rat Run with the best ghost | the Node hub simulation passes; **the harness passes** for `players=2`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5` and `&scenario=host-leave` |\n1972\t| **M7** | Polish and ship (12%) | juice (telegraph clarity, hit-stop on crits, card shakes, ambience); a balance pass with the bot's metrics plus hand play using the Dev sliders; the look review (§14.6) at 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 1024×768; text overflow fixes; About text; `exit-interview.json`; the reply | the whole command green; screenshots reviewed; JSON parses; the bundle is under the deliverable name in the root |\n1973\t\n1974\t---\n1975\t\n1976\t## 13. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1977\t\n1978\t| # | Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n1979\t|---|---|---|---|\n1980\t| 1 | The 3D engine is outside the handoff and loads from a CDN | module order, `file://`, an offline viewer | The planning spike proved `file://` with a jsDelivr import map works and matches the vendored checksums. Pin the versions. Show a clear boot error if `E.World3D` is missing. *Optional, only if a reviewer needs an offline file:* inline the libraries as Blob URLs behind an import map injected before any module. |\n1981\t| 2 | Separating the sim from the 3D world | the kit mixes them; tests need Node | Define the Sim, Presenter and Command interfaces in M0. The `lint` test suite fails if a sim file (`20-`–`31-`) mentions `world`, `World3D`, `document`, `audio` or `Math.random` (the build only warns). Every system gets a Node test. |\n1982\t| 3 | Secret and illusory walls that must look exactly like the level walls | level walls are baked and instanced | Spike it in M0: `world.box` with the floor's `side` style, compared side by side in a screenshot. If it doesn't match, add `wallBlock` to the 3D engine using the level's wall material (PATCHES.md). Mask the illusion step with a 0.15 s dissolve. |\n1983\t| 4 | Pen-drawn creatures and the boss take time and can look poor | five bespoke bodies | Prototype the leech in M0 and the boss early in M4. Borrow from the horror kit's dogs. Judge motion with `tools/filmstrip.mjs`. Keep cards (rigs and blobs) for the other 11 types. |\n1984\t| 5 | The 10-foot UI is complex (paperdoll, backpack, details, spell targeting) | many widgets, three input styles | One geometric focus system; screens as data; UI-flow tests in Node (focus moves, carry and place); screenshots at three sizes. |\n1985\t| 6 | Real-time balance | swingy fights, wipes | ★Tuning sliders, difficulty multipliers, the bot's balance report (§14.5) every milestone, attack telegraphs and the re-engage delay. |\n1986\t| 7 | Content volume (4 floors plus a race) | time | Data-driven floors; the lint and walkthrough tests from M1; floor 1 finished before floor 2; cut only side items and dressing, never a system or a floor. |\n1987\t| 8 | The hub harness running a heavy 3D page (up to 4 iframes on SwiftShader) | it allows about 11 s for hello (`connect`) and 20 s more for `ready()`; it then plays about 6 s of random arrow and WASD keys, calls time-up and wants a `result` within its 5 s grace | Call `connect()` from a classic script in `<head>` before the modules load (§10.1). A session builds only the race world, calls `ready()` before `prepare()` finishes, and uses low 3D resolution and 1 torch shadow. Run the harness at M0 with a stub page carrying the real libraries, and again at M6. |\n1988\t| 9 | Determinism (saves, bots, hub fairness) | hidden `Math.random`, frame-dependent timing | Our own seeded RNG streams kept in the state; everything in the fixed steps; hash tests twice; the save → load → same-hash test. |\n1989\t| 10 | Audio | autoplay rules, an extra bus | The engine starts sound after the first input. The babble synth uses `game.audio.ctx` and the patched voice bus. In Node it is silent but `babble.plan` is tested. |\n1990\t| 11 | Attract mode stalls | bots in a changing game | Vignettes with cheats, time boxes, skip on a stall, a test that runs all of them. |\n1991\t| 12 | Input semantics (d-pad turns, the stick strafes; the hub's Create+Options) | the engine merges directions | Own action names; raw `padAxes` for the sticks; tests for every mapping; the Create+Options rule test. |\n1992\t| 13 | Text overflow at 320 px wide (4:3) | long names and descriptions | Layout helpers measure with `E.font.width`; a test lays out every screen at 320×240 and 427×240 and fails on any overflow. |\n1993\t\n1994\t---\n1995\t\n1996\t## 14. Testing\n1997\t\n1998\t### 14.1 The one command\n1999\t\n2000\t`node tests/run.mjs [suite …] [--fast]`, run from the dev folder.\n2001\t\n2002\t- It runs every suite in §14.3 by default; `--fast` skips the browser suites, and naming suites runs only those.\n2003\t- **It prints only failures** (`FAIL <suite>: <check>: <detail>`) and **one final line**: `412 passed, 0 failed · 11 suites · 38.4 s`.\n2004\t- The exit code is 1 on any failure. Rerun it only after changing the code a suite covers.\n2005\t\n2006\t### 14.2 The Node harness (as in `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`)\n2007\t\n2008\t- Load `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, then every `src/` file in ORDER, into a `vm` context.\n2009\t- **Stand-ins:**\n2010\t  - `window` (the context itself), `addEventListener() {}`, `location { hash: '', search: '' }`;\n2011\t  - `matchMedia(q) → { matches: q === flags.coarse, addEventListener() {} }`;\n2012\t  - a Map-backed `localStorage`;\n2013\t  - `navigator { getGamepads: () => [] }`;\n2014\t  - `performance`;\n2015\t  - an `AIHub` stub that is inactive by default.\n2016\t- `E.World3D` is absent, so the game uses `NullView` and skips the 3D boot steps.\n2017\t- **Driving it.** `game.advance(seconds)` (exact 1/120 s steps); `game.input.tap(action)`, `hold(action, on)` and `press(code)` (pad and key codes); `input.feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y)` for the mouse.\n2018\t- **`game.debug`** is the handle the tests read:\n2019\t\n2020\t  | Member | What it does |\n2021\t  |---|---|\n2022\t  | `snapshot()` | scene, floor, cell, dir, the party (HP, food, statuses, cooldowns), nearby monsters, flags, the Hand, the open UI screen and its focus id |\n2023\t  | `state()` | the full sim state |\n2024\t  | `hash()` | the state's hash |\n2025\t  | `cmd(c)` | injects a command |\n2026\t  | `warp(floor, x, y, dir)` | moves the party |\n2027\t  | `give(id)` | adds an item |\n2028\t  | `cheats` | the cheat toggles |\n2029\t  | `bot` | the walkthrough runner |\n2030\t  | `layout(screen, W, H)` | every widget's rect, for the overflow test |\n2031\t\n2032\t### 14.3 Suites and what they check\n2033\t\n2034\t| Suite | Covers |\n2035\t|---|---|\n2036\t| `lint` | Every map is rectangular and walled. Every legend character is known. Every wall feature stands on an open cell facing a wall. Every wire's ids, every item, monster, spell and text id, and every lock and key pair exist. Stairs pair up. **The walkthrough reachability and sealed checks** for every floor and branch (the planning script's logic, §7.4). There is no unused text id, and no `src/` sim file breaks the layer rule. |\n2037\t| `movement` | steps, turns, strafes, the buffer and repeat; bumps on walls, doors and monsters; the timing of arrival effects; the head-bob setting; stairs and floor cards |\n2038\t| `features` | each door, gate, lock (key used up, picking, warded refusal), magic seal (spell, scroll, wand), secret wall, illusion, plate (hold, latch, toggle; party, item and monster weight; small monsters don't count), dart trap (and disarm), pit, bridge, trapdoor and landing, teleporter (silent; the loop count and hint; the switch), spinner (seeded), lever, button and its window, catch, alcove (accepts, returns), candles in sequence and the wrong order, Great Locks |\n2039\t| `items` | equip rules (class, two-handed, quiver stacks); pack moves; the Hand (take from the front or own cell, stow, put down, throw range and landing, a throw onto a plate, into a pit, hitting a monster); use (eat, drink, read, scribe); rust; stolen items returned when the thief dies |\n2040\t| `combat` | to-hit and damage with a fixed seed (expected values over 10,000 rolls within bands); crits; cooldowns and the DEX scaling; rows and reach; missiles and ammo recovery; Party Strike choosing the right hands; flank and rear targeting; telegraph dodges (a step during the wind-up makes it miss); re-engaging; statuses ticking and curing |\n2041\t| `monsters` | waking by sight and noise; hunting with A* and flanking around a full cell; keepAway and ranged Seers; fleeing and stealing Latchkins; fliers over pits; cell capacity by size; drops; the boss's phases, locks, relock, absorbing lightning, summons and its attacks' telegraphs and dodges |\n2042\t| `magic` | every spell's effect and target; slot tables; memorizing and praying persisting; rest refills; scroll casting; wands' charges; the Robe's extra slot |\n2043\t| `camp` | refusal near enemies; heal per hour; cleric auto-Mend; interruptions (seeded; safe rooms; the wanderer budget); food drain and starving; Eat; level-up timing (at once or on rest) |\n2044\t| `progress` | XP split and multipliers; thresholds; HP and slots on level-up; deeds; Down and Dead rules; Raise (spell, scroll, shrine); game over; NPCs joining, the full-party path for Veil, dismissing |\n2045\t| `save` | save at a sample point on each floor, then load: the same `hash()`; the version field; a bad save is refused gracefully |\n2046\t| `determinism` | the same seed and command script give the same hash twice, and the same again after a save and load mid-script |\n2047\t| `ui` | title → New Game → Quick Start → skip intro → play. Every screen opens and closes; focus moves by d-pad and by mouse hover; carry and place in the Party screen; Cast targeting; Camp → Rest, Memorize, Formation; Map; Journal; dialogue choices. **Prompts follow the last device** (`label()` and the badges for keyboard, pad and mouse). The **Xbox setting turns ✕ into A**. The pause menu has Dev Mode, which disappears in a session. Text overflow at 320×240 and 427×240. |\n2048\t| `dev` | each slider changes its system (e.g. Monster HP × 2 doubles a spawned rat's HP); Reset restores every default; every cheat works; Warp to every waypoint; spawning; storage persists |\n2049\t| `attract` | 10 s idle on the title starts it, 9.9 s does not; each vignette runs to its end with no errors; any key, button, stick or pointer input exits within one step to the title; it doesn't write saves or settings; on the touch flag the notice shows and the attract mode still runs |\n2050\t| `babble` | `plan()` is deterministic; vowels pick their formants; punctuation sets pauses and contours; profiles differ |\n2051\t| `hub` (Node) | the stub becomes active, and the test runs the `<head>` connect line itself (`window.__hubInfo = AIHub.connect(…)`, §3.4): the title is skipped; `connect` gets `ghost` and `[1, 4]`; `ready()` is called once with no input; the card answers ready and more; play starts at `time() ≥ 0`; sends stay at 10 Hz or less, unreliable; progress about every second; `result` once on the finish (a time), a wipe or `time-up` (a score); fake messages make ghosts; `leave` removes one; `end` stops input and sound; no Save or Dev Mode in session menus; Options is ignored while Create is held |\n2052\t| **`playthrough`** | §14.4 |\n2053\t| `browser` (Playwright) | §14.5 |\n2054\t| `harness` (Playwright) | §14.5 |\n2055\t\n2056\t### 14.4 The scripted full playthrough\n2057\t\n2058\t- **The bot** (`72-bot.js`) reads each floor's `walkthrough` data (§7.4) and plays by the game's real rules through commands. It runs at **Normal, with no cheats**, using the premade party plus every NPC who agrees to join.\n2059\t- **Its moves:**\n2060\t  - it paths with A* (doors it may open, pits and trapdoors it must avoid, the spinner it avoids when it can);\n2061\t  - it faces and uses features, puts items down and throws them;\n2062\t  - it fights: it faces attackers, uses Party Strike when a hand is ready, sidesteps telegraphed blows when it can, and backs out of Seer lines into niches;\n2063\t  - it casts usefully: Spark Dart on lines, Mend below 50%, Blazing Orb on groups, Unlatch on the seal, Free Hinge at the boss;\n2064\t  - it rests when the party is below 60% or out of slots in a safe spot, eats when hungry, drinks below 25%;\n2065\t  - it takes every deed.\n2066\t- **The run** goes New Game → floor 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → ending scene. Then it runs again from a floor 3 save with **Veil refused**.\n2067\t- **Assertions at each checkpoint:**\n2068\t  - floor flags, keys, wards and NPCs as expected;\n2069\t  - the deeds done (3);\n2070\t  - no wipe;\n2071\t  - the level pace (§4.10, ±1 level);\n2072\t  - game time under 90 minutes;\n2073\t  - no `game.errors`.\n2074\t- **It writes a balance report** (`tests/out/balance.txt`): each fight's duration and HP lost, Downs, potions, rests, food used and the time per floor. It *fails* only on gross bands: a wipe, a single fight over 3 minutes (the boss: over 6 minutes), or floor 1 cleared without a single member below 70% (too easy).\n2075\t\n2076\t### 14.5 Browser checks\n2077\t\n2078\t**Settings.** Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium 1243, run with `args: ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu', '--enable-features=Vulkan', '--use-vulkan=swiftshader', '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader', '--disable-vulkan-surface', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']`.\n2079\t\n2080\t- **`browser`** (the bundled root HTML opened from `file://…html?backend=webgl`):\n2081\t  - it boots to the title with no `pageerror` or console errors, and no request other than jsDelivr;\n2082\t  - the 3D view is not blank (the canvas has a spread of colours);\n2083\t  - Enter → Quick Start → skip the intro → play; `game.debug.snapshot()` shows floor 1 at (2,14);\n2084\t  - a scripted 20 s walk and fight with no errors;\n2085\t  - it waits 10.5 s on the title and attract starts, then a key press returns to the title;\n2086\t  - with `isMobile, hasTouch` (390×844@3), the touch notice is drawn and no touch buttons show;\n2087\t  - the engine's `tools/check.mjs` also runs on the page with `--seconds 6`, and its errors fail the suite.\n2088\t- **`harness`.** Copy `hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and the bundled HTML into `tests/out/hub/`. Serve that folder with a `node:http` server on `127.0.0.1:0`; this suite starts the server and closes it itself, and it checks that `GET /` of the game returns our `<title>`. Then open:\n2089\t  1. `harness.html?game=<file>&players=2&auto=1`\n2090\t  2. `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n2091\t  3. `…&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`\n2092\t\n2093\t  For each, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Print the failing checklist rows on a failure.\n2094\t\n2095\t### 14.6 Looking (only what scripts can't judge)\n2096\t\n2097\t- **Screenshots** to `shots/` (by `tests/shoot.mjs`, not part of pass or fail) at 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 1024×768:\n2098\t  - the title;\n2099\t  - creation;\n2100\t  - each floor's signature room;\n2101\t  - every monster at 1 and 2 cells;\n2102\t  - the boss in each phase;\n2103\t  - the Party, Cast, Camp, Map and Journal screens;\n2104\t  - dialogue;\n2105\t  - Dev Mode;\n2106\t  - the attract caption;\n2107\t  - the touch notice;\n2108\t  - About.\n2109\t\n2110\t  Check that walls, secret and illusory blocks look identical, that text is readable at TV distance, that the glyphs are right, and that nothing overlaps the engine's corner button.\n2111\t- **Filmstrips** with `tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1` for:\n2112\t  - the weapon overlay swings;\n2113\t  - a monster wind-up and strike;\n2114\t  - a gate rising;\n2115\t  - the illusion pass;\n2116\t  - the boss's bolts sliding;\n2117\t  - the lightning telegraph.\n2118\t\n2119\t  Each motion must wind up, act and settle with no snaps.\n2120\t- **Hand play** with a controller and with keyboard and mouse through floor 1, with the Dev sliders open, to tune the feel.\n2121\t\n2122\t---\n2123\t\n2124\t## 15. Definition of done (TASK.md coverage)\n2125\t\n2126\t| TASK.md asks for | Where in this plan | Done when |\n2127\t|---|---|---|\n2128\t| A title riffing on the source, picked by a real RNG | Title (top) | the title screen reads **EYE OF THE BOLT-HOLDER** |\n2129\t| Genre and perspective that fit | §2 | — |\n2130\t| A single HTML file plus a dev folder named by the pattern | §0, §3.3, §3.4 | the root `.html` boots from disk |\n2131\t| Built on the handoff (engine changes allowed) | §1.2, §3.1, §3.9 | PATCHES.md lists every change |\n2132\t| The engine's native style and animation as the base, with new assets for the source's feel | §6 | the §14.6 review passes |\n2133\t| Audio in code only, babble voices | §6.5 | no audio files; every speaker babbles |\n2134\t| AI Hub multiplayer, and the game on its own | §10 | the harness passes; solo play is unaffected |\n2135\t| A feature-complete demo showing every mechanic, polished | §4, §7 | the playthrough bot passes; every system in the §4 tables exists |\n2136\t| Dev Mode from the pause menu with live sliders and a reset | §8 | `dev` suite |\n2137\t| Attract mode after 10 s, any input exits | §9 | `attract` suite |\n2138\t| Controller-first 10-foot UI; native keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox setting; no dense web screens | §5 | `ui` suite plus the screenshots |\n2139\t| Touch-only: no touch controls, a notice and the settings button, attract mode runs | §5.7 | `attract` and `browser` suites |\n2140\t| A writing style like the source's | §7.2, §7.3, §7.9 | — |\n2141\t| Headless tests, a scripted full playthrough, one command | §14 | `node tests/run.mjs`: 0 failed |\n2142\t| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §0 | grep finds no `TODO`, `FIXME` or `placeholder` in `src/` |\n2143\t| Source Information and the three feedback sets in the chat reply and the About screen | §11 | About pages filled; the reply copies them |\n2144\t| `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape, parsing | §11 | the parse check passes |\n2145\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5572b217-8052-4a87-b3f3-49ea658fe605","uuid":"736400ac-b127-4f87-9d50-420902373d82","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:53:40.816Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/work/PLAN.md","content":"| spider | Brass Spider | 2 | M | 22 | 13 | +4 | 1d6 | 1.5 | 0.6 | 5 | 110 | 30% of hits poison | 25% potionAntidote |\n| sentinel | Clockwork Sentinel | 2 | L | 50 | 16 | +5 | 2d6 | 2.8 | 1.6 | 5 | 350 | construct: immune to Sleep, Hold, Poison and Turn; lightning does ×1.5; 0.8 s wind-up | ringOfWarding, potionGreaterHealing |\n| hound | Lidless Hound | 3 | M | 20 | 13 | +5 | 1d8 | 1.3 | 0.5 | 6 (hearing) | 120 | always aware within 6 cells | — |\n| seer | Gloam Seer | 3 | M | 18 | 12 | +3 | 1d4 | 2.2 | 1.0 | 6 | 180 | casts a **Locking Bolt** (projectile, 2d6, 6 cells) every 6 s in line; a **Hold** (1 member, 6 s, save) every 12 s; keepAway at 3 | 30% staff; 20% potionHealing; 15% elixirClarity |\n| warden | Gloam Warden | 3 | M | 26 | 15 | +6 | 1d10 | 2.2 | 0.9 | 5 | 150 | reach: strikes from 2 cells in a clear line | 25% glaive; 15% studdedLeather |\n| gazer | Gazer | 3, 4 | S | 10 | 14 | +4 | 1d3 | 2.0 | 0.8 | 5 | 90 | flies; **Spark Gaze** (1d6, ranged, line of 3 or less) every 3 s | — |\n| golem | Lockjaw Golem | 4 | L | 60 | 17 | +7 | 2d8 | 3.0 | 1.8 | 5 | 400 | construct; lightning ×1.5, blunt ×1.25 | golemA: potionGreaterHealing |\n| boltholder | The Bolt-Holder | 4 | L | 320 | 15 | +8 | see §4.7.4 | 3.5 / 2.8 / 2.2 | drift 4 s | all | 3000 | phases, locks, absorbs lightning | — |\n\n**Balance targets** (the bot measures them, §14). On Normal, with the premade party plus the NPCs:\n- a single Drain Rat dies to one or two hits;\n- a fresh party survives the first Rat Channel fight above 60% HP;\n- Snick takes 20 to 40 s and is the first time a member is likely to go Down;\n- the Sentinel takes 30 to 60 s;\n- the boss takes 2.5 to 5 minutes.\n- The party should use 1 to 3 potions and 1 to 2 rests per floor.\n\n### 7.7 Items\n\nSpeed is the cooldown in seconds. Classes are F (Fighter), P (Paladin), R (Ranger), C (Cleric), M (Mage) and T (Thief). Two-handed is 2H. Defense values are \"+n\".\n\n**Weapons:**\n\n| Id | Name | Stats | Classes | Found | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| rustyDagger | Rusty Dagger | 1d3, 1.2, throwable | all | f1 (2,13) | \"Pitted and dull, but sharper than your fingernails.\" |\n| dagger | Dagger | 1d4, 1.2, throwable | all | Mage start, drops | \"A plain blade. It goes where you put it.\" |\n| shortSword | Short Sword | 1d6, 1.6 | F P R T | f1 (3,2); Ranger and Thief start | \"Short enough for a drain, long enough for a rat.\" |\n| longSword | Long Sword | 1d8, 2.0 | F P R | Fighter and Paladin start | \"Hasp steel, with a lockwright's mark on the tang.\" |\n| wardensBlade | Warden's Blade | 1d8+2, 2.0, +2 to-hit | F P R | f3 (22,11) | \"Black as wet slate. It never seems to dull.\" |\n| handAxe | Hand Axe | 1d6, 1.8, throwable | F P R | skeleton drops | \"Balanced for splitting kindling, or Latchkins.\" |\n| lockbreaker | Lockbreaker | 1d10+1, 3.0, 2H, +1 to-hit | F P | f2 (13,5) | \"A guild axe made for doors that would not open. It does not argue.\" |\n| mace | Mace | 1d6+1, 2.0, blunt | F P R C | Cleric start | \"Flanged iron on an oak haft. Honest work.\" |\n| copperhandsMaul | Copperhand's Maul | 1d8+1, 2.4, blunt | F P C | Durgan's | \"Dwarf-forged. The copper bands are for luck, and for weight.\" |\n| warhammer | Warhammer | 1d6+1, 2.4, blunt | F P R C | f2 (11,3) | \"Half tool, half argument.\" |\n| staff | Quarterstaff | 1d6, 1.8, 2H, blunt | all | Seer drops; Veil's | \"Ash, iron-shod at both ends.\" |\n| spear | Spear | 1d6, 2.2, **reach**, throwable | F P R T | Latchkin drops (10%) | \"Long enough to reach past a friend.\" |\n| glaive | Glaive | 1d10, 2.8, 2H, **reach** | F P R | Warden drops | \"A Warden's polearm, its blade etched with a shut eye.\" |\n| tumblersPick | Tumbler's Pick | 1d6+1, 1.8, ×2 vs constructs | F P R T | f2 (9,15) | \"A locksmith's pick-hammer. Clockwork hates it.\" |\n\n**Missile weapons and ammo:**\n\n| Id | Name | Stats | Classes | Found | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sling | Sling | 1d4, 2.0, ammo slingStones | all | f1 (1,5) | \"Leather and string. Older than locks.\" |\n| shortBow | Short Bow | 1d6, 1.8, ammo arrows, 2H | F P R T | Ranger start (in pack) | \"Elf-made, light as a thought.\" |\n| lightCrossbow | Light Crossbow | 1d8, 2.6, ammo bolts, 2H | F P R T | f1 (20,1) | \"Wound by a crank. Someone loved this, before the Latchkins.\" |\n| heavyCrossbow | Heavy Crossbow | 1d10+1, 3.4, ammo bolts, 2H | F P R | f3 (13,7) | \"It punches through mail, and patience.\" |\n| darts | Darts | 1d3, 1.2, thrown, stack | all | f1 (5,1); Thief start | \"Little iron wasps.\" |\n| slingStones / arrows / bolts | ammo | stack 30 | — | f1 (1,5) ×12; Ranger ×20; f1 (20,2) ×12, f3 (17,7) ×10 | \"Bolts: the city's other export.\" |\n\n**Armour and wearables:**\n\n| Id | Name | Stats | Classes | Found | Description |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| travellersRobe | Traveller's Robe | body +0 | M | Mage start | \"Many pockets, all of them full of crumbs.\" |\n| paddedJerkin | Padded Jerkin | body +1 | all | Latchkin drops (5%); Veil's | \"Quilted, and quietly proud of it.\" |\n| leatherArmor | Leather Armour | body +2 | F P R C T | starts; f1 (13,1) | \"Boiled, stitched and smelling of both.\" |\n| studdedLeather | Studded Leather | body +3 | F P R T | Warden drops (15%) | \"Leather with ambitions.\" |\n| chainShirt | Chain Shirt | body +4 | F P R C | Paladin start; f2 (17,15) | \"Ten thousand little rings, all of them cold.\" |\n| scaleMail | Scale Mail | body +5 | F P C | Durgan's | |\n| robeOfTheLintel | Robe of the Lintel | body +2, +1 INT, +1 level-1 slot | M | f3, SQ3 | \"Embroidered with doors. Every door is open.\" |\n| buckler | Buckler | shield +1 | F P R C T | Durgan's | |\n| woodenShield | Wooden Shield | shield +1 | F P C | Fighter and Paladin start | |\n| ironShield | Iron Shield | shield +2 | F P C | f2 (13,15) | |\n| leatherCap | Leather Cap | head +1 | F P R C T | f1 (3,8) | |\n| ironHelm | Iron Helm | head +1 | F P R C | Durgan's | |\n| ratKingsCrown | Rat King's Crown | head +1 | all | f1 lair | \"Twisted tin, worn by something with too many tails.\" |\n| tumblerwrightsGoggles | Tumblerwright's Goggles | head +0; always **Seeing** (secrets and traps glint) | all | f2, SQ2 | \"The world's seams show plainly through them.\" |\n| lidlessWard | Lidless Ward | neck: immune to Hold and Gaze | all | f3, Veil | \"Shaped like a shut eye. What it cannot see cannot hold you.\" |\n| amuletOfVigor | Amulet of Vigor | neck: +1 CON | all | f1, Snick | |\n| bracersOfDefense | Bracers of Defense | arms +2 | all | f3 (22,13) | |\n| ringOfMending | Ring of Mending | 1 HP every 30 s | all | f1, SQ1 | \"Warm, as if someone just took it off.\" |\n| ringOfWarding | Ring of Warding | +1 Def, +1 saves | all | f2, Sentinel | |\n| quickstepBoots | Quickstep Boots | cooldowns −10% | all | f3 (13,10) | |\n\n**Consumables and readables:**\n\n| Id | Name | Effect | Found |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ration | Ration | +50 food | 14 placed (f1: 4, f2: 5, f3: 5), plus one each at the start and rat drops |\n| ironRation | Iron Ration | +100 food | 4 placed: f1 (20,12), f2 (14,5), f3 (13,1), f3 (21,14) |\n| potionHealing | Potion of Healing | 2d4+2 | 6 placed (f1 (8,3), (19,10); f2 (20,3); f3 (15,1), (16,10) ×2), plus Seer drops |\n| potionGreaterHealing | Potion of Greater Healing | 4d4+4, wakes a Down member | f2 (6,10); the Sentinel's and golemA's drops |\n| potionAntidote | Antidote | cures poison | f3 (4,8) and drops |\n| elixirClarity | Elixir of Clarity | restores 1 spent slot of the highest level | Seer drops (15%) |\n| scroll ×9 | Scroll of *spell* | a mage casts it or scribes it | §7.4 |\n| scrollRaising | Scroll of Raising | a cleric or paladin reads it: Raise from Rest | f2 (11,5), f3 (20,14) |\n| wandUnlatching | Wand of Unlatching | Unlatch, 3 charges, anyone | f2 (1,7) |\n| wandSparks | Wand of Sparks | Spark Dart (2 darts), 8 charges | f3 (13,1) |\n\n**Tools, keys, wards, quest items, lore and junk:**\n\n| Id | Name | Effect | Found |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| lockpicks | Lockpicks | 6 uses; a failed pick snaps one | Thief start, Tamsin |\n| holySymbol | Key of the Threshold | a cleric's holy symbol | Cleric start |\n| veilsLantern | Veil's Lantern | a holy symbol | Veil's |\n| spellbook | Spellbook | holds known spells | Mage start |\n| ironKey / drainwardensKey / gearKey / boneKey / bentKey | keys | as wired | §7.4 |\n| copperWard / brassWard / ironWard | the Three Wards | the Undergate | §7.4 |\n| tumblerGear (I–IV) | Tumbler Gear | the clock deed | f2 |\n| tornPage / guildLedger / seersPsalm | notes | lore and hints (§7.9) | f1 (6,14), f2 (10,3), f3 (5,4) |\n| rock / ironIngot / bone | junk | heavy things for plates | §7.4 |\n| ratCrown | Rat Crown (coin) | race score | race |\n\n### 7.8 Spells\n\nArcane spells come from the spellbook and its scrolls. Prayers are to the Warder of Thresholds, the city's god of doors. The numbers are × ★spell power.\n\n| Id | Name | Kind and level | Target | Effect | Look |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| sparkDart | Spark Dart | arcane 1 | line | 1 + ⌊lvl/2⌋ darts (3 at most), each 1d4+1, always hitting the first monster within 6 cells | violet-white glows, sparks |\n| wardOfBrass | Ward of Brass | arcane 1 | member | +3 Def until it absorbs 8 + lvl damage, or until rest | brass shimmer on the card |\n| findSeams | Find Seams | arcane 1 | party | 90 s of Seeing | gold outlines |\n| slumber | Slumber | arcane 1 | front | sleep 20 s: living S and M monsters, an HP pool of 10 + 3×lvl, lowest first | drifting z's |\n| unlatch | Unlatch | arcane 2 | door | opens a magic seal or a simple lock | a ghost key turns |\n| frostbite | Frostbite | arcane 2 | front | 2d6 cold to all in the front cell, and Slowed 10 s | blue shards, a frost ring |\n| featherStep | Feather Step | arcane 2 | party | 120 s of Floating | the view rises 3 units; wind |\n| forkedLightning | Forked Lightning | arcane 3 | line | 3d6 (+1d6 per level above 5) to every monster along 5 cells; it bounces back once off a near wall and never hurts the party; **it heals the Bolt-Holder** | jagged cyan bars, a flash |\n| blazingOrb | Blazing Orb | arcane 3 | line | at the first monster cell or wall: 3d6 + lvl fire to all there, half to the 4 neighbouring cells' monsters | an orange orb, an explosion, a light flash |\n| mend | Mend | prayer 1 | member | heals 1d8 + 1 + ⌊lvl/2⌋; wakes a Down member | green glints |\n| steadyHand | Steady Hand | prayer 1 | party | +1 to-hit and saves, 60 s | a golden hand icon |\n| turnDead | Turn the Dead | prayer 1 | front | undead flee 12 s; undead with HP ≤ 2×lvl crumble | a white flare |\n| purge | Purge Venom | prayer 2 | member | cures poison and heals 1d4 | |\n| holdFast | Hold Fast | prayer 2 | front | humanoids are Held 10 s (25% save) | golden chains |\n| loaves | Loaves of the Hearth | prayer 2 | party | all food to 100 | bread, a warm glow |\n| greaterMend | Greater Mend | prayer 3 | member | heals 3d8 + lvl; wakes Down | |\n| raise | Raise from Rest | prayer 3 | dead member | back at 1 HP | a rising light |\n| freeHinge | Free Hinge | prayer 3 | party | cures Held; immune to Hold and Gaze for 120 s | a hinge sigil on the cards |\n\n### 7.9 The party, the NPCs and their scripts\n\n**The premade party** (Quick Start; also the Rat Run's at level 2):\n\n| Place | Name | Race and class | STR DEX CON INT WIS | HP | Gear | Prepared |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Brannoc Ironside | Human Fighter | 17 12 16 9 10 | 12 | longSword, woodenShield, leatherArmor, ration | — |\n| 2 | Ysa Thornfeather | Elf Ranger | 14 17 12 12 13 | 8 | shortSword ×2, leatherArmor, shortBow and arrows ×20 (pack), ration | — |\n| 3 | Father Cobb | Dwarf Cleric (beard) | 13 9 16 10 16 | 10 | mace, holySymbol, leatherArmor, ration | Mend ×2 |\n| 4 | Odelia Fenn | Human Mage | 8 14 11 17 11 | 4 | dagger, spellbook (Spark Dart, Find Seams, Slumber), travellersRobe, darts ×4, ration | Spark Dart, Slumber |\n\n**The NPCs:**\n\n| Name | Race and class, level | STR DEX CON INT WIS | HP | Gear | Prepared |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Tamsin Pell | Halfling Thief 2 | 10 17 13 13 9 | 12 | dagger, darts ×6, leatherArmor, lockpicks | — |\n| Durgan Copperhand | Dwarf Fighter 3 | 17 10 17 11 10 | 28 | copperhandsMaul, buckler, ironHelm, scaleMail | — |\n| Sister Veil | Human Cleric 4 | 10 13 12 14 17 | 23 | staff, veilsLantern, paddedJerkin | Mend ×3, Steady Hand, Purge ×2, Hold Fast |\n\n**Scripts** (E.Story nodes; the choices are in brackets):\n- **tamsin** (after LV2; she steps out of the cage):\n  - \"Took you long enough! Three days in a birdcage, and the little latch-thieves poking me with forks.\"\n  - \"Tamsin Pell, journeywoman of the Lockwrights. Or I was, before the locks went mad.\"\n  - \"You're going down, aren't you? Toward the thing that's doing this. Take me along. I open what your keys can't.\"\n  - **[Join us]** \"Then let's go and annoy something big.\" She joins.\n  - **[Go home, Tamsin]** \"Suit yourself. Take these. You'll need them more than me.\" She gives the lockpicks and leaves: \"Mind the right channel. That's where they nest.\"\n- **durgan1** (through the bars):\n  - \"Don't stand there gawping. Those levers on the wall behind you are the Tumbler Lock. My own design, and I'm locked on the wrong side of it.\"\n  - \"The creed is carved in the workshop. First falls, second rises, third falls. Can't reach the blasted things from in here.\"\n- **durgan2** (when G5 opens):\n  - \"Ha! Durgan Copperhand thanks you. The guild's dead and gone, but its halls aren't done with me yet.\"\n  - \"Whatever's below took my brothers' work and twisted it. I'd like a word with it. A hammer-shaped word.\"\n  - \"And take this gear. Found it in my cell. Looks like it belongs to the big clock.\"\n  - **[Come with us]** He joins.\n  - **[Find your own way out]** \"Hmph. Then luck to you.\" He leaves; the gear is given either way.\n- **ysolde1** (the Clock Hall):\n  - \"Living feet, in the Tumbler Halls. It has been a long time.\"\n  - \"I was Guildmistress Ysolde Vane. We forged the Watcher for the Undergate: an eye that would never close, for a lock that must never open.\"\n  - \"We gave it seven Great Bolts to hold. And it learned to love holding. Now it holds the whole city, one lock at a time.\"\n  - \"Three Wards open the Undergate: copper, brass and iron. Ours, the brass, sleeps in the Guild Vault. What is sealed by art, art unseals.\"\n  - \"And if you would do an old woman a kindness, the Great Clock has lost its four gears. Let it tell the hour once more.\"\n- **ysoldeHint** (a whisper): \"The guild hid its catches in plain sight. Look to the walls.\"\n- **ysolde2** (after the Sentinel): \"Close its eye, little keys. Close it for all of us.\" She fades.\n- **veil** (after LV3):\n  - \"Do not look at me so. Your eyes are loud, surface-folk.\"\n  - \"I am Veil, once a Seer of the Lidless. I shut my eyes to the Watcher's voice, and for that they chained me here to be… corrected.\"\n  - \"You seek the Iron Ward. The Wardens keep it in the Reliquary, past their barracks. There is another way. I know the stones that move.\"\n  - \"Take me from this place and I will show you. Leave me, and pray the Wardens are asleep.\"\n  - **[We will help you]** If a place is free: \"Then I walk with you.\" If the party is full: \"Then take this. It kept me sane.\" (the `lidlessWard`). Either way: \"Push where the moss does not grow.\" H2 opens and `veilHelped` is set.\n  - **[Stay here, seer]** \"Then go with your eyes open. It will find you.\" `veilRefused` is set.\n- **Snick's barks:**\n  - `snick1`: \"MINE! All the shiny bolts are MINE!\"\n  - `snick2`: \"Latchkins! To your king!\"\n  - `snick3`: \"…not… fair…\"\n- **The Bolt-Holder's lines:**\n  - `eye1`: \"Little keys. You have come so far, only to be turned.\"\n  - `eye2`: \"Every lock is a promise. I KEEP THEM ALL.\"\n  - `eye3`: \"You… unbolt… ME?\"\n  - `eye4`: \"Then be locked in the dark FOREVER!\"\n  - `eye5`: \"Who… will keep… the promises…?\"\n- **The notes:**\n  - **tornPage**: \"…they take the bolts, all the iron, every nail and hinge, down the right channel to HIM. Snick says HE pays in shiny. Snick says HE sees everything…\"\n  - **guildLedger**: \"Tumbler Lock, cell 4: the creed governs it. Undergate wards: copper to the Drainwarden, brass to the Vault, iron to the Lidless, who swore to keep it. Watcher: bolts tested, seven of seven. God help us if it learns to like it.\"\n  - **seersPsalm**: the candle order (§7.4.3).\n\n---\n\n## 8. Dev Mode (from the pause menu; hidden in hub sessions)\n\n- **The panel** is a 10-foot list in the game's own style.\n  - L1 and R1 switch tabs; up and down move between rows; left and right change a slider (hold to speed up).\n  - ✕ toggles or runs a row, □ resets the row, △ resets the page, ○ goes back.\n  - The mouse drags sliders and clicks toggles.\n- **Storage.** Changes apply live and persist in storage key `boltholder.dev`. **Reset to defaults** is a row at the top of Tuning.\n\n| Tab | Rows |\n|---|---|\n| **Tuning: Combat** | Party damage × (0.25–4, default 1) · Party to-hit (−5…+10, 0) · Attack cooldown × (0.25–3, 1) · Spell power × (0.25–4, 1) |\n| **Tuning: Monsters** | Monster HP × (0.25–4, 1) · Monster damage × (0.25–4, 1) · Monster interval × (0.25–3, 1) · Sight (1–10 cells, 5) · Wind-up (0.1–1.5 s, 0.5) · Re-engage delay (0–2 s, 0.6) · Boss HP × (0.25–4, 1) · Loot chance × (0–3, 1) |\n| **Tuning: Exploration** | Step time (0.05–0.6 s, 0.28) · Turn time (0.05–0.5 s, 0.2) · Throw range (1–8, 4) · Trap damage × (0–4, 1) · Button window (2–15 s, 6) |\n| **Tuning: Survival** | Hunger rate × (0–5, 1) · Rest heal × (0–5, 1) · Rest interruption (0–50%, 4) · XP gain × (0–5, 1) · Time in menus (0–1, 0.25) |\n| **Cheats** | God mode · Infinite spells · No cooldowns · No hunger · One-hit kills · Noclip · Reveal map · Show secrets · Freeze monsters · Give all keys and wards |\n| **Warp** | floor ◀ ▶, then that floor's named waypoints (data: `waypoints` in each floor, e.g. \"F1 Start\", \"F1 Latchkin Den\", \"F1 Snick's Hall\", \"F1 Cistern\", \"F2 Landing\", \"F2 Clock Hall\", \"F2 Endless Hall\", \"F2 Lock Room\", \"F2 Weight Hall\", \"F2 Vault\", \"F3 Ossuary\", \"F3 Gauntlet\", \"F3 Chapel\", \"F3 Penance\", \"F3 Barracks\", \"F3 Undergate\", \"F4 Antechamber\", \"F4 Arena\", \"Rat Run\") · Next floor · Boss · Ending |\n| **Party** | Heal all · Revive all · +1 level for everyone · Max food · Give item (by category) · Learn every spell · Fill every slot · Add NPC (Tamsin, Durgan, Veil) · Reset to the premade party |\n| **Spawn** | monster type ◀ ▶, then Spawn in front (group size ◀ ▶) · Kill all on this floor · Clear wanderers |\n| **Debug** | Overlays: cell and facing; monster AI states and timers over each monster; wiring lines on the automap; sim time per step; the last 20 events · **Auto-play to floor end** (the walkthrough bot, with or without cheats) · Start the attract mode now · Play the intro or ending · Sound test (every sfx, song and voice, with a test line) · Fake hub ghosts (2 dummies walking a loop) |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Attract mode\n\n- **The trigger.** 10.0 s with no input (§5.6) on the title or any of its menus (Load, Rat Run, About). This includes touch-only devices.\n- **The `attract` scene** runs a **director of vignettes**. Each vignette is data:\n\n  ```js\n  { name, floor, at: [x, y, dir], party: 'demo',\n    cheats: { god: true, infiniteSpells: true, noHunger: true, noclip: false },\n    steps: [ bot commands ], seconds }\n  ```\n\n  - The `demo` party is the premade four at level 5 plus Tamsin and Durgan, knowing every spell, with good gear.\n  - The steps use the same commands as players (§3.5), so the bot is the one in `72-bot.js`.\n\n| # | Vignette | What it shows | About |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The Drains | take the dagger; LV1 and the gate rising; into the Rat Channel; Party Strike on the rats (damage pops); read N1 | 18 s |\n| 2 | Latchkins | the Den fight; LV2; Tamsin's lines typing with babble (auto-advancing) | 16 s |\n| 3 | Stones and plates | the rock put down on P1, G2 rising; walking through I1 (the dissolve) | 14 s |\n| 4 | Spellcraft | Spark Dart down a corridor, Mend on a card, Blazing Orb on skeletons (f2 Workshop) | 14 s |\n| 5 | The Party screen | it opens; the focus moves; a sword is equipped; the automap opens and closes | 12 s |\n| 6 | Clockwork | the Sentinel fight with Forked Lightning (×1.5) | 14 s |\n| 7 | The Gauntlet | ducking Seer bolts into the niches | 14 s |\n| 8 | The Bolt-Holder | a Great Lock turned, Chain Lightning dodged behind a pillar, Bolt Rain, the cage opening | 22 s |\n| 9 | Title | the logo and \"Press any button\" | 5 s |\n\n- **The loop.** After vignette 9 it starts over. A \"DEMO\" tag sits top left, and \"Press [glyph] / any key\" blinks at the bottom centre.\n- **Any input exits at once.** The input is consumed so the title menu doesn't act on it; the title scene, its music and its camera come back. The demo never writes saves, settings or dev storage, and never touches the player's party.\n- **Robustness.** Every vignette is time-boxed. If a step stalls for more than 4 s or throws, the director skips to the next vignette (and logs it in dev builds).\n\n---\n\n## 10. Multiplayer\n\n### 10.1 AI Hub session (`AIHub.active`): the Rat Run ghost race, 1 to 4 players\n\n1. **Boot. Connect first, build second.** The harness gives each copy **about 11 s to say hello** (`connect()`) and **20 s more to call `ready()`**. A 3D page reaches the game's module only after three.js and Rapier have downloaded, so:\n   - Put a tiny classic script in `<head>`, right after the session client: `window.__hubInfo = (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;`. It runs during parsing, before any module.\n   - The game module then does `const info = await window.__hubInfo`. Events that arrive before handlers attach are kept, so nothing is lost.\n   - If `info` is `null`, boot normally.\n   - In a session, build only the race world and the UI, and skip the title, attract and menus.\n2. **Seeding.** Seed every `B.rng` stream from `AIHub.rng('deal')`, so every copy deals the same monsters and rolls at the start.\n3. **Our own card** (the `hubcard` scene, drawn over the race floor's first view) shows:\n   - the logo and \"THE RAT RUN\";\n   - the goal, \"Fastest party out of the Rat Run wins\";\n   - the controls, with glyphs for this device;\n   - every player in their seat colour (`info.players[i].color`) with a ✓ when ready (`card.ready`);\n   - \"Ready ✕ / Enter · More time △\" and the countdown (`card.left`).\n\n   ✕ or Enter sends `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △ sends `AIHub.answer('more')`, and pressing it again takes it back. The card has no menus or choices, and any randomness on it comes from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n4. **Ready and start.** Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the race sim and its `World3D` exist, with no key press; `prepare()` may finish during the card's countdown. On `start`, show the countdown 3-2-1 from the negative `AIHub.time()`; input unlocks at 0. Measure this in M0 and M6 with `players=4`. On this machine's SwiftShader, aim for hello under 3 s and ready under 12 s.\n5. **During the run.**\n   - Every 100 ms, `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', area: 'race', cx, cy, dir, x, y, yaw, cp, hp }, { reliable: false })`.\n   - About once a second, `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`.\n   - **Ghosts** are the others' cloaked rigs in their seat colours, with name tags drawn with `E.font` (never as HTML). They are lerped to the reported positions, shown when the `area` matches, and never block or affect anything.\n6. **Finishing.** Reaching `>` sends `AIHub.result({ time: Math.round(AIHub.time()), stats: { Kills, Crowns } })` and `send({ t: 'done', time })`. The screen shows \"Escaped in 01:42.3. Waiting for the others.\"\n7. **A wipe** sends `result({ score })` once and shows \"Your party fell. The others run on.\"\n8. **`time-up`** sends `result({ score })` if nothing was sent yet. **`leave`** removes that ghost. **`end`** clears and locks the input, stops the music and sfx, and shows the reason; the hub draws the results.\n9. **The rules in a session.**\n   - No saves, no Dev Mode.\n   - The pause menu shows only Resume, Settings and Controls.\n   - No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open`, and no network but the hub.\n   - Options is ignored while Create is held.\n   - `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">`.\n\n### 10.2 On its own\n\n- **Rat Run from the title** is the same race, solo, on the local clock (the code is shared in `73-hub.js`, with its clock and ghost source swapped).\n- **The best-run ghost.** The best time and a 10 Hz trail of `{ t, cx, cy, dir }` are kept in storage `boltholder.ratrun`, and the trail runs beside you as a **golden ghost**.\n- **The results** show time, best, crowns and kills, with Run again and Title.\n- The campaign is single-player.\n\n---\n\n## 11. About and Credits, and the final report\n\n- **The About and Credits screen** opens from the title and the pause menu. Its pages are switched with L1 and R1 and scrolled with the d-pad:\n  1. **The game:** the title, the tagline \"A thousand locks. One eye.\", the version and the build date.\n  2. **Source Information:** every field of TASK.md's list (Date, Source, Plan, Genre and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage).\n  3. **Testing Feedback** (4 answers).\n  4. **Engine Feedback** (6 answers).\n  5. **Prompt Feedback** (4 answers).\n  6. **Credits:**\n     - the game by (your model);\n     - the engine: my-3D2dge (MIT);\n     - three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), the AI Hub session client;\n     - any store asset sets used (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG, CC0);\n     - \"Inspired by Eye of the Beholder (Westwood Associates / SSI, 1991). No names, text or assets from it are used.\"\n\n  Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- **One source of truth.** Keep the text in `14-data-text.js` as `B.ABOUT`. `tools/build.mjs` writes `exit-interview.json` from that same object and checks that it parses. Your chat reply copies the same text.\n- **Prefilled values** (confirm or replace them with your own run's facts):\n\n  | Field | Value |\n  |---|---|\n  | Source | Eye of the Beholder (Westwood Associates / SSI, 1991; MS-DOS and Amiga) |\n  | Plan | `PLAN.md` |\n  | Genre and Perspective | real-time, first-person, grid-based party RPG dungeon crawler; a first-person party view with tweened steps and quarter turns, plus a top-down automap |\n  | Tech | my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the 2D engine from `dist/handoff`) and my-3D2dge 3D v0.85.2 (three.js r182 WebGPU / WebGL 2 and Rapier 0.19.3, via jsDelivr); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for the tests; plain JavaScript in one HTML file |\n  | Art Direction | the engine's native retro-modern look: code-drawn low-res 3D (pixel resolution, toon light, outlines, fog), rigs as pixel-art cards, procedural textures, pen-drawn creatures and mechanisms, a brass \"lockwork\" UI |\n  | Animation | the engine's procedural rigs and moves (E.Humanoid, E.Blob, E.MOVES), a tweened first-person camera, pen-animated creatures and mechanisms, first-person weapon overlays |\n  | Audio | the engine's chip synth (step-sequencer music with combat layers and stings, synthesized sfx); voices from a custom WebAudio formant babble synth (Animalese/Simlish style) |\n  | Online | AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1 to 4 players (the Rat Run); a solo time trial against the local best ghost |\n  | Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage | your run's facts (the planning research is §1 of this plan) |\n\n- **`exit-interview.json`** (in the root, exactly TASK.md's shape). The `aiHub` part:\n\n  ```json\n  \"aiHub\": { \"name\": \"Eye of the Bolt-Holder\", \"tagline\": \"A thousand locks. One eye.\",\n    \"description\": \"A real-time, first-person party dungeon crawl beneath Hasp, the City of a Thousand Locks: four floors of drains, clockwork halls and eye-cults, levers, plates and keys, spells memorized at camp, and the caged Eye that holds the city's bolts.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\", \"genre\": \"RPG\", \"source\": \"Eye of the Beholder (1991)\", \"series\": \"Eye of the Beholder\", \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD move · D-pad/Q E turn · ✕/F use · □/Space strike · L2 R2/1-6 hands · △/I party\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"first-person\", \"fantasy\", \"retro\", \"exploration\", \"boss fights\"] }\n  ```\n\n  Fill `sourceInformation`, `testingFeedback` (4), `engineFeedback` (6) and `promptFeedback` (4) as plain text. Check it with `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Build order and milestones\n\nEach milestone ends **shippable**: it builds, the one command passes and nothing half-done is visible. Build floor 1 completely before starting floor 2. The percentages are the rough share of effort.\n\n| # | Milestone | Build | Exit criteria (tests in §14) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **M0** | Foundation and spikes (10%) | Fetch (§3.2); folder skeleton; `tools/build.mjs`; `tests/run.mjs` with the Node harness and one browser smoke; `NullView`. Spikes: (a) the bundled page boots from `file://` to a corridor of floor 1's geometry; (b) THINGS: lever, button, catch, alcove with items, keyhole, plaque, `wallBlock` (it must match the level walls) and the illusion pass-through; (c) a pen creature (the leech) and a boss sketch; (d) `babble.plan` plus a playable voice; (e) the hub harness passing against a stub page with our metas | `node tests/run.mjs` green; the bundle opens from disk with no errors; harness `__hubCheck.pass` on the stub |\n| **M1** | The dungeon (15%) | `15-data-floors.js` (all 5 maps and tables, §7.4); the floor loader; movement; every feature in §4.2 with wiring; stairs and pits between floors; the Presenter building all floors (geometry, things, lights, fog); the automap; the log; Examine; Dev Warp, Noclip and Reveal map | content lint plus the walkthrough reachability for every floor; unit tests for every feature; walking all floors by hand with Warp |\n| **M2** | The party and the fight (15%) | races, classes, stats, formation; items, inventory, equipment, the Hand (take, put down, throw, place); combat (hands, cooldowns, rows, reach, missiles, Party Strike, statuses); all 16 monster types' minds and their visuals (§6.3); the HUD (§5.2); the glyph painter and prompts; the input map for pad, keys and mouse; the Party screen with focus navigation; first-person weapon overlays | combat maths and AI unit tests; UI-flow tests (Party screen, equipping, prompts per device); a scripted floor 1 fight sequence passes |\n| **M3** | Magic, camp, progress (12%) | all 18 spells, the Cast menu and targeting; scrolls, wands, Scribe; Camp: Rest (interruptions, safe rooms), Memorize, Pray, Formation, Eat; food; XP and levels; Down, Dead, Raise; game over; saves (3 slots plus the autosave); character creation; the premade party | **floor 1 is completed by the bot with real rules on Normal**; the save and load round-trip hash; the creation flow test |\n| **M4** | Story and the deep floors (18%) | E.Story scripts for all NPCs and barks (§7.9); recruiting and dismissing; Veil's two branches; floors 2–4 content (items, monsters, events, hints, deeds); the Undergate; **the Bolt-Holder** (§4.7.4); intro and ending stages and scripts; per-floor music with fight layers; every sfx; the babble voices | **the full playthrough bot passes, start to ending, on both Veil branches**; every deed is reachable |\n| **M5** | The shell (10%) | the title (3D stage, logo, menu); the **attract mode** (§9); **Dev Mode** (§8); Settings (§4.16) including PlayStation and Xbox glyphs; the touch-only notice; About and Credits; game over and ending screens; floor cards | attract tests (start at 10 s, any input exits, every vignette runs); Dev Mode tests (a slider changes behaviour, reset works); the touch notice test |\n| **M6** | Multiplayer (8%) | the hub session flow (§10.1) with our own card, ghosts and reporting; the solo Rat Run with the best ghost | the Node hub simulation passes; **the harness passes** for `players=2`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5` and `&scenario=host-leave` |\n| **M7** | Polish and ship (12%) | juice (telegraph clarity, hit-stop on crits, card shakes, ambience); a balance pass with the bot's metrics plus hand play using the Dev sliders; the look review (§14.6) at 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 1024×768; text overflow fixes; About text; `exit-interview.json`; the reply | the whole command green; screenshots reviewed; JSON parses; the bundle is under the deliverable name in the root |\n\n---\n\n## 13. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| # | Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The 3D engine is outside the handoff and loads from a CDN | module order, `file://`, an offline viewer | The planning spike proved `file://` with a jsDelivr import map works and matches the vendored checksums. Pin the versions. Show a clear boot error if `E.World3D` is missing. *Optional, only if a reviewer needs an offline file:* inline the libraries as Blob URLs behind an import map injected before any module. |\n| 2 | Separating the sim from the 3D world | the kit mixes them; tests need Node | Define the Sim, Presenter and Command interfaces in M0. The `lint` test suite fails if a sim file (`20-`–`31-`) mentions `world`, `World3D`, `document`, `audio` or `Math.random` (the build only warns). Every system gets a Node test. |\n| 3 | Secret and illusory walls that must look exactly like the level walls | level walls are baked and instanced | Spike it in M0: `world.box` with the floor's `side` style, compared side by side in a screenshot. If it doesn't match, add `wallBlock` to the 3D engine using the level's wall material (PATCHES.md). Mask the illusion step with a 0.15 s dissolve. |\n| 4 | Pen-drawn creatures and the boss take time and can look poor | five bespoke bodies | Prototype the leech in M0 and the boss early in M4. Borrow from the horror kit's dogs. Judge motion with `tools/filmstrip.mjs`. Keep cards (rigs and blobs) for the other 11 types. |\n| 5 | The 10-foot UI is complex (paperdoll, backpack, details, spell targeting) | many widgets, three input styles | One geometric focus system; screens as data; UI-flow tests in Node (focus moves, carry and place); screenshots at three sizes. |\n| 6 | Real-time balance | swingy fights, wipes | ★Tuning sliders, difficulty multipliers, the bot's balance report (§14.5) every milestone, attack telegraphs and the re-engage delay. |\n| 7 | Content volume (4 floors plus a race) | time | Data-driven floors; the lint and walkthrough tests from M1; floor 1 finished before floor 2; cut only side items and dressing, never a system or a floor. |\n| 8 | The hub harness running a heavy 3D page (up to 4 iframes on SwiftShader) | it allows about 11 s for hello (`connect`) and 20 s more for `ready()`; it then plays about 6 s of random arrow and WASD keys, calls time-up and wants a `result` within its 5 s grace | Call `connect()` from a classic script in `<head>` before the modules load (§10.1). A session builds only the race world, calls `ready()` before `prepare()` finishes, and uses low 3D resolution and 1 torch shadow. Run the harness at M0 with a stub page carrying the real libraries, and again at M6. |\n| 9 | Determinism (saves, bots, hub fairness) | hidden `Math.random`, frame-dependent timing | Our own seeded RNG streams kept in the state; everything in the fixed steps; hash tests twice; the save → load → same-hash test. |\n| 10 | Audio | autoplay rules, an extra bus | The engine starts sound after the first input. The babble synth uses `game.audio.ctx` and the patched voice bus. In Node it is silent but `babble.plan` is tested. |\n| 11 | Attract mode stalls | bots in a changing game | Vignettes with cheats, time boxes, skip on a stall, a test that runs all of them. |\n| 12 | Input semantics (d-pad turns, the stick strafes; the hub's Create+Options) | the engine merges directions | Own action names; raw `padAxes` for the sticks; tests for every mapping; the Create+Options rule test. |\n| 13 | Text overflow at 320 px wide (4:3) | long names and descriptions | Layout helpers measure with `E.font.width`; a test lays out every screen at 320×240 and 427×240 and fails on any overflow. |\n\n---\n\n## 14. Testing\n\n### 14.1 The one command\n\n`node tests/run.mjs [suite …] [--fast]`, run from the dev folder.\n\n- It runs every suite in §14.3 by default; `--fast` skips the browser suites, and naming suites runs only those.\n- **It prints only failures** (`FAIL <suite>: <check>: <detail>`) and **one final line**: `412 passed, 0 failed · 11 suites · 38.4 s`.\n- The exit code is 1 on any failure. Rerun it only after changing the code a suite covers.\n\n### 14.2 The Node harness (as in `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`)\n\n- Load `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, then every `src/` file in ORDER, into a `vm` context.\n- **Stand-ins:**\n  - `window` (the context itself), `addEventListener() {}`, `location { hash: '', search: '' }`;\n  - `matchMedia(q) → { matches: q === flags.coarse, addEventListener() {} }`;\n  - a Map-backed `localStorage`;\n  - `navigator { getGamepads: () => [] }`;\n  - `performance`;\n  - an `AIHub` stub that is inactive by default.\n- `E.World3D` is absent, so the game uses `NullView` and skips the 3D boot steps.\n- **Driving it.** `game.advance(seconds)` (exact 1/120 s steps); `game.input.tap(action)`, `hold(action, on)` and `press(code)` (pad and key codes); `input.feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y)` for the mouse.\n- **`game.debug`** is the handle the tests read:\n\n  | Member | What it does |\n  |---|---|\n  | `snapshot()` | scene, floor, cell, dir, the party (HP, food, statuses, cooldowns), nearby monsters, flags, the Hand, the open UI screen and its focus id |\n  | `state()` | the full sim state |\n  | `hash()` | the state's hash |\n  | `cmd(c)` | injects a command |\n  | `warp(floor, x, y, dir)` | moves the party |\n  | `give(id)` | adds an item |\n  | `cheats` | the cheat toggles |\n  | `bot` | the walkthrough runner |\n  | `layout(screen, W, H)` | every widget's rect, for the overflow test |\n\n### 14.3 Suites and what they check\n\n| Suite | Covers |\n|---|---|\n| `lint` | Every map is rectangular and walled. Every legend character is known. Every wall feature stands on an open cell facing a wall. Every wire's ids, every item, monster, spell and text id, and every lock and key pair exist. Stairs pair up. **The walkthrough reachability and sealed checks** for every floor and branch (the planning script's logic, §7.4). There is no unused text id, and no `src/` sim file breaks the layer rule. |\n| `movement` | steps, turns, strafes, the buffer and repeat; bumps on walls, doors and monsters; the timing of arrival effects; the head-bob setting; stairs and floor cards |\n| `features` | each door, gate, lock (key used up, picking, warded refusal), magic seal (spell, scroll, wand), secret wall, illusion, plate (hold, latch, toggle; party, item and monster weight; small monsters don't count), dart trap (and disarm), pit, bridge, trapdoor and landing, teleporter (silent; the loop count and hint; the switch), spinner (seeded), lever, button and its window, catch, alcove (accepts, returns), candles in sequence and the wrong order, Great Locks |\n| `items` | equip rules (class, two-handed, quiver stacks); pack moves; the Hand (take from the front or own cell, stow, put down, throw range and landing, a throw onto a plate, into a pit, hitting a monster); use (eat, drink, read, scribe); rust; stolen items returned when the thief dies |\n| `combat` | to-hit and damage with a fixed seed (expected values over 10,000 rolls within bands); crits; cooldowns and the DEX scaling; rows and reach; missiles and ammo recovery; Party Strike choosing the right hands; flank and rear targeting; telegraph dodges (a step during the wind-up makes it miss); re-engaging; statuses ticking and curing |\n| `monsters` | waking by sight and noise; hunting with A* and flanking around a full cell; keepAway and ranged Seers; fleeing and stealing Latchkins; fliers over pits; cell capacity by size; drops; the boss's phases, locks, relock, absorbing lightning, summons and its attacks' telegraphs and dodges |\n| `magic` | every spell's effect and target; slot tables; memorizing and praying persisting; rest refills; scroll casting; wands' charges; the Robe's extra slot |\n| `camp` | refusal near enemies; heal per hour; cleric auto-Mend; interruptions (seeded; safe rooms; the wanderer budget); food drain and starving; Eat; level-up timing (at once or on rest) |\n| `progress` | XP split and multipliers; thresholds; HP and slots on level-up; deeds; Down and Dead rules; Raise (spell, scroll, shrine); game over; NPCs joining, the full-party path for Veil, dismissing |\n| `save` | save at a sample point on each floor, then load: the same `hash()`; the version field; a bad save is refused gracefully |\n| `determinism` | the same seed and command script give the same hash twice, and the same again after a save and load mid-script |\n| `ui` | title → New Game → Quick Start → skip intro → play. Every screen opens and closes; focus moves by d-pad and by mouse hover; carry and place in the Party screen; Cast targeting; Camp → Rest, Memorize, Formation; Map; Journal; dialogue choices. **Prompts follow the last device** (`label()` and the badges for keyboard, pad and mouse). The **Xbox setting turns ✕ into A**. The pause menu has Dev Mode, which disappears in a session. Text overflow at 320×240 and 427×240. |\n| `dev` | each slider changes its system (e.g. Monster HP × 2 doubles a spawned rat's HP); Reset restores every default; every cheat works; Warp to every waypoint; spawning; storage persists |\n| `attract` | 10 s idle on the title starts it, 9.9 s does not; each vignette runs to its end with no errors; any key, button, stick or pointer input exits within one step to the title; it doesn't write saves or settings; on the touch flag the notice shows and the attract mode still runs |\n| `babble` | `plan()` is deterministic; vowels pick their formants; punctuation sets pauses and contours; profiles differ |\n| `hub` (Node) | the stub becomes active, and the test runs the `<head>` connect line itself (`window.__hubInfo = AIHub.connect(…)`, §3.4): the title is skipped; `connect` gets `ghost` and `[1, 4]`; `ready()` is called once with no input; the card answers ready and more; play starts at `time() ≥ 0`; sends stay at 10 Hz or less, unreliable; progress about every second; `result` once on the finish (a time), a wipe or `time-up` (a score); fake messages make ghosts; `leave` removes one; `end` stops input and sound; no Save or Dev Mode in session menus; Options is ignored while Create is held |\n| **`playthrough`** | §14.4 |\n| `browser` (Playwright) | §14.5 |\n| `harness` (Playwright) | §14.5 |\n\n### 14.4 The scripted full playthrough\n\n- **The bot** (`72-bot.js`) reads each floor's `walkthrough` data (§7.4) and plays by the game's real rules through commands. It runs at **Normal, with no cheats**, using the premade party plus every NPC who agrees to join.\n- **Its moves:**\n  - it paths with A* (doors it may open, pits and trapdoors it must avoid, the spinner it avoids when it can);\n  - it faces and uses features, puts items down and throws them;\n  - it fights: it faces attackers, uses Party Strike when a hand is ready, sidesteps telegraphed blows when it can, and backs out of Seer lines into niches;\n  - it casts usefully: Spark Dart on lines, Mend below 50%, Blazing Orb on groups, Unlatch on the seal, Free Hinge at the boss;\n  - it rests when the party is below 60% or out of slots in a safe spot, eats when hungry, drinks below 25%;\n  - it takes every deed.\n- **The run** goes New Game → floor 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → ending scene. Then it runs again from a floor 3 save with **Veil refused**.\n- **Assertions at each checkpoint:**\n  - floor flags, keys, wards and NPCs as expected;\n  - the deeds done (3);\n  - no wipe;\n  - the level pace (§4.10, ±1 level);\n  - game time under 90 minutes;\n  - no `game.errors`.\n- **It writes a balance report** (`tests/out/balance.txt`): each fight's duration and HP lost, Downs, potions, rests, food used and the time per floor. It *fails* only on gross bands: a wipe, a single fight over 3 minutes (the boss: over 6 minutes), or floor 1 cleared without a single member below 70% (too easy).\n\n### 14.5 Browser checks\n\n**Settings.** Playwright 1.63.0 with Chromium 1243, run with `args: ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu', '--enable-features=Vulkan', '--use-vulkan=swiftshader', '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader', '--disable-vulkan-surface', '--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required']`.\n\n- **`browser`** (the bundled root HTML opened from `file://…html?backend=webgl`):\n  - it boots to the title with no `pageerror` or console errors, and no request other than jsDelivr;\n  - the 3D view is not blank (the canvas has a spread of colours);\n  - Enter → Quick Start → skip the intro → play; `game.debug.snapshot()` shows floor 1 at (2,14);\n  - a scripted 20 s walk and fight with no errors;\n  - it waits 10.5 s on the title and attract starts, then a key press returns to the title;\n  - with `isMobile, hasTouch` (390×844@3), the touch notice is drawn and no touch buttons show;\n  - the engine's `tools/check.mjs` also runs on the page with `--seconds 6`, and its errors fail the suite.\n- **`harness`.** Copy `hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and the bundled HTML into `tests/out/hub/`. Serve that folder with a `node:http` server on `127.0.0.1:0`; this suite starts the server and closes it itself, and it checks that `GET /` of the game returns our `<title>`. Then open:\n  1. `harness.html?game=<file>&players=2&auto=1`\n  2. `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n  3. `…&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`\n\n  For each, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Print the failing checklist rows on a failure.\n\n### 14.6 Looking (only what scripts can't judge)\n\n- **Screenshots** to `shots/` (by `tests/shoot.mjs`, not part of pass or fail) at 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 1024×768:\n  - the title;\n  - creation;\n  - each floor's signature room;\n  - every monster at 1 and 2 cells;\n  - the boss in each phase;\n  - the Party, Cast, Camp, Map and Journal screens;\n  - dialogue;\n  - Dev Mode;\n  - the attract caption;\n  - the touch notice;\n  - About.\n\n  Check that walls, secret and illusory blocks look identical, that text is readable at TV distance, that the glyphs are right, and that nothing overlaps the engine's corner button.\n- **Filmstrips** with `tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1` for:\n  - the weapon overlay swings;\n  - a monster wind-up and strike;\n  - a gate rising;\n  - the illusion pass;\n  - the boss's bolts sliding;\n  - the lightning telegraph.\n\n  Each motion must wind up, act and settle with no snaps.\n- **Hand play** with a controller and with keyboard and mouse through floor 1, with the Dev sliders open, to tune the feel.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Definition of done (TASK.md coverage)\n\n| TASK.md asks for | Where in this plan | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| A title riffing on the source, picked by a real RNG | Title (top) | the title screen reads **EYE OF THE BOLT-HOLDER** |\n| Genre and perspective that fit | §2 | — |\n| A single HTML file plus a dev folder named by the pattern | §0, §3.3, §3.4 | the root `.html` boots from disk |\n| Built on the handoff (engine changes allowed) | §1.2, §3.1, §3.9 | PATCHES.md lists every change |\n| The engine's native style and animation as the base, with new assets for the source's feel | §6 | the §14.6 review passes |\n| Audio in code only, babble voices | §6.5 | no audio files; every speaker babbles |\n| AI Hub multiplayer, and the game on its own | §10 | the harness passes; solo play is unaffected |\n| A feature-complete demo showing every mechanic, polished | §4, §7 | the playthrough bot passes; every system in the §4 tables exists |\n| Dev Mode from the pause menu with live sliders and a reset | §8 | `dev` suite |\n| Attract mode after 10 s, any input exits | §9 | `attract` suite |\n| Controller-first 10-foot UI; native keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox setting; no dense web screens | §5 | `ui` suite plus the screenshots |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, a notice and the settings button, attract mode runs | §5.7 | `attract` and `browser` suites |\n| A writing style like the source's | §7.2, §7.3, §7.9 | — |\n| Headless tests, a scripted full playthrough, one command | §14 | `node tests/run.mjs`: 0 failed |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §0 | grep finds no `TODO`, `FIXME` or `placeholder` in `src/` |\n| Source Information and the three feedback sets in the chat reply and the About screen | §11 | About pages filled; the reply copies them |\n| `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape, parsing | §11 | the parse check passes |\n","numLines":526,"startLine":1620,"totalLines":2145}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DSnsCQfL9uHa5GnBdbAtpH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
