{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0166YDY8i6A7chQMUwVNRsj6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/*!\n2\tmy-3D2dge 3D v0.85.2: real 3D worlds under my-3D2dge games (three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3)\n3\thttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n4\t\n5\tA 3D world, its physics and its camera under a my-3D2dge game. The 2D engine (engine/my-3d2dge.js) still runs the game:\n6\tits exact fixed steps, scenes, input, pause menu, settings, touch buttons, sound, the rigs and their moves, the HUD. This\n7\tmodule simulates and draws the world under the game's clear canvas. Everything is drawn by code: levels written as text,\n8\ttextures pixel by pixel, characters by the 2D engine's rigs (as cards, or as 3D puppets on the same joints), props and\n9\tpickups from four shapes. No image, model or sound files.\n10\t\n11\tAGENTS: this header is the whole manual for the 3D side; the API card (API.md) covers the 2D side (E.Game, input, rigs,\n12\tmoves, E.font, E.ui, E.Menu, audio). Read the code below to debug it, or to change it (it is yours to change, in any\n13\tway you see fit): its sections start with \"/* ===\" and a number.\n14\t\n15\t## Host it (served: browsers load modules only over http; npx serve at the repository's root, or my-3d2dge.vercel.app)\n16\t<script type=\"importmap\">{ \"imports\": { \"three\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n17\t  \"three/webgpu\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\", \"three/tsl\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js\",\n18\t  \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"/vendor/rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js\" } }</script>\n19\t<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #000 }</style>\n20\t<div id=\"stage\" style=\"position:relative;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden\">\n21\t  <canvas id=\"view\"></canvas><canvas id=\"screen\" style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%\"></canvas></div>\n22\t<script src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge.js\"></script>                   the 2D engine, a classic script, first\n23\t<script type=\"module\" src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js\"></script>  this file\n24\t<script type=\"module\" src=\"game.js\"></script>                your game, a module (const E = My3D2dge;)\n25\t\n26\t## Mental model\n27\t- The 2D engine's units: x east, y south, z up; 16 units = 1 metre = 1 tile; speeds in units a second; angles in\n28\t  radians from +x toward +y (0 east, PI/2 south, -PI/2 north).\n29\t- new E.Game({ ..., bg: null }): its canvas is clear, and the HUD draws on it over the 3D picture (r.overlay, r.text,\n30\t  E.ui, E.font) in game pixels, r.W x r.H. res: 'ps1', expand: true as in the 2D games.\n31\t- await E.World3D.init(game) once (a boot step), then new E.World3D(game, { level, ... }) for each level. In a scene:\n32\t  update(dt) { your rules, then world.step(dt) } and draw(r) { world.draw(r), then your HUD }. Paused or frozen\n33\t  (game.freeze), update doesn't run, so the world holds still and still draws. A frame between steps draws the actors\n34\t  and the camera part way from the step before (game.alpha: even motion at 144 Hz); a pose set in onDraw is placed as set.\n35\t- Deterministic: the world steps in the game's fixed steps; gameplay randomness comes from E.rng(seed); the camera's\n36\t  pose is worked out in the steps. world.reset() then the same inputs give the same world.hash() on WebGPU, WebGL 2 and\n37\t  run again. Gameplay never reads the picture or the GPU: it reads actors, props and the level.\n38\t- The camera decides what \"up the stick\" means: move with world.camera.ground(game.input.move()).\n39\t\n40\t## Quick start: a complete game (collect the gems, mind the slimes)\n41\t```js quickstart\n42\tconst E = My3D2dge;\n43\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: E.World3D.INPUT, menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } });\n44\tconst LEVEL = { rows: [\n45\t  '################',\n46\t  '#t............t#',\n47\t  '#..g.....==..g.#',\n48\t  '#........==....#',\n49\t  '#..s.....^^....#',\n50\t  '#.............s#',\n51\t  '#..g...@....g..#',\n52\t  '#t............t#',\n53\t  '################'],\n54\t  legend: { '=': { floor: 16 }, '^': { stairs: 'n', floor: 16 }, g: { mark: 'gem' }, s: { mark: 'slime' }, '@': { mark: 'start' } } };\n55\tlet world, hero, slimes, gems, hp, done;\n56\tconst move = [0, 0];\n57\tconst play = {\n58\t  view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter', 'topdown'], pausable: true, touch: ['jump'], camera: { zoom: [.6, 2] },\n59\t  enter() {\n60\t    world.reset(); const rnd = E.rng(1), s = world.marks.start[0];\n61\t    hero = world.hero({ x: s.x, y: s.y, rig: new E.Humanoid({ colors: { cloth: '#2f8f86' } }) });\n62\t    slimes = world.marks.slime.map(m => world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, blob: new E.Blob({ R: 6 }) }));\n63\t    gems = world.marks.gem.map(m => world.thing('gem', m.x, m.y, m.z + 2, { spin: .5, bob: 3 }));\n64\t    world.camera.follow(hero); hp = 3; done = false;\n65\t    for (const e of slimes) e.data.t = rnd() * 2;\n66\t  },\n67\t  update(dt) {\n68\t    if (game.input.pressed('camera')) world.camera.set(world.camera.mode === 'view' ? 'chase' : 'view');\n69\t    world.camera.ground(game.input.move(), move);\n70\t    hero.vx = E.approach(hero.vx, move[0] * 90, 900 * dt); hero.vy = E.approach(hero.vy, move[1] * 90, 900 * dt);\n71\t    if (Math.hypot(move[0], move[1]) > .1) hero.facing = Math.atan2(move[1], move[0]);\n72\t    if (hero.grounded && game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(170);\n73\t    for (const e of slimes) {   // hop at the hero now and then; touch one: a heart lost, knocked back\n74\t      if ((e.data.t -= dt) < 0 && e.grounded) { e.data.t = 1.2; const a = Math.atan2(hero.y - e.y, hero.x - e.x); e.vx = Math.cos(a) * 60; e.vy = Math.sin(a) * 60; e.vz = 140; e.facing = a; }\n75\t      if (Math.hypot(e.x - hero.x, e.y - hero.y) < 11 && Math.abs(e.z - hero.z) < 10 && !(hero.data.inv > 0)) { hp--; hero.data.inv = 1; hero.push((hero.x - e.x) * 12, (hero.y - e.y) * 12, 120); game.shake(3); }\n76\t    }\n77\t    hero.data.inv = (hero.data.inv || 0) - dt;\n78\t    for (const t of world.touching(hero, 'gem')) { world.remove(t); gems.splice(gems.indexOf(t), 1); game.particles.glints(t.x, t.y, t.z + 6, 8, '#bff8ff'); }\n79\t    if (!done && (!gems.length || hp <= 0)) { done = true; game.note(gems.length ? 'OUCH!' : 'ALL GEMS!', 2); game.after(2, () => game.go('play')); }\n80\t    world.step(dt);\n81\t  },\n82\t  draw(r) {\n83\t    world.draw(r);\n84\t    r.overlay(g => { E.ui.hearts(g, 6, 6, Math.max(0, hp), 3); E.font.text(g, 'GEMS ' + gems.length, 6, 18, '#bff8ff'); });\n85\t  }\n86\t};\n87\tgame.start({ scenes: { play }, scene: 'play', boot: { steps: [\n88\t  ['The 3D engine', () => E.World3D.init(game)],\n89\t  ['The level', () => { world = new E.World3D(game, { level: LEVEL }); world.prepare(); }]] } });\n90\t```\n91\t\n92\t## The level: text, one character per tile; row 0 is north\n93\tlevel: { rows, legend, ground, side, colors, bottom }. A legend entry says what its character is (the defaults: '#' wall\n94\t48, 'w' wall 12, 'P' pillar 56, '.' floor, ' ' pit, 't' brazier):\n95\t  { floor: h }        walkable at height h (0 the ground; above 0 a raised floor, solid to the ground)\n96\t  { wall: h }         a solid block h tall, cut low where it stands between a view camera and the level (cut: false)\n97\t  { pillar: h }       each block of these tiles is one pillar, cut to a stump when it hides the target\n98\t  { stairs: 'n'|'s'|'e'|'w', from: 0, floor: 16 }   rising toward that side, from height `from` to `floor`\n99\t  { platform: h, thick: 4 }   a slab in the air, its top at h (walk under it); add pit: true for nothing below\n100\t  { pit: true }       no floor: a body that falls in is lost (actor.fell)\n101\t  { torch: true }     a brazier with a flickering light (the lights go to the torches nearest the target)\n102\t  { mark: 'name' }    a spot: world.marks.name -> [{ x, y, z, cx, cy }] (the tile's centre, on its surface)\n103\t  { shape: 'bench', facing, scale, mats, solid }   a shape standing on the tile (world.shape), walked round when solid\n104\tand its look: ground ('flagstone' 'grass' 'dirt' 'sand' 'snow' 'planks' 'tiles' 'plain' 'water' 'lava', or (x, y) =>\n105\t[r, g, b]) with colors { base, dark, light }, side ('brick' 'block' 'earth' 'planks' 'metal') with color (and top, line).\n106\tThe level's ground is every tile's default; its side styles the floors' edges, its wallSide the walls ('brick'; a tile's\n107\town side wins). Add looks: E.World3D.GROUND.name, E.World3D.SIDE.name.\n108\t\n109\t## The world: new E.World3D(game, o)\n110\to: { level, look: 'card' | 'puppet', res: 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full', gravity: 480, sky: '#06050b' or [top,\n111\thorizon], fog: { color, near, far } (units past the target) or false, ambient: [sky, ground, intensity], sun: { color,\n112\tintensity, dir: [x, y, z] (it shines along it), area, shadow }, torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 1, torchPower: 30,\n113\tlights: 2 (your own), spots: 0 (flashlights), glowLights: 4, shadows, outlines, filter, camera: { mode, proj, fov, chase, ... }, terrain (an open\n114\tworld instead of the level: below), overlay: { fov } (first person: below), onDraw: (world, r) => {} (your own 3D drawing\n115\teach frame, whichever scene draws the world) }\n116\t  world.step(dt) / world.draw(r) / world.reset() / world.hash([your numbers]) / world.prepare() (build the shaders now)\n117\t  world.dispose(): frees a world (its physics, meshes and textures); dispose a level's world before making the next\n118\t  world.width, depth (units), mw, mh (tiles), bottom, marks, torches, actors, props, platforms, things, time, stats\n119\t  world.ground(x, y)   the ground's height (a wall's top on a wall; bottom over a pit)\n120\t  world.floorAt(x, y, z)   the surface a body at height z stands on or falls to (platforms too)\n121\t  world.topH(x, y)     the top of whatever stands there (shots stop below it)\n122\t  world.tile(cx, cy), spec(cx, cy), solidTile(cx, cy)   the level's character, its legend entry, walls and pillars\n123\t  world.flow() -> flow: flow.to(x, y) aims it; flow.dir(x, y, out) -> the way there ([x, y], or null: go straight);\n124\t      it climbs stairs and gentle slopes and drops off ledges, never jumps\n125\t  world.randomFloor(rnd, minDist, fx, fy) -> [x, y]; world.clear(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1) -> a clear line of sight?\n126\t  world.ray(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len, { skip: actor(s), level: true (sight lines), down }) -> the first hit { x, y, z, nx,\n127\t      ny, nz, dist, actor, prop, ground } or null: hitscan, ledges, feet on the ground\n128\t  world.block({ x, y, z, w, d, h, yaw } | { x, y, z, r, h }): an invisible fixed collider (walls you draw your own way;\n129\t      z its base, as for world.box, world.thing and world.shape)\n130\t  world.near(x, y, r, kind) -> actors within r; world.touching(actor, kind) -> things it touches\n131\t  world.project(x, y, z) -> [x, y] in game pixels for the HUD (null behind the camera)\n132\t  world.remove(actor | prop | platform | thing)\n133\t\n134\t## Actors: world.hero(o) and world.mob(o)\n135\thero: a kinematic capsule walked by Rapier's character controller: it slides along walls, climbs stairs and slopes,\n136\tsteps up curbs, rides moving platforms, pushes crates and shoves mobs. mob: a dynamic body; the crowd pushes and piles\n137\tup by itself, knockback is momentum. o: { x, y, z, rig: new E.Humanoid(...) | blob: new E.Blob(...) | orb: { color, r },\n138\tr, half (the capsule: radius, half its straight part; half 0 a ball), facing, fly (no gravity), mass, trail (a color for\n139\tthe rig's weapon trail), look ('card' | 'puppet' for this one), shadow, pose: false (you pose it yourself) }\n140\tEach step you set what it wants: a.vx, a.vy (units a second on the ground: E.approach toward a target speed), a.jump(v)\n141\tor a.vz, a.facing, a.anim (what its rig does: { attack: move.state, pose: 'cheer' | 'die' | 'cast', hurt, dash, expr };\n142\ta blob's { squash, look: [dx, dy], squint, flap }); world.step moves it, reads back a.x, a.y, a.z (its feet), a.vx,\n143\ta.vy, a.vz, a.grounded, a.landed (this step), a.fell (dropped below the level), and poses its rig.\n144\t  a.place(x, y, z), a.push(vx, vy, vz) (knockback), a.setSolid(false) (fallen: it stops blocking the others), a.remove(),\n145\t  a.resize(half) (a crouch, a slide: the capsule shorter, the feet kept; look up with world.ray before standing)\n146\t  a.flash (a hit flash while above 0: count it down yourself, a.flash -= dt), a.fade (0..1), a.sink (units drawn into the floor: spawning, sinking away), a.visible,\n147\t  a.data (yours). E.Attack, E.Combo and E.MOVES work as in 2D: attack.hits(list, e => E.inArc(a, a.facing, e, range,\n148\t  half), e => ...) on actors.\n149\t\n150\t## Props, platforms and things\n151\t  world.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing, scale, mats, flip, params, solid: true }): a shape (docs/ASSETS.md: an E.SHAPES id,\n152\t  a store set's 'SET:id' after E.addAssets, or an entry) in 3D, from the 2D engine's parts and materials, solid as\n153\t  map.solid's box. A reset takes yours away (the legend's stand again); world.shapes holds them; world.remove(s)\n154\t  world.crate(x, y, z, yaw), world.barrel(x, y, z): dynamic bodies (z their centre; left out, on the floor); world.knock(p, fromX, fromY, dv, up) throws one;\n155\t  world.box({ x, y, z, w, d, h, color, side, fixed, mass }); a prop has x, y, z, q (its rotation), data\n156\t  world.platform({ w, d, h, path: [[x, y, z], ...] (its top's points), speed, wait, loop, side, color }): a platform that\n157\t  moves (there and back, or round with loop); heroes on it ride it, bodies on it are carried\n158\t  world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o): drawn by code: coin gem heart key star potion chest door flag sign lever pad spring\n159\t  tree bush rock mushroom fence crystal trunk (an item box) typewriter (a save point); o: { yaw, spin (turns a second),\n160\t  bob, size, color, open (0..1), on, solid: true | [w, d, h] (a block where it stands: world.setSolid(t, false) opens\n161\t  it), data }. Add a kind:\n162\t  E.World3D.THINGS.lamp = (pen, t, time) => { pen.tube(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 20, 1, '#555').glow(0, 0, 21, 2, '#ffd36a'); }\n163\t  A door: { w (32, across its local x), h (40), swing: true (leaves on hinges; else a gate that rises), locked: 'iron' (a\n164\t  key's id) }. world.reach(hero, 14, kinds) -> the thing in front of it within reach (what a check button acts on);\n165\t  world.unlock(door, inv) -> 'open' | 'unlocked' (the key taken from an E.RPG inventory) | 'locked';\n166\t  world.through(door, hero, { then }): the door opening between rooms (Resident Evil's): the camera goes through as it\n167\t  swings open, the hero comes out beyond it; while world.passing the world holds still: skip your rules\n168\t\n169\t## Drawing for one frame (in draw, before world.draw(r))\n170\t  world.arc(x, y, z, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha): a flat arc on the ground (a telegraph)\n171\t  world.glow(x, y, z, r, color, { core, light: true }): a glowing ball (a bolt); the first four asked for light the scene\n172\t  world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll).box(x, y, z, w, d, h, color).ball(x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, color).tube(x0, y0, z0, x1,\n173\t      y1, z1, r, color).cone(...base to tip).bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color).glow(x, y, z, r, color)\n174\t      .slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color) (a box from one point to the other, w wide along a: any lean)\n175\t  world.light({ color, reach, power, flicker }) (made once, with the world): a light; set its x, y, z and on each frame\n176\t  world.flashlight(hero, { color, reach, angle, power, flicker: 0..1 (a failing bulb) }) (a world made with { spots: 1 }):\n177\t  a spot from its hand along its facing, every frame, casting shadows; .on\n178\t  game.particles (sparks, dust, bits, rings, glints, fire, text): drawn in 3D; they land on the level; text goes on the HUD\n179\t  game.shake(n), game.flash(color), game.freeze(s), game.note(text): as in 2D\n180\t\n181\t## The camera: world.camera\n182\t  modes: 'view' (the 2D engine's views as real 3D cameras following camera.target: game.view (game.nextView()),\n183\t  game.yaw (game.rotateView(45)): the starter's shell binds V and [ ] to them, the engine no key; game.zoom (the wheel,\n184\t  a pinch, Settings, where the scene's camera.zoom allows); proj 'persp' | 'ortho'; dist; walls in\n185\t  front cut low), 'chase' (behind the target; it swings round behind as the target moves; a click captures the mouse to\n186\t  turn it), 'first' (the target's eyes), 'fly', 'fixed' (camera.fixed = { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }: your own),\n187\t  'zones' (Resident Evil's: camera.zones = [{ box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], at: [x, y, z], look: [x, y, z] (fixed) | follow:\n188\t  true (turning after the target) | rail: [[x, y, z], [x, y, z]] (sliding level with it), fov (framed for 4:3: a taller\n189\t  screen widens it) }]: the target's zone is the camera, cut once it is camera.margin (8) units in (camera.zone,\n190\t  camera.cuts); across a cut ground() keeps the old way while the stick is held)\n191\t  camera: { capture: true (a click captures the mouse in any mode; camera.takeMouse(out) -> its [dx, dy] since the last\n192\t  call: turn your own camera), near, far (units) }; camera.target also sizes the outlines and centres the sun's shadow\n193\t  camera.set(mode), camera.follow(actor), camera.ground(move, out) -> the stick turned to the ground,\n194\t  camera.aim(actor) -> the angle the mouse (on the floor) or right stick points from it, or null; camera.heading,\n195\t  camera.pose, camera.chase = { pitch, dist, fov, height, auto }, camera.first = { pitch, fov }\n196\t  camera.steer(hero, move, dt, out) -> the way to go by the player's setting (game.settings.define(E.World3D.CONTROLS)):\n197\t  ground(), or tank controls (up forward along hero.facing, down back, left and right turn it: set facing yourself only\n198\t  when !camera.tank)\n199\t  Lock-on (Zelda's targeting): camera.lock(hero, mobs, { range: 160 }) -> the one in sight (alive, in range, a clear\n200\t  line) nearest where hero faces, or null; camera.cycle(mobs, 1 | -1) the next round the hero; camera.unlock();\n201\t  camera.lockOn. The chase and first cameras swing behind the hero to frame both, the view frames both, ground() strafes\n202\t  round it, a reticle marks it (camera.reticle: a color, false); it lets go when the target dies (alive = false), leaves\n203\t  or goes past 1.25 times the range. Turn the hero to it yourself\n204\t\n205\t## Open worlds: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } })\n206\tterrain: { size (32768: two kilometres), height, color: (x, y, z, nz, out) => [r, g, b] (0..255), cell (32), chunk (32\n207\tcells), far (draw distance), physics (heightfields this near an actor), detail (1.7), rock: { colors, band, slope: [s0,\n208\ts1] } (strata where it steepens), speckle, mottle, bottom }. Streamed: a chunk is sampled when first asked about, its\n209\tcollider made near actors (world.step), its meshes near the camera (world.draw: finer near). world.ground, floorAt, topH\n210\tand world.terrain.normal(x, y) read the triangles Rapier collides with; flow() goes straight. sky: { top, horizon, ground,\n211\tsun, haze } is a dome; fog: { color, near, far }. Keep height() fast: it runs per sample.\n212\t\n213\t## Vehicles, tracks, flight (the RACING and FLIGHT slices show them)\n214\tworld.vehicle({ kind: 'kart' | 'car' | 'hover', x, y, z, angle, rig (its driver, seated), color, and the drive module's\n215\tE.Car options over the kind's (top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, hop...), surfaces, ground: (x, y) => tag }): a ball\n216\tRapier rolls (walls, bumps, ramps, jumps) steered by E.Car's arcade handling; an actor. Each step v.update(dt, null,\n217\t{ steer, gas, brake, drift }) (or an input), then world.step; it reads speed, slide, angle, drifting, charge (a kart's\n218\tdrift boost), boostT, onGround, surface ('road', 'boost', a track's off, the level's ground: grass, sand... slow it),\n219\tbumped; v.boost(sec, power), v.spinOut(sec). E.Race (the drive module) races vehicles as it races E.Cars.\n220\tworld.track({ path: new E.Path(points [x, y, z], { closed: true, smooth: 'catmull' }), width: 96, bank: .25 (radians at\n221\tthe tightest bends), walls: true, kerb: 8, pads: [[d, across]] (boost pads), gaps: [[d0, d1, side]] (no wall: a\n222\tshortcut's way off), off (the surface beside it, 'grass'; null: the ground's own), surface: 'road' (a shortcut's\n223\t'dirt'), color, line }): the road and its walls, drawn\n224\tand solid (heights in the path: hills, a hump to jump; banked about the low edge); track.at(d) -> { x, y, z, angle, bank\n225\t}, track.where(x, y) -> { d, across, z }, track.surface(x, y). A terrain under it keeps below it (your height function).\n226\tworld.flyer({ x, y, z, yaw, speed: 300, min, max (brake, boost), turn, climb, bank, invert, low (least height), bounds:\n227\t[x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] | rail: { path, speed, w, h } (Star Fox: the rail's point rides on, the ship moves about a w x h\n228\twindow across it) }): each step f.update(dt, { steer: [x, y], boost, brake, roll: -1 | 1 (a barrel roll: f.rolling),\n229\tloop }); f.x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, speed, frame (the rail's point), hitGround; f.seek(list, { cone, range }): what a\n230\tcharged shot locks on; f.at(): where to draw it this frame. world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll) tips the pen.\n231\tcamera 'behind': behind the target's heading (yaw, angle or facing) and pitch, swinging after it (camera.behind = { dist,\n232\theight, ahead, lag, fov, roll }): a kart's camera, a ship's (follow f.frame on a rail).\n233\tSplit screen: game.splitScreen(2) and world.addCamera(o): viewport i draws through world.cameras[i]; world.project\n234\tanswers in the viewport drawn last; no filter while split.\n235\t\n236\t## First person and third: a shooter (the starter's SHOOTER slice shows it all)\n237\tcamera 'fixed' with capture: each step turn by camera.takeMouse(), set camera.fixed (the eyes, or over the shoulder pulled\n238\tin by world.ray). overlay: { fov } makes world.overlay = { scene, camera, pen, on }: drawn after the world, its depth\n239\tcleared (the gun never sinks into a wall), lit like the world. overlay.pen is a pen in the eye's frame (engine units: x\n240\tahead, y right, z up): draw the arms and gun in onDraw; world.pen there draws bodies (the pens empty after each frame).\n241\t\n242\t## The look\n243\t  world.look = 'card' | 'puppet'; world.res = 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full'; world.shadows; world.outlines\n244\t  world.filter = { look: 'clean' | 'cel' (Comic cel: flat bands of light, ink) | 'pixel' (big dithered pixels), apply:\n245\t  'all' | 'objects' | 'env', bloom, fxaa, bands, ink, inkW, punch, px, levels, dither }\n246\t  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n247\t  E.World3D.INPUT: WASD or arrows move, Space jumps, J or a click attacks, Shift dashes, E skill, Q lock, C camera.\n248\t\n249\t## Your own three.js\n250\tE.THREE (three/webgpu), E.TSL, E.RAPIER; world.scene, world.pw (Rapier's world), E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z) (engine\n251\tunits to three's metres, y up). The rules: WebGPURenderer and node materials only (MeshLambertNodeMaterial,\n252\tMeshToonNodeMaterial, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, TSL): never WebGLRenderer, ShaderMaterial, onBeforeCompile, EffectComposer or\n253\tthree/addons (not vendored); no compute shaders or storage buffers; nothing read back from the GPU. An InstancedMesh with\n254\tover 1,000 instances never uses DynamicDrawUsage (r182 drops its updates). Make meshes and lights when the world is made,\n255\tnot mid-game (a new material builds its shader: a stall).\n256\t\n257\t## Tests\n258\tHeadless Chromium runs it on WebGL 2 (?backend=webgl) and WebGPU (SwiftShader). world.hash() is the proof; game.advance(s)\n259\truns fixed steps at once; game.input.hold / tap script input. The kits expose window.__game.\n260\t*/\n261\timport * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\n262\timport * as TSL from 'three/tsl';"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5572b217-8052-4a87-b3f3-49ea658fe605","uuid":"b8d908da-887e-4ff8-b12e-23108a58c14c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:53:58.378Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-185330/_ref/engine-src/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js","content":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge 3D v0.85.2: real 3D worlds under my-3D2dge games (three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3)\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n\nA 3D world, its physics and its camera under a my-3D2dge game. The 2D engine (engine/my-3d2dge.js) still runs the game:\nits exact fixed steps, scenes, input, pause menu, settings, touch buttons, sound, the rigs and their moves, the HUD. This\nmodule simulates and draws the world under the game's clear canvas. Everything is drawn by code: levels written as text,\ntextures pixel by pixel, characters by the 2D engine's rigs (as cards, or as 3D puppets on the same joints), props and\npickups from four shapes. No image, model or sound files.\n\nAGENTS: this header is the whole manual for the 3D side; the API card (API.md) covers the 2D side (E.Game, input, rigs,\nmoves, E.font, E.ui, E.Menu, audio). Read the code below to debug it, or to change it (it is yours to change, in any\nway you see fit): its sections start with \"/* ===\" and a number.\n\n## Host it (served: browsers load modules only over http; npx serve at the repository's root, or my-3d2dge.vercel.app)\n<script type=\"importmap\">{ \"imports\": { \"three\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n  \"three/webgpu\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\", \"three/tsl\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js\",\n  \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"/vendor/rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js\" } }</script>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #000 }</style>\n<div id=\"stage\" style=\"position:relative;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden\">\n  <canvas id=\"view\"></canvas><canvas id=\"screen\" style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%\"></canvas></div>\n<script src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge.js\"></script>                   the 2D engine, a classic script, first\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js\"></script>  this file\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"game.js\"></script>                your game, a module (const E = My3D2dge;)\n\n## Mental model\n- The 2D engine's units: x east, y south, z up; 16 units = 1 metre = 1 tile; speeds in units a second; angles in\n  radians from +x toward +y (0 east, PI/2 south, -PI/2 north).\n- new E.Game({ ..., bg: null }): its canvas is clear, and the HUD draws on it over the 3D picture (r.overlay, r.text,\n  E.ui, E.font) in game pixels, r.W x r.H. res: 'ps1', expand: true as in the 2D games.\n- await E.World3D.init(game) once (a boot step), then new E.World3D(game, { level, ... }) for each level. In a scene:\n  update(dt) { your rules, then world.step(dt) } and draw(r) { world.draw(r), then your HUD }. Paused or frozen\n  (game.freeze), update doesn't run, so the world holds still and still draws. A frame between steps draws the actors\n  and the camera part way from the step before (game.alpha: even motion at 144 Hz); a pose set in onDraw is placed as set.\n- Deterministic: the world steps in the game's fixed steps; gameplay randomness comes from E.rng(seed); the camera's\n  pose is worked out in the steps. world.reset() then the same inputs give the same world.hash() on WebGPU, WebGL 2 and\n  run again. Gameplay never reads the picture or the GPU: it reads actors, props and the level.\n- The camera decides what \"up the stick\" means: move with world.camera.ground(game.input.move()).\n\n## Quick start: a complete game (collect the gems, mind the slimes)\n```js quickstart\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: E.World3D.INPUT, menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } });\nconst LEVEL = { rows: [\n  '################',\n  '#t............t#',\n  '#..g.....==..g.#',\n  '#........==....#',\n  '#..s.....^^....#',\n  '#.............s#',\n  '#..g...@....g..#',\n  '#t............t#',\n  '################'],\n  legend: { '=': { floor: 16 }, '^': { stairs: 'n', floor: 16 }, g: { mark: 'gem' }, s: { mark: 'slime' }, '@': { mark: 'start' } } };\nlet world, hero, slimes, gems, hp, done;\nconst move = [0, 0];\nconst play = {\n  view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter', 'topdown'], pausable: true, touch: ['jump'], camera: { zoom: [.6, 2] },\n  enter() {\n    world.reset(); const rnd = E.rng(1), s = world.marks.start[0];\n    hero = world.hero({ x: s.x, y: s.y, rig: new E.Humanoid({ colors: { cloth: '#2f8f86' } }) });\n    slimes = world.marks.slime.map(m => world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, blob: new E.Blob({ R: 6 }) }));\n    gems = world.marks.gem.map(m => world.thing('gem', m.x, m.y, m.z + 2, { spin: .5, bob: 3 }));\n    world.camera.follow(hero); hp = 3; done = false;\n    for (const e of slimes) e.data.t = rnd() * 2;\n  },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (game.input.pressed('camera')) world.camera.set(world.camera.mode === 'view' ? 'chase' : 'view');\n    world.camera.ground(game.input.move(), move);\n    hero.vx = E.approach(hero.vx, move[0] * 90, 900 * dt); hero.vy = E.approach(hero.vy, move[1] * 90, 900 * dt);\n    if (Math.hypot(move[0], move[1]) > .1) hero.facing = Math.atan2(move[1], move[0]);\n    if (hero.grounded && game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(170);\n    for (const e of slimes) {   // hop at the hero now and then; touch one: a heart lost, knocked back\n      if ((e.data.t -= dt) < 0 && e.grounded) { e.data.t = 1.2; const a = Math.atan2(hero.y - e.y, hero.x - e.x); e.vx = Math.cos(a) * 60; e.vy = Math.sin(a) * 60; e.vz = 140; e.facing = a; }\n      if (Math.hypot(e.x - hero.x, e.y - hero.y) < 11 && Math.abs(e.z - hero.z) < 10 && !(hero.data.inv > 0)) { hp--; hero.data.inv = 1; hero.push((hero.x - e.x) * 12, (hero.y - e.y) * 12, 120); game.shake(3); }\n    }\n    hero.data.inv = (hero.data.inv || 0) - dt;\n    for (const t of world.touching(hero, 'gem')) { world.remove(t); gems.splice(gems.indexOf(t), 1); game.particles.glints(t.x, t.y, t.z + 6, 8, '#bff8ff'); }\n    if (!done && (!gems.length || hp <= 0)) { done = true; game.note(gems.length ? 'OUCH!' : 'ALL GEMS!', 2); game.after(2, () => game.go('play')); }\n    world.step(dt);\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    world.draw(r);\n    r.overlay(g => { E.ui.hearts(g, 6, 6, Math.max(0, hp), 3); E.font.text(g, 'GEMS ' + gems.length, 6, 18, '#bff8ff'); });\n  }\n};\ngame.start({ scenes: { play }, scene: 'play', boot: { steps: [\n  ['The 3D engine', () => E.World3D.init(game)],\n  ['The level', () => { world = new E.World3D(game, { level: LEVEL }); world.prepare(); }]] } });\n```\n\n## The level: text, one character per tile; row 0 is north\nlevel: { rows, legend, ground, side, colors, bottom }. A legend entry says what its character is (the defaults: '#' wall\n48, 'w' wall 12, 'P' pillar 56, '.' floor, ' ' pit, 't' brazier):\n  { floor: h }        walkable at height h (0 the ground; above 0 a raised floor, solid to the ground)\n  { wall: h }         a solid block h tall, cut low where it stands between a view camera and the level (cut: false)\n  { pillar: h }       each block of these tiles is one pillar, cut to a stump when it hides the target\n  { stairs: 'n'|'s'|'e'|'w', from: 0, floor: 16 }   rising toward that side, from height `from` to `floor`\n  { platform: h, thick: 4 }   a slab in the air, its top at h (walk under it); add pit: true for nothing below\n  { pit: true }       no floor: a body that falls in is lost (actor.fell)\n  { torch: true }     a brazier with a flickering light (the lights go to the torches nearest the target)\n  { mark: 'name' }    a spot: world.marks.name -> [{ x, y, z, cx, cy }] (the tile's centre, on its surface)\n  { shape: 'bench', facing, scale, mats, solid }   a shape standing on the tile (world.shape), walked round when solid\nand its look: ground ('flagstone' 'grass' 'dirt' 'sand' 'snow' 'planks' 'tiles' 'plain' 'water' 'lava', or (x, y) =>\n[r, g, b]) with colors { base, dark, light }, side ('brick' 'block' 'earth' 'planks' 'metal') with color (and top, line).\nThe level's ground is every tile's default; its side styles the floors' edges, its wallSide the walls ('brick'; a tile's\nown side wins). Add looks: E.World3D.GROUND.name, E.World3D.SIDE.name.\n\n## The world: new E.World3D(game, o)\no: { level, look: 'card' | 'puppet', res: 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full', gravity: 480, sky: '#06050b' or [top,\nhorizon], fog: { color, near, far } (units past the target) or false, ambient: [sky, ground, intensity], sun: { color,\nintensity, dir: [x, y, z] (it shines along it), area, shadow }, torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 1, torchPower: 30,\nlights: 2 (your own), spots: 0 (flashlights), glowLights: 4, shadows, outlines, filter, camera: { mode, proj, fov, chase, ... }, terrain (an open\nworld instead of the level: below), overlay: { fov } (first person: below), onDraw: (world, r) => {} (your own 3D drawing\neach frame, whichever scene draws the world) }\n  world.step(dt) / world.draw(r) / world.reset() / world.hash([your numbers]) / world.prepare() (build the shaders now)\n  world.dispose(): frees a world (its physics, meshes and textures); dispose a level's world before making the next\n  world.width, depth (units), mw, mh (tiles), bottom, marks, torches, actors, props, platforms, things, time, stats\n  world.ground(x, y)   the ground's height (a wall's top on a wall; bottom over a pit)\n  world.floorAt(x, y, z)   the surface a body at height z stands on or falls to (platforms too)\n  world.topH(x, y)     the top of whatever stands there (shots stop below it)\n  world.tile(cx, cy), spec(cx, cy), solidTile(cx, cy)   the level's character, its legend entry, walls and pillars\n  world.flow() -> flow: flow.to(x, y) aims it; flow.dir(x, y, out) -> the way there ([x, y], or null: go straight);\n      it climbs stairs and gentle slopes and drops off ledges, never jumps\n  world.randomFloor(rnd, minDist, fx, fy) -> [x, y]; world.clear(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1) -> a clear line of sight?\n  world.ray(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len, { skip: actor(s), level: true (sight lines), down }) -> the first hit { x, y, z, nx,\n      ny, nz, dist, actor, prop, ground } or null: hitscan, ledges, feet on the ground\n  world.block({ x, y, z, w, d, h, yaw } | { x, y, z, r, h }): an invisible fixed collider (walls you draw your own way;\n      z its base, as for world.box, world.thing and world.shape)\n  world.near(x, y, r, kind) -> actors within r; world.touching(actor, kind) -> things it touches\n  world.project(x, y, z) -> [x, y] in game pixels for the HUD (null behind the camera)\n  world.remove(actor | prop | platform | thing)\n\n## Actors: world.hero(o) and world.mob(o)\nhero: a kinematic capsule walked by Rapier's character controller: it slides along walls, climbs stairs and slopes,\nsteps up curbs, rides moving platforms, pushes crates and shoves mobs. mob: a dynamic body; the crowd pushes and piles\nup by itself, knockback is momentum. o: { x, y, z, rig: new E.Humanoid(...) | blob: new E.Blob(...) | orb: { color, r },\nr, half (the capsule: radius, half its straight part; half 0 a ball), facing, fly (no gravity), mass, trail (a color for\nthe rig's weapon trail), look ('card' | 'puppet' for this one), shadow, pose: false (you pose it yourself) }\nEach step you set what it wants: a.vx, a.vy (units a second on the ground: E.approach toward a target speed), a.jump(v)\nor a.vz, a.facing, a.anim (what its rig does: { attack: move.state, pose: 'cheer' | 'die' | 'cast', hurt, dash, expr };\na blob's { squash, look: [dx, dy], squint, flap }); world.step moves it, reads back a.x, a.y, a.z (its feet), a.vx,\na.vy, a.vz, a.grounded, a.landed (this step), a.fell (dropped below the level), and poses its rig.\n  a.place(x, y, z), a.push(vx, vy, vz) (knockback), a.setSolid(false) (fallen: it stops blocking the others), a.remove(),\n  a.resize(half) (a crouch, a slide: the capsule shorter, the feet kept; look up with world.ray before standing)\n  a.flash (a hit flash while above 0: count it down yourself, a.flash -= dt), a.fade (0..1), a.sink (units drawn into the floor: spawning, sinking away), a.visible,\n  a.data (yours). E.Attack, E.Combo and E.MOVES work as in 2D: attack.hits(list, e => E.inArc(a, a.facing, e, range,\n  half), e => ...) on actors.\n\n## Props, platforms and things\n  world.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing, scale, mats, flip, params, solid: true }): a shape (docs/ASSETS.md: an E.SHAPES id,\n  a store set's 'SET:id' after E.addAssets, or an entry) in 3D, from the 2D engine's parts and materials, solid as\n  map.solid's box. A reset takes yours away (the legend's stand again); world.shapes holds them; world.remove(s)\n  world.crate(x, y, z, yaw), world.barrel(x, y, z): dynamic bodies (z their centre; left out, on the floor); world.knock(p, fromX, fromY, dv, up) throws one;\n  world.box({ x, y, z, w, d, h, color, side, fixed, mass }); a prop has x, y, z, q (its rotation), data\n  world.platform({ w, d, h, path: [[x, y, z], ...] (its top's points), speed, wait, loop, side, color }): a platform that\n  moves (there and back, or round with loop); heroes on it ride it, bodies on it are carried\n  world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o): drawn by code: coin gem heart key star potion chest door flag sign lever pad spring\n  tree bush rock mushroom fence crystal trunk (an item box) typewriter (a save point); o: { yaw, spin (turns a second),\n  bob, size, color, open (0..1), on, solid: true | [w, d, h] (a block where it stands: world.setSolid(t, false) opens\n  it), data }. Add a kind:\n  E.World3D.THINGS.lamp = (pen, t, time) => { pen.tube(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 20, 1, '#555').glow(0, 0, 21, 2, '#ffd36a'); }\n  A door: { w (32, across its local x), h (40), swing: true (leaves on hinges; else a gate that rises), locked: 'iron' (a\n  key's id) }. world.reach(hero, 14, kinds) -> the thing in front of it within reach (what a check button acts on);\n  world.unlock(door, inv) -> 'open' | 'unlocked' (the key taken from an E.RPG inventory) | 'locked';\n  world.through(door, hero, { then }): the door opening between rooms (Resident Evil's): the camera goes through as it\n  swings open, the hero comes out beyond it; while world.passing the world holds still: skip your rules\n\n## Drawing for one frame (in draw, before world.draw(r))\n  world.arc(x, y, z, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha): a flat arc on the ground (a telegraph)\n  world.glow(x, y, z, r, color, { core, light: true }): a glowing ball (a bolt); the first four asked for light the scene\n  world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll).box(x, y, z, w, d, h, color).ball(x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, color).tube(x0, y0, z0, x1,\n      y1, z1, r, color).cone(...base to tip).bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color).glow(x, y, z, r, color)\n      .slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color) (a box from one point to the other, w wide along a: any lean)\n  world.light({ color, reach, power, flicker }) (made once, with the world): a light; set its x, y, z and on each frame\n  world.flashlight(hero, { color, reach, angle, power, flicker: 0..1 (a failing bulb) }) (a world made with { spots: 1 }):\n  a spot from its hand along its facing, every frame, casting shadows; .on\n  game.particles (sparks, dust, bits, rings, glints, fire, text): drawn in 3D; they land on the level; text goes on the HUD\n  game.shake(n), game.flash(color), game.freeze(s), game.note(text): as in 2D\n\n## The camera: world.camera\n  modes: 'view' (the 2D engine's views as real 3D cameras following camera.target: game.view (game.nextView()),\n  game.yaw (game.rotateView(45)): the starter's shell binds V and [ ] to them, the engine no key; game.zoom (the wheel,\n  a pinch, Settings, where the scene's camera.zoom allows); proj 'persp' | 'ortho'; dist; walls in\n  front cut low), 'chase' (behind the target; it swings round behind as the target moves; a click captures the mouse to\n  turn it), 'first' (the target's eyes), 'fly', 'fixed' (camera.fixed = { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }: your own),\n  'zones' (Resident Evil's: camera.zones = [{ box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], at: [x, y, z], look: [x, y, z] (fixed) | follow:\n  true (turning after the target) | rail: [[x, y, z], [x, y, z]] (sliding level with it), fov (framed for 4:3: a taller\n  screen widens it) }]: the target's zone is the camera, cut once it is camera.margin (8) units in (camera.zone,\n  camera.cuts); across a cut ground() keeps the old way while the stick is held)\n  camera: { capture: true (a click captures the mouse in any mode; camera.takeMouse(out) -> its [dx, dy] since the last\n  call: turn your own camera), near, far (units) }; camera.target also sizes the outlines and centres the sun's shadow\n  camera.set(mode), camera.follow(actor), camera.ground(move, out) -> the stick turned to the ground,\n  camera.aim(actor) -> the angle the mouse (on the floor) or right stick points from it, or null; camera.heading,\n  camera.pose, camera.chase = { pitch, dist, fov, height, auto }, camera.first = { pitch, fov }\n  camera.steer(hero, move, dt, out) -> the way to go by the player's setting (game.settings.define(E.World3D.CONTROLS)):\n  ground(), or tank controls (up forward along hero.facing, down back, left and right turn it: set facing yourself only\n  when !camera.tank)\n  Lock-on (Zelda's targeting): camera.lock(hero, mobs, { range: 160 }) -> the one in sight (alive, in range, a clear\n  line) nearest where hero faces, or null; camera.cycle(mobs, 1 | -1) the next round the hero; camera.unlock();\n  camera.lockOn. The chase and first cameras swing behind the hero to frame both, the view frames both, ground() strafes\n  round it, a reticle marks it (camera.reticle: a color, false); it lets go when the target dies (alive = false), leaves\n  or goes past 1.25 times the range. Turn the hero to it yourself\n\n## Open worlds: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } })\nterrain: { size (32768: two kilometres), height, color: (x, y, z, nz, out) => [r, g, b] (0..255), cell (32), chunk (32\ncells), far (draw distance), physics (heightfields this near an actor), detail (1.7), rock: { colors, band, slope: [s0,\ns1] } (strata where it steepens), speckle, mottle, bottom }. Streamed: a chunk is sampled when first asked about, its\ncollider made near actors (world.step), its meshes near the camera (world.draw: finer near). world.ground, floorAt, topH\nand world.terrain.normal(x, y) read the triangles Rapier collides with; flow() goes straight. sky: { top, horizon, ground,\nsun, haze } is a dome; fog: { color, near, far }. Keep height() fast: it runs per sample.\n\n## Vehicles, tracks, flight (the RACING and FLIGHT slices show them)\nworld.vehicle({ kind: 'kart' | 'car' | 'hover', x, y, z, angle, rig (its driver, seated), color, and the drive module's\nE.Car options over the kind's (top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, hop...), surfaces, ground: (x, y) => tag }): a ball\nRapier rolls (walls, bumps, ramps, jumps) steered by E.Car's arcade handling; an actor. Each step v.update(dt, null,\n{ steer, gas, brake, drift }) (or an input), then world.step; it reads speed, slide, angle, drifting, charge (a kart's\ndrift boost), boostT, onGround, surface ('road', 'boost', a track's off, the level's ground: grass, sand... slow it),\nbumped; v.boost(sec, power), v.spinOut(sec). E.Race (the drive module) races vehicles as it races E.Cars.\nworld.track({ path: new E.Path(points [x, y, z], { closed: true, smooth: 'catmull' }), width: 96, bank: .25 (radians at\nthe tightest bends), walls: true, kerb: 8, pads: [[d, across]] (boost pads), gaps: [[d0, d1, side]] (no wall: a\nshortcut's way off), off (the surface beside it, 'grass'; null: the ground's own), surface: 'road' (a shortcut's\n'dirt'), color, line }): the road and its walls, drawn\nand solid (heights in the path: hills, a hump to jump; banked about the low edge); track.at(d) -> { x, y, z, angle, bank\n}, track.where(x, y) -> { d, across, z }, track.surface(x, y). A terrain under it keeps below it (your height function).\nworld.flyer({ x, y, z, yaw, speed: 300, min, max (brake, boost), turn, climb, bank, invert, low (least height), bounds:\n[x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] | rail: { path, speed, w, h } (Star Fox: the rail's point rides on, the ship moves about a w x h\nwindow across it) }): each step f.update(dt, { steer: [x, y], boost, brake, roll: -1 | 1 (a barrel roll: f.rolling),\nloop }); f.x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, speed, frame (the rail's point), hitGround; f.seek(list, { cone, range }): what a\ncharged shot locks on; f.at(): where to draw it this frame. world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll) tips the pen.\ncamera 'behind': behind the target's heading (yaw, angle or facing) and pitch, swinging after it (camera.behind = { dist,\nheight, ahead, lag, fov, roll }): a kart's camera, a ship's (follow f.frame on a rail).\nSplit screen: game.splitScreen(2) and world.addCamera(o): viewport i draws through world.cameras[i]; world.project\nanswers in the viewport drawn last; no filter while split.\n\n## First person and third: a shooter (the starter's SHOOTER slice shows it all)\ncamera 'fixed' with capture: each step turn by camera.takeMouse(), set camera.fixed (the eyes, or over the shoulder pulled\nin by world.ray). overlay: { fov } makes world.overlay = { scene, camera, pen, on }: drawn after the world, its depth\ncleared (the gun never sinks into a wall), lit like the world. overlay.pen is a pen in the eye's frame (engine units: x\nahead, y right, z up): draw the arms and gun in onDraw; world.pen there draws bodies (the pens empty after each frame).\n\n## The look\n  world.look = 'card' | 'puppet'; world.res = 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full'; world.shadows; world.outlines\n  world.filter = { look: 'clean' | 'cel' (Comic cel: flat bands of light, ink) | 'pixel' (big dithered pixels), apply:\n  'all' | 'objects' | 'env', bloom, fxaa, bands, ink, inkW, punch, px, levels, dither }\n  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n  E.World3D.INPUT: WASD or arrows move, Space jumps, J or a click attacks, Shift dashes, E skill, Q lock, C camera.\n\n## Your own three.js\nE.THREE (three/webgpu), E.TSL, E.RAPIER; world.scene, world.pw (Rapier's world), E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z) (engine\nunits to three's metres, y up). The rules: WebGPURenderer and node materials only (MeshLambertNodeMaterial,\nMeshToonNodeMaterial, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, TSL): never WebGLRenderer, ShaderMaterial, onBeforeCompile, EffectComposer or\nthree/addons (not vendored); no compute shaders or storage buffers; nothing read back from the GPU. An InstancedMesh with\nover 1,000 instances never uses DynamicDrawUsage (r182 drops its updates). Make meshes and lights when the world is made,\nnot mid-game (a new material builds its shader: a stall).\n\n## Tests\nHeadless Chromium runs it on WebGL 2 (?backend=webgl) and WebGPU (SwiftShader). world.hash() is the proof; game.advance(s)\nruns fixed steps at once; game.input.hold / tap script input. The kits expose window.__game.\n*/\nimport * as THREE from 'three/webgpu';\nimport * as TSL from 'three/tsl';","numLines":262,"startLine":1,"totalLines":3302}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0166YDY8i6A7chQMUwVNRsj6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh45Bn6imGaF8mYYHBmh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NB9DWymqiesoVHuxe6kETj","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-185330/_ref/engine-src/src/starter3d/70-crawler.js"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":825,"cache_read_input_tokens":105605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":825},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5572b217-8052-4a87-b3f3-49ea658fe605","uuid":"574ee900-cda0-46aa-aa2c-9406a645f567","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:53:59.498Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh45BYDBkgKMx9eZR4Pi","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NB9DWymqiesoVHuxe6kETj":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-185330/_ref/engine-src/src/starter3d/70-crawler.js"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NB9DWymqiesoVHuxe6kETj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/* =====================================================================================\n2\t * SLICE 7  CRAWLER  (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder, King's Field). @modules grid\n3\t * The Lantern Vaults in first person, a cell at a time: W and S (or up and down) step forward and back, A and D turn a\n4\t * quarter turn, Q and E step aside, each one tweened. A party of four, their portraits under the view: two in front who\n5\t * fight, two behind who cast. J (or a click on the view) uses what is in front (a lever, a locked gate) or has the next\n6\t * one ready act: a blow at what stands in front, else the mage's bolt; K the mage's bolt down the corridor, H the\n7\t * cleric's heal, 1 to 4 (or a click on a portrait) that one's own act; Tab the map (what the party has seen: E.Fog).\n8\t * Gates that rise (one with an iron lock), a lever on a wall, plates in the floor (one raises a gate, one springs darts);\n9\t * wisps, slimes, the dead of the vaults and the Warden at the bottom; the stair out behind it. Settings, Turns: REAL TIME\n10\t * (each one's gauge fills on game time, E.Turns 'atb': Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder) or TURNS (the vaults wait:\n11\t * each step, turn or blow is the party's turn, the monsters act by their speed, E.Turns 'speed': Wizardry).\n12\t * THE 3D: the camera 'fixed' at the party's eyes, tweened per step; a level of 2 x 2 tiles a cell, braziers in niches,\n13\t * a ceiling and the party's lantern; world.thing gates that rise, and a lever, plates and a stair drawn by the slice;\n14\t * mobs walked cell to cell. Deep link: #crawler/warden (the Warden's hall, its gates open). CRAWLER.run(n): a scripted\n15\t * walk's hash (the proof); CRAWLER.bot(): to the Warden and out\n16\t * ===================================================================================== */\n17\tconst CRAWLER = (() => {\n18\t  const C = 32, PI = Math.PI, EYE = 25, STEP_T = .28, TURN_T = .2, MOVE_T = .4;\n19\t  // the four ways, a quarter turn apart: 0 north, 1 east, 2 south, 3 west\n20\t  const DX = [0, 1, 0, -1], DY = [-1, 0, 1, 0], YAW = d => -PI / 2 + d * PI / 2, WAYS = ['N', 'E', 'S', 'W'];\n21\t  /* ---- THE VAULTS: one character a cell (2 metres: 2 x 2 of the level's tiles). # wall, . floor, @ the start (facing\n22\t   * north), n a wall with a brazier in a niche, L a wall with a lever, G a gate (raised by what is wired to it), K a gate\n23\t   * with an iron lock, P a plate (raises a gate), T a plate that springs darts, X the stair out, i the iron key, h a\n24\t   * flask, w wisps, s slimes, k the dead, W the Warden ---- */\n25\t  const MAP = [\n26\t    '#########n#n###n###n#',\n27\t    '#######.....i.#..X..#',\n28\t    '#######....k..#..W..#',\n29\t    '#######.s.....#.....#',\n30\t    '#.....#.....s.###G###',\n31\t    'n.w.h.#.......#..P..n',\n32\t    '#w....#.......#...k.#',\n33\t    '###.######.######K###',\n34\t    '###............T..###',\n35\t    '######n###G##########',\n36\t    '########.....########',\n37\t    '#######L.....n#######',\n38\t    '########..@..########',\n39\t    '#####################'];\n40\t  const MW = MAP[0].length, MH = MAP.length, at = (x, y) => (MAP[y] || '')[x] || '#';\n41\t  const WALLS = '#nL', wallCell = (x, y) => WALLS.includes(at(x, y));\n42\t  // what is wired to what: a lever's or a plate's cell -> the gate it raises\n43\t  const WIRES = { '7,11': '10,9', '17,5': '17,4' };\n44\t  // a wall cell's open side (a niche's brazier, a lever's face): the first way with floor beyond it\n45\t  const openSide = (x, y) => [0, 1, 2, 3].find(d => !wallCell(x + DX[d], y + DY[d]));\n46\t  // the level: each cell 2 x 2 tiles; a niche holds a brazier ('t') in the tile on its open side\n47\t  const NICHE = [['t#', '##'], ['#t', '##'], ['##', 't#'], ['t#', '##']];\n48\t  const rows = [];\n49\t  for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let k = 0; k < 2; k++) {\n50\t    let row = ''; for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) { const c = at(x, y); row += c === 'n' ? NICHE[openSide(x, y)][k] : wallCell(x, y) ? '##' : '..'; }\n51\t    rows.push(row);\n52\t  }\n53\t  const LEVEL = { rows, ground: 'flagstone', colors: { base: '#4a4656', dark: '#34303e', light: '#5a5668' }, side: 'brick', color: '#4e4858', legend: {} };\n54\t  const mid = c => c * C + C / 2;\n55\t\n56\t  /* ---- THE PARTY: two in front who fight, two behind who cast; each one's portrait is its rig's (drawPortrait) ---- */\n57\t  const PARTY = [\n58\t    { name: 'BRAM', role: 'FIGHTER', hp: 46, speed: 100, hit: [8, 13], rig: { build: 'heroic', hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#8a92a0' }, colors: { cloth: '#7a3a2e', pants: '#3a3440', hair: '#4a2e1e', skin: '#d8a888', metal: '#b8c0cc' } } },\n59\t    { name: 'TESK', role: 'ROGUE', hp: 34, speed: 135, hit: [5, 10], rig: { hood: true, colors: { cloth: '#3a5a3e', pants: '#2e2a26', hair: '#2a3a2c', skin: '#c89070' } } },\n60\t    { name: 'MAREN', role: 'CLERIC', hp: 30, mp: 16, speed: 90, heal: [12, 19], rig: { hair: 'long', hat: 'band', colors: { cloth: '#d8d0b8', pants: '#8a7a5a', hair: '#c8a050', skin: '#e8c0a0', hat: '#c8a040' } } },\n61\t    { name: 'QUILL', role: 'MAGE', hp: 22, mp: 18, speed: 85, bolt: [11, 18], rig: { hat: 'pointed', weapon: null, colors: { cloth: '#3a3a7a', pants: '#2a2a4a', hair: '#e0e0e8', skin: '#e0b090', hat: '#3a3a7a' } } }];\n62\t  const BOLT_MP = 4, HEAL_MP = 3;\n63\t  /* ---- THE MONSTERS: hp, a blow's damage, speed (100: a turn as the party's), how far they see (cells) ---- */\n64\t  const BONE = { bone: '#d8cfb4', cloth: '#2c2434', belt: '#5a4a38', metal: '#b3b8c0', metalDk: '#636872', hilt: '#6a5038' };\n65\t  const WARDEN = { cloth: '#3a3a52', pants: '#2a2832', boot: '#1e1c24', belt: '#5a4a30', trim: '#9a8a5a', metal: '#7a8294', metalDk: '#3e4452', skin: '#8a9aa8', hair: '#1a1a22' };\n66\t  const KINDS = {\n67\t    wisp: { hp: 9, dmg: [2, 4], speed: 150, sight: 4, z: 16 },\n68\t    slime: { hp: 20, dmg: [3, 6], speed: 70, sight: 3 },\n69\t    skeleton: { hp: 28, dmg: [4, 8], speed: 100, sight: 5, move: 'slash' },\n70\t    warden: { hp: 120, dmg: [6, 10], speed: 95, sight: 6, move: 'overhead', boss: true }\n71\t  };\n72\t  const MARK = { w: 'wisp', s: 'slime', k: 'skeleton', W: 'warden' };\n73\t\n74\t  /* ---- THINGS drawn by this slice (the engine's kinds are in its manual): a lever on a wall, a plate in the floor, the\n75\t   * stair out (an arch over steps down, lit once the Warden falls) ---- */\n76\t  W3.THINGS.wallLever = (p, t) => {   // its local +y points out of the wall\n77\t    const a = t.on ? -1 : 1;\n78\t    p.box(0, .8, 20, 6, 1.6, 9, '#4a4452').box(0, 1.8, 20, 2, .8, 5.5, '#24202a')\n79\t      .tube(0, 2.2, 20, 0, 3.6, 20 + a * 5, .55, '#a8a8b8').ball(0, 3.8, 20 + a * 5.4, 1.1, 1.1, 1.1, t.on ? '#4ae070' : '#e8483a');\n80\t  };\n81\t  W3.THINGS.plate = (p, t) => { const s = t.on ? .2 : 1, c = t.color || '#6a6474'; p.box(0, 0, s / 2, 22, 22, s, c).box(0, 0, s + .05, 17, 17, .1, E.shade(c, -.2)); };\n82\t  W3.THINGS.stair = (p, t) => {\n83\t    const s = '#5a5468';\n84\t    p.box(-13, 0, 19, 4, 5, 38, s).box(13, 0, 19, 4, 5, 38, s).box(0, 0, 39, 30, 6, 4, s);\n85\t    for (let k = 0; k < 4; k++) p.box(0, -2 - k * 3, -1 - k * 2.5, 22, 3, 2, '#3a3644');   // the steps going down\n86\t    if (t.on) p.glow(0, 0, 16, 5 + Math.sin((t.t || 0) * 3) * .8, '#9ae8ff').halo(0, 0, 16, 18, [.15, .3, .38]);\n87\t    else p.box(0, 0, 18, 22, 1, 34, '#14121a');\n88\t  };\n89\t\n90\t  /* ---- SOUNDS AND MUSIC (the step sequencer's format: original songs) ---- */\n91\t  const SOUNDS = {\n92\t    step: { wave: 'noise', freq: 320, to: 120, dur: .07, vol: .1, filter: 'lowpass' }, turn: { wave: 'noise', freq: 900, to: 500, dur: .06, vol: .05 },\n93\t    thud: [{ wave: 'square', freq: 90, to: 50, dur: .1, vol: .2 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 300, dur: .06, vol: .12 }],\n94\t    swing: { wave: 'noise', freq: 2600, to: 800, dur: .1, vol: .12 }, bolt: [{ wave: 'saw', freq: 220, to: 880, dur: .18, vol: .16 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 3000, to: 600, dur: .2, vol: .1 }],\n95\t    lever: [{ wave: 'square', freq: 260, to: 140, dur: .08, vol: .2 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 1200, dur: .05, vol: .12, delay: .09 }],\n96\t    gate: { wave: 'saw', freq: 70, to: 110, dur: .9, vol: .12, vib: [12, .1], filter: 'lowpass' }, plate: { wave: 'square', freq: 140, to: 90, dur: .1, vol: .2 },\n97\t    dart: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 4000, to: 2000, dur: .05, vol: .2 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 4000, to: 2000, dur: .05, vol: .2, delay: .07 }],\n98\t    locked: { wave: 'square', freq: 180, dur: .05, vol: .16 }, unlock: { wave: 'square', freq: 660, arp: [0, 7], step: .06, dur: .14, vol: .18 },\n99\t    rattle: { wave: 'noise', freq: 2200, arp: [0, 3, 0, 5], step: .04, dur: .2, vol: .1 }, squelch: { wave: 'sine', freq: 140, to: 60, dur: .16, vol: .25 },\n100\t    zap: { wave: 'square', freq: 1400, to: 300, dur: .1, vol: .1 }, roar: [{ wave: 'saw', freq: 110, to: 55, dur: 1, vol: .2, vib: [7, .12] }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 500, to: 120, dur: .8, vol: .15, filter: 'lowpass' }]\n101\t  };\n102\t  const VAULT = { bpm: 72, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the vaults: a slow figure over a drone, water dripping\n103\t    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .26, notes: 'A1 - - - - - - - | A1 - - - - - - - | F1 - - - - - - - | E1 - - - - - - -' },\n104\t    { wave: 'pulse25', vol: .05, notes: 'A3 . C4 . E4 . . . | D4 . C4 . B3 . . . | A3 . C4 . F4 . E4 . | E4 . . . G#3 . . .' },\n105\t    { wave: 'sine', vol: .07, notes: '. . . . . . E5 . | . . . . . . . . | . . . . . . . A5 | . . . . . . . .' }] };\n106\t  const FIGHT = { bpm: 128, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the Warden\n107\t    { wave: 'saw', vol: .06, notes: 'A3 A3 . A3 C4 . A3 . | G3 G3 . G3 Bb3 . G3 . | F3 F3 . F3 A3 . F3 . | E3 . G#3 . B3 . E4 .' },\n108\t    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'A1 . A1 . A1 . A1 . | G1 . G1 . G1 . G1 . | F1 . F1 . F1 . F1 . | E1 . E1 . E1 . E1 .' },\n109\t    { wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . h k s . h . | k k h . s . h h' }] };\n110\t\n111\t  /* ---- THE STATE ---- */\n112\t  let world = null, hero = null, lamp = null, grid = null, fog = null, turns = null, rnd = Math.random, mode = 'real', scripted = false;\n113\t  let party = null, S = null, foes = [], gates = {}, levers = [], plates = {}, items = [], stair = null, bolts = [], keys = null;\n114\t  let total = 0, msg = null, showMap = false, song = null, ended = 0, slashT = 0, phase = 'party', took = 0, rounds = 0;\n115\t  BOOT.push(['The vaults', () => {\n116\t    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(SOUNDS)) A.define(k, v);\n117\t    world = new W3(game, { level: LEVEL, torchLights: 4, torchShadows: 0, torchPower: 16, torchReach: 160, torchColor: '#ffb070', lights: 2,\n118\t      ambient: ['#5a5478', '#221e2a', 3.4], fog: { color: '#050407', near: 40, far: 250 }, sky: '#050407', camera: { mode: 'fixed' },\n119\t      onDraw: w => {   // the ceiling over the vaults, the bolts in flight, the wisps' zaps\n120\t        w.pen.at().box(w.width / 2, w.depth / 2, 50, w.width, w.depth, 4, '#1c1a22');   // (at(): the pen's origin back at the world's)\n121\t        for (const b of bolts) w.glow(b.x, b.y, b.z, 3.2, '#ffb14a', { light: true });\n122\t        for (const e of foes) if (e.zap > 0) w.pen.at().bar(e.x, e.y, e.z + 2, S.x, S.y, EYE - 6, .6, .6, '#bff4ff');\n123\t      } });\n124\t  }]);\n125\t\n126\t  /** a fresh descent (seed: the dice; m: 'real' or 'turns', else the player's setting) */\n127\t  function reset(seed = 1, m = null) {\n128\t    world.reset(); rnd = E.rng(seed); mode = m || game.settings.crawlTurns || 'real';\n129\t    const st = MAP.findIndex(r => r.includes('@')), sx = MAP[st].indexOf('@');\n130\t    hero = world.hero({ x: mid(sx), y: mid(st), r: 4, visible: false }); world.camera.follow(hero);\n131\t    S = { cx: sx, cy: st, dir: 0, x: mid(sx), y: mid(st), yaw: YAW(0), px: mid(sx), py: mid(st), pyaw: YAW(0), from: null, t: 0, dur: 0, bump: 0, act: 0 };\n132\t    party = PARTY.map((o, i) => ({ i, name: o.name, role: o.role, front: i < 2, max: o.hp, hp: o.hp, mpMax: o.mp || 0, mp: o.mp || 0, speed: o.speed, o, hurtT: 0, flash: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid(Object.assign({ speedRef: 60 }, o.rig)), _turn: 100 }));\n133\t    if (!lamp) lamp = world.light({ color: '#ffd8a0', reach: 190, power: 10 });\n134\t    keys = new Set(); items = []; bolts = []; foes = []; gates = {}; levers = []; plates = {}; stair = null;\n135\t    for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) {\n136\t      const c = at(x, y), k = x + ',' + y;\n137\t      if (c === 'G' || c === 'K') {   // a gate across its corridor (walls east and west: it spans x)\n138\t        const ns = wallCell(x - 1, y) && wallCell(x + 1, y);\n139\t        gates[k] = { cx: x, cy: y, up: false, t: world.thing('door', mid(x), mid(y), 0, { yaw: ns ? 0 : PI / 2, w: 32, h: 46, color: '#26242c', frame: '#3a3444', locked: c === 'K' ? 'iron' : null, solid: true }) };\n140\t      } else if (c === 'L') {\n141\t        const d = openSide(x, y), fx = x + DX[d], fy = y + DY[d];   // its face: toward the floor cell beside it\n142\t        levers.push({ cx: fx, cy: fy, dir: (d + 2) % 4, gate: WIRES[k], t: world.thing('wallLever', mid(x) + DX[d] * C / 2, mid(y) + DY[d] * C / 2, 0, { yaw: Math.atan2(DY[d], DX[d]) - PI / 2 }) });\n143\t      } else if (c === 'P' || c === 'T') plates[k] = { trap: c === 'T', gate: WIRES[k], t: world.thing('plate', mid(x), mid(y), 0, { color: c === 'T' ? '#625c6a' : '#6e6878' }) };\n144\t      else if (c === 'X') stair = { cx: x, cy: y, t: world.thing('stair', mid(x), mid(y) - 6, 0, { on: false }) };\n145\t      else if (c === 'i') items.push({ cx: x, cy: y, kind: 'key', t: world.thing('key', mid(x), mid(y), 5, { color: '#8a8c98', spin: .3, bob: 1.5 }) });\n146\t      else if (c === 'h') items.push({ cx: x, cy: y, kind: 'flask', t: world.thing('potion', mid(x), mid(y), 0, { color: '#e04a4a', spin: .2 }) });\n147\t      else if (MARK[c]) foes.push(spawn(MARK[c], x, y));\n148\t    }\n149\t    total = foes.length;\n150\t    grid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => open(x, y), opaque: (x, y) => wallCell(x, y) || !!(gates[x + ',' + y] && gates[x + ',' + y].t.open < .5) });\n151\t    fog = new E.Fog(grid); look();\n152\t    makeTurns(); msg = null; showMap = false; song = null; ended = 0; slashT = 0; phase = 'party'; took = 0; rounds = 0;\n153\t    world.camera.set('fixed'); place(0);\n154\t  }\n155\t  function spawn(type, x, y) {\n156\t    const k = KINDS[type], X = mid(x), Y = mid(y);\n157\t    const e = type === 'wisp' ? world.mob({ x: X, y: Y, z: k.z, r: 4, half: 0, fly: true, orb: { color: '#8ae0ff', r: 3.6 } })\n158\t      : type === 'slime' ? world.mob({ x: X, y: Y, r: 6, half: 0, mass: 2, blob: new E.Blob({ R: 7, face: 'front', colors: { base: '#5ac86a', dk: '#2e7a3e', lt: '#a8f0a0' } }) })\n159\t      : world.mob({ x: X, y: Y, r: type === 'warden' ? 8 : 4.5, half: type === 'warden' ? 12 : 8, mass: type === 'warden' ? 8 : 1.4,\n160\t        rig: type === 'warden' ? new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.45, build: 'bulky', armor: true, sleeves: 'long', bladeLen: 13, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#5a5e6e' }, eyeGlow: '#7ad8ff', colors: WARDEN, speedRef: 45 })\n161\t          : new E.Humanoid({ build: 'skeleton', bladeLen: 9, colors: BONE, speedRef: 40 }) });\n162\t    return Object.assign(e, { type, k, cx: x, cy: y, hp: k.hp, max: k.hp, speed: k.speed, awake: false, atk: null, hitT: 0, zap: 0, tx: X, ty: Y, deadT: 0, blows: 0, _turn: 0, facing: PI / 2 });\n163\t  }\n164\t  /** the turns: real time, each one's gauge on game time ('atb'); turns, the party one actor among the monsters ('speed') */\n165\t  function makeTurns() {\n166\t    const live = foes.filter(e => e.hp > 0);\n167\t    turns = mode === 'turns' ? new E.Turns([S, ...live], { mode: 'speed' }) : new E.Turns([...party.filter(m => m.hp > 0), ...live], { mode: 'atb', fill: .55 });\n168\t    S.speed = 100; for (const m of party) m._turn = mode === 'turns' ? 100 : Math.min(m._turn, 100);\n169\t  }\n170\t  const say = (text, t = 2.4) => { msg = { text, t }; };\n171\t  const gateAt = (x, y) => gates[x + ',' + y];\n172\t  const foeAt = (x, y) => foes.find(e => e.hp > 0 && e.cx === x && e.cy === y);\n173\t  /** can a body stand in this cell (a wall, a gate down: no) */\n174\t  function open(x, y) { if (wallCell(x, y)) return false; const g = gateAt(x, y); return !g || (g.up && g.t.open > .85); }\n175\t  const alive = () => party.filter(m => m.hp > 0);\n176\t  /** the party sees: the fog's field of view, and the monsters it falls on wake */\n177\t  function look() {\n178\t    fog.update([{ cx: S.cx, cy: S.cy, r: 5 }]);\n179\t    for (const e of foes) if (e.hp > 0 && !e.awake && fog.visible([e.cx, e.cy]) && Math.abs(e.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(e.cy - S.cy) <= e.k.sight) wake(e);\n180\t  }\n181\t  function wake(e) { e.awake = true; A.sfx(e.type === 'slime' ? 'squelch' : e.type === 'wisp' ? 'zap' : e.type === 'warden' ? 'roar' : 'rattle'); if (e.type === 'warden') say('THE WARDEN WAKES', 3); }\n182\t\n183\t  /* ---- MOVING: a step or a turn, tweened; bumping a wall ---- */\n184\t  function place(u) {   // where the eyes are this step (u: the tween's 0..1)\n185\t    const s = u * u * (3 - 2 * u), F = S.from;\n186\t    S.px = S.x; S.py = S.y; S.pyaw = S.yaw;\n187\t    if (F) { S.x = lerp(F[0], mid(S.cx), s); S.y = lerp(F[1], mid(S.cy), s); S.yaw = F[2] + E.angDiff(F[2], YAW(S.dir)) * s; }\n188\t    else { S.x = mid(S.cx); S.y = mid(S.cy); S.yaw = YAW(S.dir); }\n189\t    const b = Math.sin(Math.min(1, S.bump) * PI) * 4;   // a bump into a wall: a lurch forward and back\n190\t    hero.place(S.x + Math.cos(S.yaw) * b, S.y + Math.sin(S.yaw) * b, 0);\n191\t    world.camera.fixed = { x: S.x + Math.cos(S.yaw) * (b - 4), y: S.y + Math.sin(S.yaw) * (b - 4), z: EYE + Math.sin(s * PI) * (F && F[3] ? .8 : 0), yaw: S.yaw, pitch: -.04, fov: 74 };\n192\t  }\n193\t  const busy = () => S.dur > 0 && S.t < S.dur;\n194\t  /** try to step one cell along way d (relative to nothing: 0..3 on the map); true when the party moves */\n195\t  function stepTo(d) {\n196\t    const x = S.cx + DX[d], y = S.cy + DY[d];\n197\t    if (!open(x, y) || foeAt(x, y)) { S.bump = .001; A.sfx('thud'); const g = gateAt(x, y); if (g && !g.up && !scripted) say(g.t.locked ? 'A GATE WITH AN IRON LOCK' : 'THE GATE WILL NOT BUDGE'); return false; }\n198\t    S.from = [S.x, S.y, S.yaw, 1]; S.cx = x; S.cy = y; S.t = 0; S.dur = STEP_T; A.sfx('step'); return true;\n199\t  }\n200\t  function turnBy(s) { S.from = [S.x, S.y, S.yaw, 0]; S.dir = (S.dir + s + 4) % 4; S.t = 0; S.dur = TURN_T; A.sfx('turn'); return true; }\n201\t  /** the party has come into its cell: plates, things to take, the stair */\n202\t  function arrive() {\n203\t    look(); const k = S.cx + ',' + S.cy, pl = plates[k];\n204\t    if (pl && !pl.t.on) {\n205\t      pl.t.on = true; A.sfx('plate');\n206\t      if (pl.trap) { A.sfx('dart'); say('DARTS FROM THE WALLS!'); for (const m of alive().filter(m => m.front)) hurtMember(m, 4 + ((rnd() * 4) | 0)); }\n207\t      else { raise(gates[pl.gate]); say('A GRINDING, FAR OFF', 2.6); }\n208\t    }\n209\t    for (const it of items.slice()) if (it.cx === S.cx && it.cy === S.cy) {\n210\t      world.remove(it.t); items.splice(items.indexOf(it), 1); took++; A.sfx('pickup');\n211\t      if (it.kind === 'key') { keys.add('iron'); say('THE IRON KEY'); } else { for (const m of alive()) heal(m, 15); say('A FLASK: EVERYONE FEELS BETTER'); }\n212\t    }\n213\t    if (stair && S.cx === stair.cx && S.cy === stair.cy) { if (stair.t.on) win(); else if (!scripted) say('THE STAIR IS SEALED: SOMETHING HOLDS IT'); }\n214\t  }\n215\t  function raise(g) { if (!g || g.up) return; g.up = true; g.t.locked = null; A.sfx('gate'); }\n216\t  /** J at what is in front: a lever on this wall, a locked gate; true when it used something */\n217\t  function use() {\n218\t    const fx = S.cx + DX[S.dir], fy = S.cy + DY[S.dir];\n219\t    const lv = levers.find(l => l.cx === S.cx && l.cy === S.cy && l.dir === S.dir);\n220\t    if (lv) { lv.t.on = !lv.t.on; A.sfx('lever'); if (lv.t.on) { raise(gates[lv.gate]); say('A LEVER: SOMEWHERE A GATE RISES'); } return true; }\n221\t    const g = gateAt(fx, fy);\n222\t    if (g && !g.up && g.t.locked) {\n223\t      const r = world.unlock(g.t, { has: k => keys.has(k), remove: k => keys.delete(k) });\n224\t      if (r === 'unlocked') { A.sfx('unlock'); raise(g); say('THE IRON KEY TURNS'); } else { A.sfx('locked'); say('LOCKED: IT WANTS AN IRON KEY'); }\n225\t      return true;\n226\t    }\n227\t    return false;\n228\t  }\n229\t\n230\t  /* ---- FIGHTING: the front rank's blows at what stands in front, the mage's bolt, the cleric's heal ---- */\n231\t  const roll = ([a, b]) => a + ((rnd() * (b - a + 1)) | 0);\n232\t  const ahead = () => foeAt(S.cx + DX[S.dir], S.cy + DY[S.dir]);\n233\t  /** member m acts by its role; false when it has nothing to do (no foe in reach, no one hurt, no magic) */\n234\t  function act(m) {\n235\t    if (!m || m.hp <= 0 || (mode === 'real' && m._turn < 100)) return false;\n236\t    if (m.o.heal) {\n237\t      const w = alive().filter(o => o.hp < o.max).sort((a, b) => a.hp / a.max - b.hp / b.max)[0];\n238\t      if (!w || m.mp < HEAL_MP) return false;\n239\t      m.mp -= HEAL_MP; heal(w, roll(m.o.heal)); A.sfx('heal'); m.flash = .3; say(m.name + ' HEALS ' + w.name, 1.6);\n240\t    } else if (m.o.bolt) {\n241\t      if (m.mp < BOLT_MP) return false;\n242\t      m.mp -= BOLT_MP; bolts.push({ cx: S.cx, cy: S.cy, d: S.dir, x: S.x, y: S.y, z: EYE - 5, t: 0, dmg: roll(m.o.bolt), by: m }); A.sfx('bolt');\n243\t    } else {\n244\t      const e = ahead(); slashT = .16; A.sfx('swing');\n245\t      if (e) hurtFoe(e, roll(m.o.hit), m);\n246\t    }\n247\t    m.cool = .3; if (mode === 'real') turns.done(m); return true;\n248\t  }\n249\t  /** the first foe down the line the party faces (6 cells, until a wall or a gate), or null: what a bolt would hit */\n250\t  function inLine() {\n251\t    for (let k = 1, x = S.cx, y = S.cy; k <= 6; k++) { x += DX[S.dir]; y += DY[S.dir]; const e = foeAt(x, y); if (e) return e; if (!open(x, y)) return null; }\n252\t    return null;\n253\t  }\n254\t  /** J in real time: the next one ready, the front rank first at what stands in front, the mage at what comes down the\n255\t   *  line; with nothing there, the front swings at the air */\n256\t  function anyAct() {\n257\t    const order = ahead() ? [0, 1, 3] : inLine() ? [3] : [0, 1];\n258\t    for (const i of order) if (act(party[i])) return true;\n259\t    return false;\n260\t  }\n261\t  /** J in turns: the party's round, each one that has something to do: blows at what is in front, a bolt down the line,\n262\t   *  the cleric's heal for one below two thirds */\n263\t  function round() {\n264\t    const foe = ahead(), line = inLine(); let n = 0;\n265\t    for (const m of party) if (m.hp > 0 && (m.o.hit ? foe : m.o.bolt ? line : alive().some(o => o.hp < o.max * .67)) && act(m)) n++;\n266\t    if (!n && party.some(m => m.hp > 0 && m.o.hit)) { slashT = .16; A.sfx('swing'); n = 1; }   // (nothing to do: a swing at the air is the round)\n267\t    return n > 0;\n268\t  }\n269\t  function heal(m, n) { if (m.hp <= 0) return; m.hp = Math.min(m.max, m.hp + n); m.flash = .4; }\n270\t  function hurtFoe(e, dmg, by) {\n271\t    e.hp -= dmg; e.flash = .15; if (!e.awake) wake(e);\n272\t    P.sparks(e.x, e.y, (e.z || 0) + 14, 6, Math.atan2(S.y - e.y, S.x - e.x)); P.text(e.x, e.y, (e.z || 0) + 30, dmg, '#fff2c4'); A.sfx('hit');\n273\t    if (e.hp <= 0) {\n274\t      e.alive = false; e.setSolid(false); turns.remove(e); A.sfx(e.type === 'warden' ? 'roar' : 'die');\n275\t      if (e.type === 'warden') { stair.t.on = true; say('THE WARDEN FALLS: THE STAIR IS OPEN', 3.2); song = null; }\n276\t    }\n277\t  }\n278\t  function hurtMember(m, dmg) {\n279\t    if (m.hp <= 0) return;\n280\t    m.hp = Math.max(0, m.hp - dmg); m.hurtT = .5; game.shake(2); A.sfx('hurt');\n281\t    if (m.hp <= 0) { say(m.name + ' FALLS', 2); turns.remove(m); }\n282\t  }\n283\t  /** a monster's blow lands: the front rank takes what comes from ahead or the sides, the back rank what comes from behind */\n284\t  function blow(e) {\n285\t    const rel = ((Math.round(Math.atan2(e.cy - S.cy, e.cx - S.cx) / (PI / 2)) + 1 - S.dir) % 4 + 4) % 4;   // 0 ahead, 2 behind\n286\t    let pool = alive().filter(m => m.front === (rel !== 2)); if (!pool.length) pool = alive(); if (!pool.length) return;\n287\t    const hits = e.type === 'warden' && e.blows % 3 === 2 ? pool : [pool[(rnd() * pool.length) | 0]];   // the Warden's sweep, every third blow\n288\t    for (const m of hits) hurtMember(m, roll(e.k.dmg));\n289\t    if (hits.length > 1) { game.shake(5); say('THE WARDEN SWEEPS THE FRONT', 1.6); }\n290\t    e.blows++;\n291\t  }\n292\t  /** a monster's turn: strike when beside the party, else close in by the grid's path (awake ones only) */\n293\t  function foeTurn(e) {\n294\t    if (e.hp <= 0 || !e.awake) return;\n295\t    const d = Math.abs(e.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(e.cy - S.cy);\n296\t    e.facing = Math.atan2(S.y - e.y, S.x - e.x);\n297\t    if (d === 1) {\n298\t      e.hitT = .3;\n299\t      if (e.k.move) { e.atk = new E.Attack(e.k.move); e.atk.start(); } else if (e.type === 'wisp') e.zap = .18; else { e.vx += Math.cos(e.facing) * 60; e.vy += Math.sin(e.facing) * 60; }\n300\t      return;\n301\t    }\n302\t    const path = grid.path([e.cx, e.cy], [S.cx, S.cy], { blocked: (x, y) => !!foeAt(x, y) && !(x === e.cx && y === e.cy), ends: true });\n303\t    if (path.length > 2) { const [nx, ny] = path[1]; if (!(nx === S.cx && ny === S.cy)) { e.cx = nx; e.cy = ny; e.tx = mid(nx); e.ty = mid(ny); e.moveT = MOVE_T; } }\n304\t  }\n305\t  /** each step: walk each monster to its cell's middle, its blow's timing, its death */\n306\t  function foeStep(e, dt) {\n307\t    if (e.hp <= 0) {\n308\t      e.deadT += dt; e.vx = approach(e.vx, 0, 300 * dt); e.vy = approach(e.vy, 0, 300 * dt);\n309\t      e.anim = e.rig ? { pose: 'die' } : e.blob ? { squash: -.45, squint: true } : null; if (e.type === 'wisp') { e.fade = Math.max(0, 1 - e.deadT * 1.5); e.vz = -10; }\n310\t      if (e.deadT > 1.2) e.sink += dt * 12;\n311\t      if (e.deadT > 2.6 && foes.includes(e)) { world.remove(e); e.gone = true; }\n312\t      return;\n313\t    }\n314\t    const sp = e.type === 'warden' ? 70 : 90, dx = e.tx - e.x, dy = e.ty - e.y;\n315\t    e.vx = clamp(dx * 9, -sp, sp); e.vy = clamp(dy * 9, -sp, sp);\n316\t    if (e.fly) e.vz = (e.k.z + Math.sin(world.time * 3 + e.cx) * 2 - e.z) * 5;\n317\t    if (Math.hypot(dx, dy) > 2) e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, Math.atan2(dy, dx), dt * 10);\n318\t    if (e.hitT > 0 && (e.hitT -= dt) <= 0 && Math.abs(e.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(e.cy - S.cy) === 1) blow(e);\n319\t    if (e.atk) { e.atk.update(dt); if (!e.atk.busy) e.atk = null; }\n320\t    e.zap = Math.max(0, e.zap - dt); e.moveT = Math.max(0, (e.moveT || 0) - dt);\n321\t    e.anim = e.rig ? { attack: e.atk && e.atk.state, hurt: e.flash > 0, expr: e.atk ? 'angry' : null } : e.blob ? { squash: e.hitT > 0 ? -.35 : Math.sin(world.time * 4 + e.cx) * .06, look: [Math.cos(e.facing), Math.sin(e.facing)] } : null;\n322\t  }\n323\t  /** the bolts: a cell every .07 s down the corridor, until a monster, a wall or a gate */\n324\t  function boltStep(dt) {\n325\t    for (let i = bolts.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n326\t      const b = bolts[i]; b.t += dt;\n327\t      const nx = mid(b.cx) + DX[b.d] * C * Math.min(1, b.t / .07), ny = mid(b.cy) + DY[b.d] * C * Math.min(1, b.t / .07);\n328\t      b.x = nx; b.y = ny;\n329\t      if (b.t < .07) continue;\n330\t      b.t = 0; b.cx += DX[b.d]; b.cy += DY[b.d];\n331\t      const e = foeAt(b.cx, b.cy), stop = !open(b.cx, b.cy) || Math.abs(b.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(b.cy - S.cy) > 7;\n332\t      if (e) hurtFoe(e, b.dmg, b.by);\n333\t      if (e || stop) { P.sparks(mid(b.cx) - DX[b.d] * 12, mid(b.cy) - DY[b.d] * 12, b.z, 10, null, { color: '#ffb14a' }); bolts.splice(i, 1); }\n334\t    }\n335\t  }\n336\t\n337\t  /* ---- A STEP OF THE GAME: the party's controls, the turns, the monsters ---- */\n338\t  function step(dt, ctl) {\n339\t    if (msg && (msg.t -= dt) <= 0) msg = null;\n340\t    slashT = Math.max(0, slashT - dt);\n341\t    for (const m of party) { m.hurtT = Math.max(0, m.hurtT - dt); m.flash = Math.max(0, m.flash - dt); m.rig.update(dt, { x: 0, y: 0, hurt: m.hurtT > 0, expr: m.hurtT > 0 ? 'wince' : null }); }\n342\t    for (const g of Object.values(gates)) { const was = g.t.open || 0; g.t.open = approach(was, g.up ? 1 : 0, dt * .9); if (g.up && g.t.open > .85 && g.t.body) world.setSolid(g.t, false); if ((was < .5) !== (g.t.open < .5)) look(); }\n343\t    if (mode !== (game.settings.crawlTurns || mode) && !scripted) { mode = game.settings.crawlTurns; makeTurns(); phase = 'party'; }\n344\t    const dead = !alive().length;\n345\t    // the party: a step or turn tweening, or the controls (in turns, only on the party's turn)\n346\t    if (busy()) { S.t += dt; place(Math.min(1, S.t / S.dur)); if (!busy()) { const stepped = S.from[3]; S.from = null; S.dur = 0; if (stepped) arrive(); } }\n347\t    else {\n348\t      if (S.bump > 0) { S.bump += dt * 6; if (S.bump >= 1) S.bump = 0; }\n349\t      place(1);\n350\t      if (!dead && !ended && (mode === 'real' || phase === 'party')) control(ctl);\n351\t    }\n352\t    boltStep(dt);\n353\t    // the monsters: real time, each by its gauge; turns, all of them once the party has had its turn and its move is done\n354\t    if (mode === 'real') {\n355\t      turns.update(dt);\n356\t      for (const a of turns.ready()) if (a.k) { turns.done(a); foeTurn(a); }\n357\t    } else if (phase === 'world' && !busy() && !bolts.length) {\n358\t      for (let guard = 0; guard < 40; guard++) { const a = turns.next(); if (!a || a === S) break; foeTurn(a); }\n359\t      phase = 'wait';\n360\t    } else if (phase === 'wait' && !foes.some(e => e.hp > 0 && (e.moveT > 0 || e.hitT > 0))) { phase = 'party'; rounds++; for (const m of alive()) if (m.mpMax) m.mp = Math.min(m.mpMax, m.mp + .5); }\n361\t    if (mode === 'real') for (const m of alive()) if (m.mpMax) m.mp = Math.min(m.mpMax, m.mp + dt / 4);\n362\t    for (const e of foes) foeStep(e, dt);\n363\t    for (let i = foes.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (foes[i].gone) foes.splice(i, 1);\n364\t    lamp.x = S.x; lamp.y = S.y; lamp.z = EYE + 4; lamp.on = true;\n365\t    if (dead && !ended) { ended = 2; if (!scripted) game.after(1.5, () => game.go('over', { from: 'crawler', world, lines: ['THE PARTY IS LOST', 'IN THE LANTERN VAULTS'] })); }\n366\t    world.step(dt);\n367\t  }\n368\t  /** the controls when the party may act: the stick or keys to step and turn, Q and E aside, J, K, H, 1 to 4 */\n369\t  function control(c) {\n370\t    const mv = c.move, turnsMode = mode === 'turns';\n371\t    let did = false;\n372\t    if (c.pressed('act')) { c.use('act'); did = use() || (turnsMode ? round() : anyAct()); }\n373\t    else if (c.pressed('spell')) { c.use('spell'); did = act(party[3]); }\n374\t    else if (c.pressed('heal')) { c.use('heal'); did = act(party[2]); }\n375\t    else for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) if (c.pressed('m' + (i + 1))) { c.use('m' + (i + 1)); did = act(party[i]); break; }\n376\t    if (did) { if (turnsMode) { phase = 'world'; for (const m of party) m._turn = 100; } return; }\n377\t    if (S.bump > 0) return;\n378\t    let moved = false;\n379\t    if (mv[1] < -.5) moved = stepTo(S.dir); else if (mv[1] > .5) moved = stepTo((S.dir + 2) % 4);\n380\t    else if (mv[0] < -.5) moved = turnBy(-1); else if (mv[0] > .5) moved = turnBy(1);\n381\t    else if (c.down('strafeL')) moved = stepTo((S.dir + 3) % 4); else if (c.down('strafeR')) moved = stepTo((S.dir + 1) % 4);\n382\t    if (moved && turnsMode) phase = 'world';\n383\t  }\n384\t  function win() {\n385\t    if (ended) return; ended = 1; if (scripted) return; A.music('victory');\n386\t    game.after(1.4, () => game.go('over', { from: 'crawler', world, won: true, title: 'OUT OF THE VAULTS', lines: ['THE WARDEN IS DOWN', alive().length + ' OF 4 CLIMB THE STAIR   ' + foes.filter(e => e.hp <= 0).length + ' FOES'] }));\n387\t  }\n388\t\n389\t  /* ---- THE HUD: the party's cards (portrait, life, magic, gauge), the compass, the map ---- */\n390\t  const card = (r, i) => {   // a card's box: one row of four on a wide screen, two by two on a narrow one; at the top on a touch screen (below the corner's buttons where they would cover it)\n391\t    const four = r.W >= 300, cw = four ? Math.min(92, Math.floor((r.W - 10) / 4)) : Math.floor((r.W - 8) / 2), ch = 38, n = four ? 4 : 2;\n392\t    const x0 = Math.round((r.W - (cw * n + 2 * (n - 1))) / 2), row = four ? 0 : i >> 1, col = four ? i : i & 1, top = touch();\n393\t    const ca = top && game.cornerArea(), y0 = ca && ca.x0 < x0 + n * (cw + 2) ? Math.ceil(ca.y1) + 3 : 4;\n394\t    return [x0 + col * (cw + 2), top ? y0 + row * (ch + 2) : r.H - (four ? 1 : 2) * (ch + 2) - 2 + row * (ch + 2), cw, ch];\n395\t  };\n396\t  const below = r => touch() ? card(r, 3)[1] + 42 : 4;   // where the compass and the little map go: under the cards on a touch screen\n397\t  function hud(g, r) {\n398\t    // a blow's streak across the view\n399\t    if (slashT > 0) { g.save(); g.globalAlpha = slashT / .16; g.strokeStyle = '#fff6e0'; g.lineWidth = 2; g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(r.W * .7, r.H * .28); g.lineTo(r.W * .3, r.H * .62); g.stroke(); g.restore(); }\n400\t    for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n401\t      const m = party[i], [x, y, w, h] = card(r, i), ko = m.hp <= 0, ready = mode === 'real' ? m._turn >= 100 : phase === 'party';\n402\t      E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg: m.hurtT > 0 ? '#5a1a1e' : m.flash > 0 ? '#1e4a2e' : '#1a1626', border: ready && !ko ? '#d8c890' : '#6a6080', alpha: .9 });\n403\t      m.rig.drawPortrait(g, x + 3, y + 3, 26, { zoom: 2.4, turn: .4, bg: '#2a2438', tint: ko ? '#707070' : undefined });\n404\t      E.font.text(g, (i + 1) + ' ' + m.name, x + 32, y + 3, ko ? '#8a8090' : '#f0e8d8', { font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n405\t      E.ui.bar(g, x + 32, y + 12, w - 36, 5, m.hp / m.max, '#e0463c');\n406\t      if (m.mpMax) E.ui.bar(g, x + 32, y + 19, w - 36, 4, m.mp / m.mpMax, '#4a8aff');\n407\t      if (mode === 'real' && !ko) E.ui.bar(g, x + 32, y + h - 9, w - 36, 3, Math.min(1, m._turn / 100), ready ? '#ffd36a' : '#8a7a4a');\n408\t      E.font.text(g, ko ? 'DOWN' : m.hp + '/' + m.max, x + 32, y + 26, ko ? '#c84a4a' : '#c8c0b0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n409\t    }\n410\t    // the compass, the mode, the message\n411\t    const cx = Math.round(r.W / 2), ty = below(r);\n412\t    E.ui.box(g, cx - 26, ty, 52, 14, { bg: '#1a1626', border: '#6a6080', alpha: .85 });\n413\t    E.font.text(g, WAYS[(S.dir + 3) % 4] + '   ' + WAYS[S.dir] + '   ' + WAYS[(S.dir + 1) % 4], cx, ty + 4, '#d8c890', { align: 'center', font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n414\t    E.font.text(g, mode === 'turns' ? (phase === 'party' ? 'YOUR TURN' : 'THEIR TURN') : 'REAL TIME', 4, ty + 4, mode === 'turns' && phase !== 'party' ? '#e8a060' : '#9a90b0', { font: 'tiny', outline: '#000' });\n415\t    if (msg) E.font.text(g, msg.text, cx, touch() ? r.H * .62 : card(r, 0)[1] - 12, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n416\t    automap(g, r, showMap);\n417\t  }\n418\t  /** the map from the fog: what the party has seen (walls beside it), gates, plates, the stair, the party's arrow */\n419\t  function automap(g, r, big) {\n420\t    const s = big ? Math.max(4, Math.min(10, Math.floor(Math.min(r.W - 20, r.H - 60) / MW))) : 3, w = MW * s, h = MH * s;\n421\t    const x0 = big ? Math.round((r.W - w) / 2) : r.W - w - 4, y0 = big ? Math.round((r.H - h) / 2) : below(r);\n422\t    E.ui.box(g, x0 - 2, y0 - 2, w + 4, h + 4, { bg: '#0c0a12', border: '#6a6080', alpha: big ? .95 : .75 });\n423\t    const seenNear = (x, y) => [0, 1, 2, 3].some(d => fog.seen([x + DX[d], y + DY[d]]) && !wallCell(x + DX[d], y + DY[d]));\n424\t    for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) {\n425\t      const wall = wallCell(x, y); if (wall ? !seenNear(x, y) : !fog.seen([x, y])) continue;\n426\t      const k = x + ',' + y, gt = gates[k], pl = plates[k];\n427\t      g.fillStyle = wall ? '#6a6080' : gt ? (gt.up ? '#4a4458' : '#c8a050') : pl ? (pl.trap && !pl.t.on ? '#3a3448' : '#8a7aa0') : stair && stair.cx === x && stair.cy === y ? '#9ae8ff' : fog.visible([x, y]) ? '#3a3448' : '#2a2436';\n428\t      g.fillRect(x0 + x * s, y0 + y * s, s, s);\n429\t      const f = foeAt(x, y); if (f && fog.visible([x, y])) { g.fillStyle = '#ff5a4a'; g.fillRect(x0 + x * s + (s >> 2), y0 + y * s + (s >> 2), Math.max(1, s >> 1), Math.max(1, s >> 1)); }\n430\t    }\n431\t    // the party: a dot and the way it faces\n432\t    const px = x0 + S.cx * s + s / 2, py = y0 + S.cy * s + s / 2;\n433\t    g.fillStyle = '#ffe08a'; g.fillRect(Math.round(px - 1), Math.round(py - 1), 2, 2); g.fillRect(Math.round(px + DX[S.dir] * s * .45 - .5), Math.round(py + DY[S.dir] * s * .45 - .5), 1, 1);\n434\t    if (big) E.font.text(g, 'THE LANTERN VAULTS   ' + (keys.has('iron') ? 'IRON KEY' : ''), r.W / 2, y0 - 12, '#d8c890', { align: 'center', font: 'tiny', outline: '#000' });\n435\t  }\n436\t\n437\t  /* ---- THE CONTROLS: keys, touch, and clicks on the cards and the map ---- */\n438\t  const KEYS = { up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n439\t    strafeL: ['KeyQ', 'Pad4'], strafeR: ['KeyE', 'Pad5'], act: ['KeyJ', 'Space', 'Pad0'], spell: ['KeyK', 'Pad2'], heal: ['KeyH', 'Pad3'], map: ['Tab', 'Pad8'],\n440\t    m1: ['Digit1'], m2: ['Digit2'], m3: ['Digit3'], m4: ['Digit4'],\n441\t    start: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'], confirm: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'Pad1'] };\n442\t  const TOUCH = ['map', 'heal', 'spell', 'act'], TOUCH_LABELS = { map: 'MAP', heal: 'HEAL', spell: 'BOLT', act: 'ACT' };\n443\t  const SETTING = { key: 'crawlTurns', label: 'Turns', group: 'Game', type: 'select', value: 'real', options: [['real', 'Real time'], ['turns', 'Turns']],\n444\t    help: 'Real time: each one acts when its gauge fills, and the monsters do not wait. Turns: the vaults wait for you; each step, turn or blow is a turn' };\n445\t  const ctl = { move: [0, 0], down: a => game.input.down(a), pressed: a => game.input.pressed(a), use: a => game.input.consume(a) };\n446\t  function controls() {\n447\t    const m = game.input.move(); ctl.move[0] = m[0]; ctl.move[1] = m[1];\n448\t    const tap = game.input.clicked();\n449\t    if (tap) {   // a portrait acts; the little map opens the big one; the view uses what is in front, or fights\n450\t      const r = game.r || { W: game.W, H: game.H }, i = [0, 1, 2, 3].find(k => { const [x, y, w, h] = card(r, k); return tap[0] >= x && tap[0] < x + w && tap[1] >= y && tap[1] < y + h; });\n451\t      if (i !== undefined) { if ((mode === 'real' || phase === 'party') && act(party[i]) && mode === 'turns') phase = 'world'; }\n452\t      else if (tap[0] > r.W - MW * 3 - 8 && tap[1] >= below(r) - 2 && tap[1] < below(r) + MH * 3 + 6) showMap = !showMap;\n453\t      else if (!touch()) { const t = { pressed: a => a === 'act', use() {}, down: () => false, move: [0, 0] }; if (mode === 'real' || phase === 'party') control(t); }\n454\t    }\n455\t    return ctl;\n456\t  }\n457\t\n458\t  /** the proof: a scripted walk from the start (forward, a quarter turn to the lever, pull it, round to the gate it raised,\n459\t   *  through it), in real time; n steps of 1/120 s. The world's hash with the party's cell and way, the gate's height and\n460\t   *  the party's lives: the same on WebGPU, WebGL 2 and run again */\n461\t  function run(n = 600) {\n462\t    reset(3, 'real'); scripted = true;\n463\t    const plan = ['up', 'left', 'up', 'up', 'act', 'right', 'up', 'right', 'up', 'up', 'left', 'up', 'up'], keys0 = new Set();\n464\t    const c = { move: [0, 0], down: a => keys0.has(a), pressed: a => keys0.has(a), use: a => keys0.delete(a) };\n465\t    let k = 0, wait = 0;\n466\t    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n467\t      keys0.clear(); c.move[0] = c.move[1] = 0;\n468\t      if (!busy() && S.bump === 0 && k < plan.length && (wait -= 1 / 120) <= 0) {\n469\t        const a = plan[k++];\n470\t        if (a === 'up') c.move[1] = -1; else if (a === 'left') c.move[0] = -1; else if (a === 'right') c.move[0] = 1; else keys0.add(a);\n471\t        if (a === 'act') wait = 1.4;   // (the gate takes a while to rise)\n472\t      }\n473\t      step(1 / 120, c);\n474\t    }\n475\t    scripted = false; const g = gates['10,9'];\n476\t    return world.hash([S.cx, S.cy, S.dir, g.t.open, levers[0].t.on ? 1 : 0, ...party.map(m => m.hp), k]);\n477\t  }\n478\t\n479\t  /** the bot: plays the vaults by the game's own rules (a stick and buttons each step, as a player gives them): the\n480\t   *  lever, the iron key in the slimes' hall, the locked gate, the plate, the Warden, the stair; it walks the grid's\n481\t   *  paths, turns to face what attacks, fights (the front's blows, the mage's bolts down a line), heals when hurt. Then\n482\t   *  the same start in TURNS: the vaults hold still while the party waits, and act once it steps.\n483\t   *  Returns { lever, key, unlocked, plate, warden, won, alive, killed, steps, errors, turns: { waited, acted } } */\n484\t  function bot(max = 120 * 60 * 10) {\n485\t    reset(5, 'real'); scripted = true;\n486\t    const keys0 = new Set(), c = { move: [0, 0], down: a => keys0.has(a), pressed: a => keys0.has(a), use: a => keys0.delete(a) };\n487\t    const GOALS = [['use', 8, 11, 3], ['go', 12, 1], ['use', 17, 8, 0], ['go', 17, 5], ['go', 17, 3], ['go', 17, 1]];\n488\t    let g = 0, steps = 0, errors = 0, waitT = 0;\n489\t    const r = { lever: false, key: false, unlocked: false, plate: false, warden: false, won: false };\n490\t    try {\n491\t      for (; steps < max && !ended && alive().length; steps++) {\n492\t        keys0.clear(); c.move[0] = c.move[1] = 0;\n493\t        r.lever = r.lever || levers[0].t.on; r.key = r.key || keys.has('iron') || gates['17,7'].up; r.unlocked = gates['17,7'].up; r.plate = plates['17,5'].t.on;\n494\t        if (busy() || S.bump > 0) { step(1 / 120, c); continue; }\n495\t        // a foe beside the party: face it and fight; heal whoever is low; bolt what stands in line ahead\n496\t        const near = foes.find(e => e.hp > 0 && Math.abs(e.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(e.cy - S.cy) === 1);\n497\t        const low = alive().some(m => m.hp < m.max * .45) && party[2].hp > 0 && party[2].mp >= HEAL_MP && party[2]._turn >= 100;\n498\t        if (low) keys0.add('heal');\n499\t        else if (near) {\n500\t          const want = [0, 1, 2, 3].find(d => S.cx + DX[d] === near.cx && S.cy + DY[d] === near.cy);\n501\t          if (want !== S.dir) c.move[0] = ((want - S.dir + 4) % 4) === 3 ? -1 : 1; else keys0.add('act');\n502\t        } else {\n503\t          const lineFoe = foes.find(e => e.hp > 0 && e.awake && fog.visible([e.cx, e.cy]) && ((e.cx === S.cx && Math.sign(e.cy - S.cy) === DY[S.dir] && DY[S.dir]) || (e.cy === S.cy && Math.sign(e.cx - S.cx) === DX[S.dir] && DX[S.dir])));\n504\t          if (lineFoe && party[3].hp > 0 && party[3].mp >= BOLT_MP && party[3]._turn >= 100) keys0.add('spell');\n505\t          else if (lineFoe && Math.abs(lineFoe.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(lineFoe.cy - S.cy) <= 3 && (waitT += 1 / 120) < 3) { /* wait for it to come (3 s at most) */ }\n506\t          else if (g < GOALS.length) {\n507\t            waitT = 0;\n508\t            const [kind, gx, gy, gd] = GOALS[g];\n509\t            if (S.cx === gx && S.cy === gy) {\n510\t              if (kind === 'use') { if (S.dir !== gd) c.move[0] = ((gd - S.dir + 4) % 4) === 3 ? -1 : 1; else { keys0.add('act'); g++; } }\n511\t              else g++;\n512\t            } else {\n513\t              const path = grid.path([S.cx, S.cy], [gx, gy], { blocked: (x, y) => !!foeAt(x, y) });\n514\t              if (path.length > 1) {\n515\t                const [nx, ny] = path[1], want = [0, 1, 2, 3].find(d => S.cx + DX[d] === nx && S.cy + DY[d] === ny);\n516\t                if (want === S.dir) c.move[1] = -1; else c.move[0] = ((want - S.dir + 4) % 4) === 3 ? -1 : 1;\n517\t              }\n518\t            }\n519\t          }\n520\t        }\n521\t        step(1 / 120, c);\n522\t        r.warden = r.warden || foes.every(e => e.type !== 'warden') || !!(stair && stair.t.on);\n523\t      }\n524\t    } catch (e) { errors++; console.error(e); }\n525\t    Object.assign(r, { won: ended === 1, alive: alive().length, killed: total - foes.filter(e => e.hp > 0).length, steps, errors, goal: g });\n526\t    // TURNS: the vaults hold still while the party waits (a second and a half), then a step: the wisps by the start's\n527\t    // hall act (none are awake there yet: the dead in the hall beyond the gate are not seen), so the count is of turns had\n528\t    reset(5, 'turns');\n529\t    try {\n530\t      const before = foes.map(e => [e.cx, e.cy, e._turn].join()).join('|');\n531\t      for (let i = 0; i < 180; i++) { keys0.clear(); c.move[0] = c.move[1] = 0; step(1 / 120, c); }\n532\t      const still = foes.map(e => [e.cx, e.cy, e._turn].join()).join('|') === before && phase === 'party';\n533\t      c.move[1] = -1; step(1 / 120, c); c.move[1] = 0; const t0 = S.cy;\n534\t      for (let i = 0; i < 120; i++) step(1 / 120, c);\n535\t      r.turns = { waited: still, stepped: t0 !== MAP.findIndex(row => row.includes('@')), back: phase === 'party', rounds, energy: foes.some(e => e._turn > 0) };\n536\t    } catch (e) { errors++; r.errors = errors; console.error(e); }\n537\t    scripted = false; ended = 0; return r;\n538\t  }\n539\t\n540\t  return {\n541\t    view: 'iso', input: KEYS, pausable: true, touch: TOUCH,\n542\t    enter(d) {\n543\t      game.settings.define(SETTING); reset(1); active = world; game.input.touchButtons(TOUCH, { labels: TOUCH_LABELS });\n544\t      if (d && d.part === 'warden') { for (const k of ['10,9', '17,7', '17,4']) { raise(gates[k]); gates[k].t.open = 1; world.setSolid(gates[k].t, false); } S.cx = 17; S.cy = 5; S.dir = 0; plates['17,5'].t.on = true; place(1); look(); }\n545\t      say(d && d.part === 'warden' ? 'THE WARDEN\\'S HALL' : 'THE LANTERN VAULTS. FIND THE WAY DOWN', 3.5);\n546\t    },\n547\t    update(dt) {\n548\t      if (game.input.pressed('map')) { game.input.consume('map'); showMap = !showMap; }\n549\t      step(dt, controls());\n550\t      const want = foes.some(e => e.type === 'warden' && e.awake && e.hp > 0) ? FIGHT : VAULT;\n551\t      if (want !== song && !ended) { song = want; A.music(want); }\n552\t    },\n553\t    draw(r) {\n554\t      world.draw(r);\n555\t      r.overlay(g => hud(g, r));\n556\t    },\n557\t    get world() { return world; }, get hero() { return hero; }, get party() { return party; }, get foes() { return foes; }, get state() { return S; }, get mode() { return mode; },\n558\t    get gates() { return gates; }, reset, run, bot, MAP\n559\t  };\n560\t})();\n561\tscenes.crawler = CRAWLER;\n562\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5572b217-8052-4a87-b3f3-49ea658fe605","uuid":"12e4b19c-8141-4592-97b2-e6239c08d05f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:53:59.622Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-185330/_ref/engine-src/src/starter3d/70-crawler.js","content":"/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 7  CRAWLER  (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder, King's Field). @modules grid\n * The Lantern Vaults in first person, a cell at a time: W and S (or up and down) step forward and back, A and D turn a\n * quarter turn, Q and E step aside, each one tweened. A party of four, their portraits under the view: two in front who\n * fight, two behind who cast. J (or a click on the view) uses what is in front (a lever, a locked gate) or has the next\n * one ready act: a blow at what stands in front, else the mage's bolt; K the mage's bolt down the corridor, H the\n * cleric's heal, 1 to 4 (or a click on a portrait) that one's own act; Tab the map (what the party has seen: E.Fog).\n * Gates that rise (one with an iron lock), a lever on a wall, plates in the floor (one raises a gate, one springs darts);\n * wisps, slimes, the dead of the vaults and the Warden at the bottom; the stair out behind it. Settings, Turns: REAL TIME\n * (each one's gauge fills on game time, E.Turns 'atb': Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder) or TURNS (the vaults wait:\n * each step, turn or blow is the party's turn, the monsters act by their speed, E.Turns 'speed': Wizardry).\n * THE 3D: the camera 'fixed' at the party's eyes, tweened per step; a level of 2 x 2 tiles a cell, braziers in niches,\n * a ceiling and the party's lantern; world.thing gates that rise, and a lever, plates and a stair drawn by the slice;\n * mobs walked cell to cell. Deep link: #crawler/warden (the Warden's hall, its gates open). CRAWLER.run(n): a scripted\n * walk's hash (the proof); CRAWLER.bot(): to the Warden and out\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst CRAWLER = (() => {\n  const C = 32, PI = Math.PI, EYE = 25, STEP_T = .28, TURN_T = .2, MOVE_T = .4;\n  // the four ways, a quarter turn apart: 0 north, 1 east, 2 south, 3 west\n  const DX = [0, 1, 0, -1], DY = [-1, 0, 1, 0], YAW = d => -PI / 2 + d * PI / 2, WAYS = ['N', 'E', 'S', 'W'];\n  /* ---- THE VAULTS: one character a cell (2 metres: 2 x 2 of the level's tiles). # wall, . floor, @ the start (facing\n   * north), n a wall with a brazier in a niche, L a wall with a lever, G a gate (raised by what is wired to it), K a gate\n   * with an iron lock, P a plate (raises a gate), T a plate that springs darts, X the stair out, i the iron key, h a\n   * flask, w wisps, s slimes, k the dead, W the Warden ---- */\n  const MAP = [\n    '#########n#n###n###n#',\n    '#######.....i.#..X..#',\n    '#######....k..#..W..#',\n    '#######.s.....#.....#',\n    '#.....#.....s.###G###',\n    'n.w.h.#.......#..P..n',\n    '#w....#.......#...k.#',\n    '###.######.######K###',\n    '###............T..###',\n    '######n###G##########',\n    '########.....########',\n    '#######L.....n#######',\n    '########..@..########',\n    '#####################'];\n  const MW = MAP[0].length, MH = MAP.length, at = (x, y) => (MAP[y] || '')[x] || '#';\n  const WALLS = '#nL', wallCell = (x, y) => WALLS.includes(at(x, y));\n  // what is wired to what: a lever's or a plate's cell -> the gate it raises\n  const WIRES = { '7,11': '10,9', '17,5': '17,4' };\n  // a wall cell's open side (a niche's brazier, a lever's face): the first way with floor beyond it\n  const openSide = (x, y) => [0, 1, 2, 3].find(d => !wallCell(x + DX[d], y + DY[d]));\n  // the level: each cell 2 x 2 tiles; a niche holds a brazier ('t') in the tile on its open side\n  const NICHE = [['t#', '##'], ['#t', '##'], ['##', 't#'], ['t#', '##']];\n  const rows = [];\n  for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let k = 0; k < 2; k++) {\n    let row = ''; for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) { const c = at(x, y); row += c === 'n' ? NICHE[openSide(x, y)][k] : wallCell(x, y) ? '##' : '..'; }\n    rows.push(row);\n  }\n  const LEVEL = { rows, ground: 'flagstone', colors: { base: '#4a4656', dark: '#34303e', light: '#5a5668' }, side: 'brick', color: '#4e4858', legend: {} };\n  const mid = c => c * C + C / 2;\n\n  /* ---- THE PARTY: two in front who fight, two behind who cast; each one's portrait is its rig's (drawPortrait) ---- */\n  const PARTY = [\n    { name: 'BRAM', role: 'FIGHTER', hp: 46, speed: 100, hit: [8, 13], rig: { build: 'heroic', hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#8a92a0' }, colors: { cloth: '#7a3a2e', pants: '#3a3440', hair: '#4a2e1e', skin: '#d8a888', metal: '#b8c0cc' } } },\n    { name: 'TESK', role: 'ROGUE', hp: 34, speed: 135, hit: [5, 10], rig: { hood: true, colors: { cloth: '#3a5a3e', pants: '#2e2a26', hair: '#2a3a2c', skin: '#c89070' } } },\n    { name: 'MAREN', role: 'CLERIC', hp: 30, mp: 16, speed: 90, heal: [12, 19], rig: { hair: 'long', hat: 'band', colors: { cloth: '#d8d0b8', pants: '#8a7a5a', hair: '#c8a050', skin: '#e8c0a0', hat: '#c8a040' } } },\n    { name: 'QUILL', role: 'MAGE', hp: 22, mp: 18, speed: 85, bolt: [11, 18], rig: { hat: 'pointed', weapon: null, colors: { cloth: '#3a3a7a', pants: '#2a2a4a', hair: '#e0e0e8', skin: '#e0b090', hat: '#3a3a7a' } } }];\n  const BOLT_MP = 4, HEAL_MP = 3;\n  /* ---- THE MONSTERS: hp, a blow's damage, speed (100: a turn as the party's), how far they see (cells) ---- */\n  const BONE = { bone: '#d8cfb4', cloth: '#2c2434', belt: '#5a4a38', metal: '#b3b8c0', metalDk: '#636872', hilt: '#6a5038' };\n  const WARDEN = { cloth: '#3a3a52', pants: '#2a2832', boot: '#1e1c24', belt: '#5a4a30', trim: '#9a8a5a', metal: '#7a8294', metalDk: '#3e4452', skin: '#8a9aa8', hair: '#1a1a22' };\n  const KINDS = {\n    wisp: { hp: 9, dmg: [2, 4], speed: 150, sight: 4, z: 16 },\n    slime: { hp: 20, dmg: [3, 6], speed: 70, sight: 3 },\n    skeleton: { hp: 28, dmg: [4, 8], speed: 100, sight: 5, move: 'slash' },\n    warden: { hp: 120, dmg: [6, 10], speed: 95, sight: 6, move: 'overhead', boss: true }\n  };\n  const MARK = { w: 'wisp', s: 'slime', k: 'skeleton', W: 'warden' };\n\n  /* ---- THINGS drawn by this slice (the engine's kinds are in its manual): a lever on a wall, a plate in the floor, the\n   * stair out (an arch over steps down, lit once the Warden falls) ---- */\n  W3.THINGS.wallLever = (p, t) => {   // its local +y points out of the wall\n    const a = t.on ? -1 : 1;\n    p.box(0, .8, 20, 6, 1.6, 9, '#4a4452').box(0, 1.8, 20, 2, .8, 5.5, '#24202a')\n      .tube(0, 2.2, 20, 0, 3.6, 20 + a * 5, .55, '#a8a8b8').ball(0, 3.8, 20 + a * 5.4, 1.1, 1.1, 1.1, t.on ? '#4ae070' : '#e8483a');\n  };\n  W3.THINGS.plate = (p, t) => { const s = t.on ? .2 : 1, c = t.color || '#6a6474'; p.box(0, 0, s / 2, 22, 22, s, c).box(0, 0, s + .05, 17, 17, .1, E.shade(c, -.2)); };\n  W3.THINGS.stair = (p, t) => {\n    const s = '#5a5468';\n    p.box(-13, 0, 19, 4, 5, 38, s).box(13, 0, 19, 4, 5, 38, s).box(0, 0, 39, 30, 6, 4, s);\n    for (let k = 0; k < 4; k++) p.box(0, -2 - k * 3, -1 - k * 2.5, 22, 3, 2, '#3a3644');   // the steps going down\n    if (t.on) p.glow(0, 0, 16, 5 + Math.sin((t.t || 0) * 3) * .8, '#9ae8ff').halo(0, 0, 16, 18, [.15, .3, .38]);\n    else p.box(0, 0, 18, 22, 1, 34, '#14121a');\n  };\n\n  /* ---- SOUNDS AND MUSIC (the step sequencer's format: original songs) ---- */\n  const SOUNDS = {\n    step: { wave: 'noise', freq: 320, to: 120, dur: .07, vol: .1, filter: 'lowpass' }, turn: { wave: 'noise', freq: 900, to: 500, dur: .06, vol: .05 },\n    thud: [{ wave: 'square', freq: 90, to: 50, dur: .1, vol: .2 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 300, dur: .06, vol: .12 }],\n    swing: { wave: 'noise', freq: 2600, to: 800, dur: .1, vol: .12 }, bolt: [{ wave: 'saw', freq: 220, to: 880, dur: .18, vol: .16 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 3000, to: 600, dur: .2, vol: .1 }],\n    lever: [{ wave: 'square', freq: 260, to: 140, dur: .08, vol: .2 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 1200, dur: .05, vol: .12, delay: .09 }],\n    gate: { wave: 'saw', freq: 70, to: 110, dur: .9, vol: .12, vib: [12, .1], filter: 'lowpass' }, plate: { wave: 'square', freq: 140, to: 90, dur: .1, vol: .2 },\n    dart: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 4000, to: 2000, dur: .05, vol: .2 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 4000, to: 2000, dur: .05, vol: .2, delay: .07 }],\n    locked: { wave: 'square', freq: 180, dur: .05, vol: .16 }, unlock: { wave: 'square', freq: 660, arp: [0, 7], step: .06, dur: .14, vol: .18 },\n    rattle: { wave: 'noise', freq: 2200, arp: [0, 3, 0, 5], step: .04, dur: .2, vol: .1 }, squelch: { wave: 'sine', freq: 140, to: 60, dur: .16, vol: .25 },\n    zap: { wave: 'square', freq: 1400, to: 300, dur: .1, vol: .1 }, roar: [{ wave: 'saw', freq: 110, to: 55, dur: 1, vol: .2, vib: [7, .12] }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 500, to: 120, dur: .8, vol: .15, filter: 'lowpass' }]\n  };\n  const VAULT = { bpm: 72, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the vaults: a slow figure over a drone, water dripping\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .26, notes: 'A1 - - - - - - - | A1 - - - - - - - | F1 - - - - - - - | E1 - - - - - - -' },\n    { wave: 'pulse25', vol: .05, notes: 'A3 . C4 . E4 . . . | D4 . C4 . B3 . . . | A3 . C4 . F4 . E4 . | E4 . . . G#3 . . .' },\n    { wave: 'sine', vol: .07, notes: '. . . . . . E5 . | . . . . . . . . | . . . . . . . A5 | . . . . . . . .' }] };\n  const FIGHT = { bpm: 128, steps: 4, tracks: [   // the Warden\n    { wave: 'saw', vol: .06, notes: 'A3 A3 . A3 C4 . A3 . | G3 G3 . G3 Bb3 . G3 . | F3 F3 . F3 A3 . F3 . | E3 . G#3 . B3 . E4 .' },\n    { wave: 'triangle', vol: .3, notes: 'A1 . A1 . A1 . A1 . | G1 . G1 . G1 . G1 . | F1 . F1 . F1 . F1 . | E1 . E1 . E1 . E1 .' },\n    { wave: 'drums', vol: .1, notes: 'k . h k s . h . | k k h . s . h h' }] };\n\n  /* ---- THE STATE ---- */\n  let world = null, hero = null, lamp = null, grid = null, fog = null, turns = null, rnd = Math.random, mode = 'real', scripted = false;\n  let party = null, S = null, foes = [], gates = {}, levers = [], plates = {}, items = [], stair = null, bolts = [], keys = null;\n  let total = 0, msg = null, showMap = false, song = null, ended = 0, slashT = 0, phase = 'party', took = 0, rounds = 0;\n  BOOT.push(['The vaults', () => {\n    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(SOUNDS)) A.define(k, v);\n    world = new W3(game, { level: LEVEL, torchLights: 4, torchShadows: 0, torchPower: 16, torchReach: 160, torchColor: '#ffb070', lights: 2,\n      ambient: ['#5a5478', '#221e2a', 3.4], fog: { color: '#050407', near: 40, far: 250 }, sky: '#050407', camera: { mode: 'fixed' },\n      onDraw: w => {   // the ceiling over the vaults, the bolts in flight, the wisps' zaps\n        w.pen.at().box(w.width / 2, w.depth / 2, 50, w.width, w.depth, 4, '#1c1a22');   // (at(): the pen's origin back at the world's)\n        for (const b of bolts) w.glow(b.x, b.y, b.z, 3.2, '#ffb14a', { light: true });\n        for (const e of foes) if (e.zap > 0) w.pen.at().bar(e.x, e.y, e.z + 2, S.x, S.y, EYE - 6, .6, .6, '#bff4ff');\n      } });\n  }]);\n\n  /** a fresh descent (seed: the dice; m: 'real' or 'turns', else the player's setting) */\n  function reset(seed = 1, m = null) {\n    world.reset(); rnd = E.rng(seed); mode = m || game.settings.crawlTurns || 'real';\n    const st = MAP.findIndex(r => r.includes('@')), sx = MAP[st].indexOf('@');\n    hero = world.hero({ x: mid(sx), y: mid(st), r: 4, visible: false }); world.camera.follow(hero);\n    S = { cx: sx, cy: st, dir: 0, x: mid(sx), y: mid(st), yaw: YAW(0), px: mid(sx), py: mid(st), pyaw: YAW(0), from: null, t: 0, dur: 0, bump: 0, act: 0 };\n    party = PARTY.map((o, i) => ({ i, name: o.name, role: o.role, front: i < 2, max: o.hp, hp: o.hp, mpMax: o.mp || 0, mp: o.mp || 0, speed: o.speed, o, hurtT: 0, flash: 0, rig: new E.Humanoid(Object.assign({ speedRef: 60 }, o.rig)), _turn: 100 }));\n    if (!lamp) lamp = world.light({ color: '#ffd8a0', reach: 190, power: 10 });\n    keys = new Set(); items = []; bolts = []; foes = []; gates = {}; levers = []; plates = {}; stair = null;\n    for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) {\n      const c = at(x, y), k = x + ',' + y;\n      if (c === 'G' || c === 'K') {   // a gate across its corridor (walls east and west: it spans x)\n        const ns = wallCell(x - 1, y) && wallCell(x + 1, y);\n        gates[k] = { cx: x, cy: y, up: false, t: world.thing('door', mid(x), mid(y), 0, { yaw: ns ? 0 : PI / 2, w: 32, h: 46, color: '#26242c', frame: '#3a3444', locked: c === 'K' ? 'iron' : null, solid: true }) };\n      } else if (c === 'L') {\n        const d = openSide(x, y), fx = x + DX[d], fy = y + DY[d];   // its face: toward the floor cell beside it\n        levers.push({ cx: fx, cy: fy, dir: (d + 2) % 4, gate: WIRES[k], t: world.thing('wallLever', mid(x) + DX[d] * C / 2, mid(y) + DY[d] * C / 2, 0, { yaw: Math.atan2(DY[d], DX[d]) - PI / 2 }) });\n      } else if (c === 'P' || c === 'T') plates[k] = { trap: c === 'T', gate: WIRES[k], t: world.thing('plate', mid(x), mid(y), 0, { color: c === 'T' ? '#625c6a' : '#6e6878' }) };\n      else if (c === 'X') stair = { cx: x, cy: y, t: world.thing('stair', mid(x), mid(y) - 6, 0, { on: false }) };\n      else if (c === 'i') items.push({ cx: x, cy: y, kind: 'key', t: world.thing('key', mid(x), mid(y), 5, { color: '#8a8c98', spin: .3, bob: 1.5 }) });\n      else if (c === 'h') items.push({ cx: x, cy: y, kind: 'flask', t: world.thing('potion', mid(x), mid(y), 0, { color: '#e04a4a', spin: .2 }) });\n      else if (MARK[c]) foes.push(spawn(MARK[c], x, y));\n    }\n    total = foes.length;\n    grid = new E.Grid(MW, MH, { walkable: (x, y) => open(x, y), opaque: (x, y) => wallCell(x, y) || !!(gates[x + ',' + y] && gates[x + ',' + y].t.open < .5) });\n    fog = new E.Fog(grid); look();\n    makeTurns(); msg = null; showMap = false; song = null; ended = 0; slashT = 0; phase = 'party'; took = 0; rounds = 0;\n    world.camera.set('fixed'); place(0);\n  }\n  function spawn(type, x, y) {\n    const k = KINDS[type], X = mid(x), Y = mid(y);\n    const e = type === 'wisp' ? world.mob({ x: X, y: Y, z: k.z, r: 4, half: 0, fly: true, orb: { color: '#8ae0ff', r: 3.6 } })\n      : type === 'slime' ? world.mob({ x: X, y: Y, r: 6, half: 0, mass: 2, blob: new E.Blob({ R: 7, face: 'front', colors: { base: '#5ac86a', dk: '#2e7a3e', lt: '#a8f0a0' } }) })\n      : world.mob({ x: X, y: Y, r: type === 'warden' ? 8 : 4.5, half: type === 'warden' ? 12 : 8, mass: type === 'warden' ? 8 : 1.4,\n        rig: type === 'warden' ? new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.45, build: 'bulky', armor: true, sleeves: 'long', bladeLen: 13, hat: { style: 'helmet', color: '#5a5e6e' }, eyeGlow: '#7ad8ff', colors: WARDEN, speedRef: 45 })\n          : new E.Humanoid({ build: 'skeleton', bladeLen: 9, colors: BONE, speedRef: 40 }) });\n    return Object.assign(e, { type, k, cx: x, cy: y, hp: k.hp, max: k.hp, speed: k.speed, awake: false, atk: null, hitT: 0, zap: 0, tx: X, ty: Y, deadT: 0, blows: 0, _turn: 0, facing: PI / 2 });\n  }\n  /** the turns: real time, each one's gauge on game time ('atb'); turns, the party one actor among the monsters ('speed') */\n  function makeTurns() {\n    const live = foes.filter(e => e.hp > 0);\n    turns = mode === 'turns' ? new E.Turns([S, ...live], { mode: 'speed' }) : new E.Turns([...party.filter(m => m.hp > 0), ...live], { mode: 'atb', fill: .55 });\n    S.speed = 100; for (const m of party) m._turn = mode === 'turns' ? 100 : Math.min(m._turn, 100);\n  }\n  const say = (text, t = 2.4) => { msg = { text, t }; };\n  const gateAt = (x, y) => gates[x + ',' + y];\n  const foeAt = (x, y) => foes.find(e => e.hp > 0 && e.cx === x && e.cy === y);\n  /** can a body stand in this cell (a wall, a gate down: no) */\n  function open(x, y) { if (wallCell(x, y)) return false; const g = gateAt(x, y); return !g || (g.up && g.t.open > .85); }\n  const alive = () => party.filter(m => m.hp > 0);\n  /** the party sees: the fog's field of view, and the monsters it falls on wake */\n  function look() {\n    fog.update([{ cx: S.cx, cy: S.cy, r: 5 }]);\n    for (const e of foes) if (e.hp > 0 && !e.awake && fog.visible([e.cx, e.cy]) && Math.abs(e.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(e.cy - S.cy) <= e.k.sight) wake(e);\n  }\n  function wake(e) { e.awake = true; A.sfx(e.type === 'slime' ? 'squelch' : e.type === 'wisp' ? 'zap' : e.type === 'warden' ? 'roar' : 'rattle'); if (e.type === 'warden') say('THE WARDEN WAKES', 3); }\n\n  /* ---- MOVING: a step or a turn, tweened; bumping a wall ---- */\n  function place(u) {   // where the eyes are this step (u: the tween's 0..1)\n    const s = u * u * (3 - 2 * u), F = S.from;\n    S.px = S.x; S.py = S.y; S.pyaw = S.yaw;\n    if (F) { S.x = lerp(F[0], mid(S.cx), s); S.y = lerp(F[1], mid(S.cy), s); S.yaw = F[2] + E.angDiff(F[2], YAW(S.dir)) * s; }\n    else { S.x = mid(S.cx); S.y = mid(S.cy); S.yaw = YAW(S.dir); }\n    const b = Math.sin(Math.min(1, S.bump) * PI) * 4;   // a bump into a wall: a lurch forward and back\n    hero.place(S.x + Math.cos(S.yaw) * b, S.y + Math.sin(S.yaw) * b, 0);\n    world.camera.fixed = { x: S.x + Math.cos(S.yaw) * (b - 4), y: S.y + Math.sin(S.yaw) * (b - 4), z: EYE + Math.sin(s * PI) * (F && F[3] ? .8 : 0), yaw: S.yaw, pitch: -.04, fov: 74 };\n  }\n  const busy = () => S.dur > 0 && S.t < S.dur;\n  /** try to step one cell along way d (relative to nothing: 0..3 on the map); true when the party moves */\n  function stepTo(d) {\n    const x = S.cx + DX[d], y = S.cy + DY[d];\n    if (!open(x, y) || foeAt(x, y)) { S.bump = .001; A.sfx('thud'); const g = gateAt(x, y); if (g && !g.up && !scripted) say(g.t.locked ? 'A GATE WITH AN IRON LOCK' : 'THE GATE WILL NOT BUDGE'); return false; }\n    S.from = [S.x, S.y, S.yaw, 1]; S.cx = x; S.cy = y; S.t = 0; S.dur = STEP_T; A.sfx('step'); return true;\n  }\n  function turnBy(s) { S.from = [S.x, S.y, S.yaw, 0]; S.dir = (S.dir + s + 4) % 4; S.t = 0; S.dur = TURN_T; A.sfx('turn'); return true; }\n  /** the party has come into its cell: plates, things to take, the stair */\n  function arrive() {\n    look(); const k = S.cx + ',' + S.cy, pl = plates[k];\n    if (pl && !pl.t.on) {\n      pl.t.on = true; A.sfx('plate');\n      if (pl.trap) { A.sfx('dart'); say('DARTS FROM THE WALLS!'); for (const m of alive().filter(m => m.front)) hurtMember(m, 4 + ((rnd() * 4) | 0)); }\n      else { raise(gates[pl.gate]); say('A GRINDING, FAR OFF', 2.6); }\n    }\n    for (const it of items.slice()) if (it.cx === S.cx && it.cy === S.cy) {\n      world.remove(it.t); items.splice(items.indexOf(it), 1); took++; A.sfx('pickup');\n      if (it.kind === 'key') { keys.add('iron'); say('THE IRON KEY'); } else { for (const m of alive()) heal(m, 15); say('A FLASK: EVERYONE FEELS BETTER'); }\n    }\n    if (stair && S.cx === stair.cx && S.cy === stair.cy) { if (stair.t.on) win(); else if (!scripted) say('THE STAIR IS SEALED: SOMETHING HOLDS IT'); }\n  }\n  function raise(g) { if (!g || g.up) return; g.up = true; g.t.locked = null; A.sfx('gate'); }\n  /** J at what is in front: a lever on this wall, a locked gate; true when it used something */\n  function use() {\n    const fx = S.cx + DX[S.dir], fy = S.cy + DY[S.dir];\n    const lv = levers.find(l => l.cx === S.cx && l.cy === S.cy && l.dir === S.dir);\n    if (lv) { lv.t.on = !lv.t.on; A.sfx('lever'); if (lv.t.on) { raise(gates[lv.gate]); say('A LEVER: SOMEWHERE A GATE RISES'); } return true; }\n    const g = gateAt(fx, fy);\n    if (g && !g.up && g.t.locked) {\n      const r = world.unlock(g.t, { has: k => keys.has(k), remove: k => keys.delete(k) });\n      if (r === 'unlocked') { A.sfx('unlock'); raise(g); say('THE IRON KEY TURNS'); } else { A.sfx('locked'); say('LOCKED: IT WANTS AN IRON KEY'); }\n      return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n  }\n\n  /* ---- FIGHTING: the front rank's blows at what stands in front, the mage's bolt, the cleric's heal ---- */\n  const roll = ([a, b]) => a + ((rnd() * (b - a + 1)) | 0);\n  const ahead = () => foeAt(S.cx + DX[S.dir], S.cy + DY[S.dir]);\n  /** member m acts by its role; false when it has nothing to do (no foe in reach, no one hurt, no magic) */\n  function act(m) {\n    if (!m || m.hp <= 0 || (mode === 'real' && m._turn < 100)) return false;\n    if (m.o.heal) {\n      const w = alive().filter(o => o.hp < o.max).sort((a, b) => a.hp / a.max - b.hp / b.max)[0];\n      if (!w || m.mp < HEAL_MP) return false;\n      m.mp -= HEAL_MP; heal(w, roll(m.o.heal)); A.sfx('heal'); m.flash = .3; say(m.name + ' HEALS ' + w.name, 1.6);\n    } else if (m.o.bolt) {\n      if (m.mp < BOLT_MP) return false;\n      m.mp -= BOLT_MP; bolts.push({ cx: S.cx, cy: S.cy, d: S.dir, x: S.x, y: S.y, z: EYE - 5, t: 0, dmg: roll(m.o.bolt), by: m }); A.sfx('bolt');\n    } else {\n      const e = ahead(); slashT = .16; A.sfx('swing');\n      if (e) hurtFoe(e, roll(m.o.hit), m);\n    }\n    m.cool = .3; if (mode === 'real') turns.done(m); return true;\n  }\n  /** the first foe down the line the party faces (6 cells, until a wall or a gate), or null: what a bolt would hit */\n  function inLine() {\n    for (let k = 1, x = S.cx, y = S.cy; k <= 6; k++) { x += DX[S.dir]; y += DY[S.dir]; const e = foeAt(x, y); if (e) return e; if (!open(x, y)) return null; }\n    return null;\n  }\n  /** J in real time: the next one ready, the front rank first at what stands in front, the mage at what comes down the\n   *  line; with nothing there, the front swings at the air */\n  function anyAct() {\n    const order = ahead() ? [0, 1, 3] : inLine() ? [3] : [0, 1];\n    for (const i of order) if (act(party[i])) return true;\n    return false;\n  }\n  /** J in turns: the party's round, each one that has something to do: blows at what is in front, a bolt down the line,\n   *  the cleric's heal for one below two thirds */\n  function round() {\n    const foe = ahead(), line = inLine(); let n = 0;\n    for (const m of party) if (m.hp > 0 && (m.o.hit ? foe : m.o.bolt ? line : alive().some(o => o.hp < o.max * .67)) && act(m)) n++;\n    if (!n && party.some(m => m.hp > 0 && m.o.hit)) { slashT = .16; A.sfx('swing'); n = 1; }   // (nothing to do: a swing at the air is the round)\n    return n > 0;\n  }\n  function heal(m, n) { if (m.hp <= 0) return; m.hp = Math.min(m.max, m.hp + n); m.flash = .4; }\n  function hurtFoe(e, dmg, by) {\n    e.hp -= dmg; e.flash = .15; if (!e.awake) wake(e);\n    P.sparks(e.x, e.y, (e.z || 0) + 14, 6, Math.atan2(S.y - e.y, S.x - e.x)); P.text(e.x, e.y, (e.z || 0) + 30, dmg, '#fff2c4'); A.sfx('hit');\n    if (e.hp <= 0) {\n      e.alive = false; e.setSolid(false); turns.remove(e); A.sfx(e.type === 'warden' ? 'roar' : 'die');\n      if (e.type === 'warden') { stair.t.on = true; say('THE WARDEN FALLS: THE STAIR IS OPEN', 3.2); song = null; }\n    }\n  }\n  function hurtMember(m, dmg) {\n    if (m.hp <= 0) return;\n    m.hp = Math.max(0, m.hp - dmg); m.hurtT = .5; game.shake(2); A.sfx('hurt');\n    if (m.hp <= 0) { say(m.name + ' FALLS', 2); turns.remove(m); }\n  }\n  /** a monster's blow lands: the front rank takes what comes from ahead or the sides, the back rank what comes from behind */\n  function blow(e) {\n    const rel = ((Math.round(Math.atan2(e.cy - S.cy, e.cx - S.cx) / (PI / 2)) + 1 - S.dir) % 4 + 4) % 4;   // 0 ahead, 2 behind\n    let pool = alive().filter(m => m.front === (rel !== 2)); if (!pool.length) pool = alive(); if (!pool.length) return;\n    const hits = e.type === 'warden' && e.blows % 3 === 2 ? pool : [pool[(rnd() * pool.length) | 0]];   // the Warden's sweep, every third blow\n    for (const m of hits) hurtMember(m, roll(e.k.dmg));\n    if (hits.length > 1) { game.shake(5); say('THE WARDEN SWEEPS THE FRONT', 1.6); }\n    e.blows++;\n  }\n  /** a monster's turn: strike when beside the party, else close in by the grid's path (awake ones only) */\n  function foeTurn(e) {\n    if (e.hp <= 0 || !e.awake) return;\n    const d = Math.abs(e.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(e.cy - S.cy);\n    e.facing = Math.atan2(S.y - e.y, S.x - e.x);\n    if (d === 1) {\n      e.hitT = .3;\n      if (e.k.move) { e.atk = new E.Attack(e.k.move); e.atk.start(); } else if (e.type === 'wisp') e.zap = .18; else { e.vx += Math.cos(e.facing) * 60; e.vy += Math.sin(e.facing) * 60; }\n      return;\n    }\n    const path = grid.path([e.cx, e.cy], [S.cx, S.cy], { blocked: (x, y) => !!foeAt(x, y) && !(x === e.cx && y === e.cy), ends: true });\n    if (path.length > 2) { const [nx, ny] = path[1]; if (!(nx === S.cx && ny === S.cy)) { e.cx = nx; e.cy = ny; e.tx = mid(nx); e.ty = mid(ny); e.moveT = MOVE_T; } }\n  }\n  /** each step: walk each monster to its cell's middle, its blow's timing, its death */\n  function foeStep(e, dt) {\n    if (e.hp <= 0) {\n      e.deadT += dt; e.vx = approach(e.vx, 0, 300 * dt); e.vy = approach(e.vy, 0, 300 * dt);\n      e.anim = e.rig ? { pose: 'die' } : e.blob ? { squash: -.45, squint: true } : null; if (e.type === 'wisp') { e.fade = Math.max(0, 1 - e.deadT * 1.5); e.vz = -10; }\n      if (e.deadT > 1.2) e.sink += dt * 12;\n      if (e.deadT > 2.6 && foes.includes(e)) { world.remove(e); e.gone = true; }\n      return;\n    }\n    const sp = e.type === 'warden' ? 70 : 90, dx = e.tx - e.x, dy = e.ty - e.y;\n    e.vx = clamp(dx * 9, -sp, sp); e.vy = clamp(dy * 9, -sp, sp);\n    if (e.fly) e.vz = (e.k.z + Math.sin(world.time * 3 + e.cx) * 2 - e.z) * 5;\n    if (Math.hypot(dx, dy) > 2) e.facing = E.approachAng(e.facing, Math.atan2(dy, dx), dt * 10);\n    if (e.hitT > 0 && (e.hitT -= dt) <= 0 && Math.abs(e.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(e.cy - S.cy) === 1) blow(e);\n    if (e.atk) { e.atk.update(dt); if (!e.atk.busy) e.atk = null; }\n    e.zap = Math.max(0, e.zap - dt); e.moveT = Math.max(0, (e.moveT || 0) - dt);\n    e.anim = e.rig ? { attack: e.atk && e.atk.state, hurt: e.flash > 0, expr: e.atk ? 'angry' : null } : e.blob ? { squash: e.hitT > 0 ? -.35 : Math.sin(world.time * 4 + e.cx) * .06, look: [Math.cos(e.facing), Math.sin(e.facing)] } : null;\n  }\n  /** the bolts: a cell every .07 s down the corridor, until a monster, a wall or a gate */\n  function boltStep(dt) {\n    for (let i = bolts.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n      const b = bolts[i]; b.t += dt;\n      const nx = mid(b.cx) + DX[b.d] * C * Math.min(1, b.t / .07), ny = mid(b.cy) + DY[b.d] * C * Math.min(1, b.t / .07);\n      b.x = nx; b.y = ny;\n      if (b.t < .07) continue;\n      b.t = 0; b.cx += DX[b.d]; b.cy += DY[b.d];\n      const e = foeAt(b.cx, b.cy), stop = !open(b.cx, b.cy) || Math.abs(b.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(b.cy - S.cy) > 7;\n      if (e) hurtFoe(e, b.dmg, b.by);\n      if (e || stop) { P.sparks(mid(b.cx) - DX[b.d] * 12, mid(b.cy) - DY[b.d] * 12, b.z, 10, null, { color: '#ffb14a' }); bolts.splice(i, 1); }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /* ---- A STEP OF THE GAME: the party's controls, the turns, the monsters ---- */\n  function step(dt, ctl) {\n    if (msg && (msg.t -= dt) <= 0) msg = null;\n    slashT = Math.max(0, slashT - dt);\n    for (const m of party) { m.hurtT = Math.max(0, m.hurtT - dt); m.flash = Math.max(0, m.flash - dt); m.rig.update(dt, { x: 0, y: 0, hurt: m.hurtT > 0, expr: m.hurtT > 0 ? 'wince' : null }); }\n    for (const g of Object.values(gates)) { const was = g.t.open || 0; g.t.open = approach(was, g.up ? 1 : 0, dt * .9); if (g.up && g.t.open > .85 && g.t.body) world.setSolid(g.t, false); if ((was < .5) !== (g.t.open < .5)) look(); }\n    if (mode !== (game.settings.crawlTurns || mode) && !scripted) { mode = game.settings.crawlTurns; makeTurns(); phase = 'party'; }\n    const dead = !alive().length;\n    // the party: a step or turn tweening, or the controls (in turns, only on the party's turn)\n    if (busy()) { S.t += dt; place(Math.min(1, S.t / S.dur)); if (!busy()) { const stepped = S.from[3]; S.from = null; S.dur = 0; if (stepped) arrive(); } }\n    else {\n      if (S.bump > 0) { S.bump += dt * 6; if (S.bump >= 1) S.bump = 0; }\n      place(1);\n      if (!dead && !ended && (mode === 'real' || phase === 'party')) control(ctl);\n    }\n    boltStep(dt);\n    // the monsters: real time, each by its gauge; turns, all of them once the party has had its turn and its move is done\n    if (mode === 'real') {\n      turns.update(dt);\n      for (const a of turns.ready()) if (a.k) { turns.done(a); foeTurn(a); }\n    } else if (phase === 'world' && !busy() && !bolts.length) {\n      for (let guard = 0; guard < 40; guard++) { const a = turns.next(); if (!a || a === S) break; foeTurn(a); }\n      phase = 'wait';\n    } else if (phase === 'wait' && !foes.some(e => e.hp > 0 && (e.moveT > 0 || e.hitT > 0))) { phase = 'party'; rounds++; for (const m of alive()) if (m.mpMax) m.mp = Math.min(m.mpMax, m.mp + .5); }\n    if (mode === 'real') for (const m of alive()) if (m.mpMax) m.mp = Math.min(m.mpMax, m.mp + dt / 4);\n    for (const e of foes) foeStep(e, dt);\n    for (let i = foes.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (foes[i].gone) foes.splice(i, 1);\n    lamp.x = S.x; lamp.y = S.y; lamp.z = EYE + 4; lamp.on = true;\n    if (dead && !ended) { ended = 2; if (!scripted) game.after(1.5, () => game.go('over', { from: 'crawler', world, lines: ['THE PARTY IS LOST', 'IN THE LANTERN VAULTS'] })); }\n    world.step(dt);\n  }\n  /** the controls when the party may act: the stick or keys to step and turn, Q and E aside, J, K, H, 1 to 4 */\n  function control(c) {\n    const mv = c.move, turnsMode = mode === 'turns';\n    let did = false;\n    if (c.pressed('act')) { c.use('act'); did = use() || (turnsMode ? round() : anyAct()); }\n    else if (c.pressed('spell')) { c.use('spell'); did = act(party[3]); }\n    else if (c.pressed('heal')) { c.use('heal'); did = act(party[2]); }\n    else for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) if (c.pressed('m' + (i + 1))) { c.use('m' + (i + 1)); did = act(party[i]); break; }\n    if (did) { if (turnsMode) { phase = 'world'; for (const m of party) m._turn = 100; } return; }\n    if (S.bump > 0) return;\n    let moved = false;\n    if (mv[1] < -.5) moved = stepTo(S.dir); else if (mv[1] > .5) moved = stepTo((S.dir + 2) % 4);\n    else if (mv[0] < -.5) moved = turnBy(-1); else if (mv[0] > .5) moved = turnBy(1);\n    else if (c.down('strafeL')) moved = stepTo((S.dir + 3) % 4); else if (c.down('strafeR')) moved = stepTo((S.dir + 1) % 4);\n    if (moved && turnsMode) phase = 'world';\n  }\n  function win() {\n    if (ended) return; ended = 1; if (scripted) return; A.music('victory');\n    game.after(1.4, () => game.go('over', { from: 'crawler', world, won: true, title: 'OUT OF THE VAULTS', lines: ['THE WARDEN IS DOWN', alive().length + ' OF 4 CLIMB THE STAIR   ' + foes.filter(e => e.hp <= 0).length + ' FOES'] }));\n  }\n\n  /* ---- THE HUD: the party's cards (portrait, life, magic, gauge), the compass, the map ---- */\n  const card = (r, i) => {   // a card's box: one row of four on a wide screen, two by two on a narrow one; at the top on a touch screen (below the corner's buttons where they would cover it)\n    const four = r.W >= 300, cw = four ? Math.min(92, Math.floor((r.W - 10) / 4)) : Math.floor((r.W - 8) / 2), ch = 38, n = four ? 4 : 2;\n    const x0 = Math.round((r.W - (cw * n + 2 * (n - 1))) / 2), row = four ? 0 : i >> 1, col = four ? i : i & 1, top = touch();\n    const ca = top && game.cornerArea(), y0 = ca && ca.x0 < x0 + n * (cw + 2) ? Math.ceil(ca.y1) + 3 : 4;\n    return [x0 + col * (cw + 2), top ? y0 + row * (ch + 2) : r.H - (four ? 1 : 2) * (ch + 2) - 2 + row * (ch + 2), cw, ch];\n  };\n  const below = r => touch() ? card(r, 3)[1] + 42 : 4;   // where the compass and the little map go: under the cards on a touch screen\n  function hud(g, r) {\n    // a blow's streak across the view\n    if (slashT > 0) { g.save(); g.globalAlpha = slashT / .16; g.strokeStyle = '#fff6e0'; g.lineWidth = 2; g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(r.W * .7, r.H * .28); g.lineTo(r.W * .3, r.H * .62); g.stroke(); g.restore(); }\n    for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n      const m = party[i], [x, y, w, h] = card(r, i), ko = m.hp <= 0, ready = mode === 'real' ? m._turn >= 100 : phase === 'party';\n      E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg: m.hurtT > 0 ? '#5a1a1e' : m.flash > 0 ? '#1e4a2e' : '#1a1626', border: ready && !ko ? '#d8c890' : '#6a6080', alpha: .9 });\n      m.rig.drawPortrait(g, x + 3, y + 3, 26, { zoom: 2.4, turn: .4, bg: '#2a2438', tint: ko ? '#707070' : undefined });\n      E.font.text(g, (i + 1) + ' ' + m.name, x + 32, y + 3, ko ? '#8a8090' : '#f0e8d8', { font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n      E.ui.bar(g, x + 32, y + 12, w - 36, 5, m.hp / m.max, '#e0463c');\n      if (m.mpMax) E.ui.bar(g, x + 32, y + 19, w - 36, 4, m.mp / m.mpMax, '#4a8aff');\n      if (mode === 'real' && !ko) E.ui.bar(g, x + 32, y + h - 9, w - 36, 3, Math.min(1, m._turn / 100), ready ? '#ffd36a' : '#8a7a4a');\n      E.font.text(g, ko ? 'DOWN' : m.hp + '/' + m.max, x + 32, y + 26, ko ? '#c84a4a' : '#c8c0b0', { font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n    }\n    // the compass, the mode, the message\n    const cx = Math.round(r.W / 2), ty = below(r);\n    E.ui.box(g, cx - 26, ty, 52, 14, { bg: '#1a1626', border: '#6a6080', alpha: .85 });\n    E.font.text(g, WAYS[(S.dir + 3) % 4] + '   ' + WAYS[S.dir] + '   ' + WAYS[(S.dir + 1) % 4], cx, ty + 4, '#d8c890', { align: 'center', font: 'tiny', outline: false });\n    E.font.text(g, mode === 'turns' ? (phase === 'party' ? 'YOUR TURN' : 'THEIR TURN') : 'REAL TIME', 4, ty + 4, mode === 'turns' && phase !== 'party' ? '#e8a060' : '#9a90b0', { font: 'tiny', outline: '#000' });\n    if (msg) E.font.text(g, msg.text, cx, touch() ? r.H * .62 : card(r, 0)[1] - 12, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    automap(g, r, showMap);\n  }\n  /** the map from the fog: what the party has seen (walls beside it), gates, plates, the stair, the party's arrow */\n  function automap(g, r, big) {\n    const s = big ? Math.max(4, Math.min(10, Math.floor(Math.min(r.W - 20, r.H - 60) / MW))) : 3, w = MW * s, h = MH * s;\n    const x0 = big ? Math.round((r.W - w) / 2) : r.W - w - 4, y0 = big ? Math.round((r.H - h) / 2) : below(r);\n    E.ui.box(g, x0 - 2, y0 - 2, w + 4, h + 4, { bg: '#0c0a12', border: '#6a6080', alpha: big ? .95 : .75 });\n    const seenNear = (x, y) => [0, 1, 2, 3].some(d => fog.seen([x + DX[d], y + DY[d]]) && !wallCell(x + DX[d], y + DY[d]));\n    for (let y = 0; y < MH; y++) for (let x = 0; x < MW; x++) {\n      const wall = wallCell(x, y); if (wall ? !seenNear(x, y) : !fog.seen([x, y])) continue;\n      const k = x + ',' + y, gt = gates[k], pl = plates[k];\n      g.fillStyle = wall ? '#6a6080' : gt ? (gt.up ? '#4a4458' : '#c8a050') : pl ? (pl.trap && !pl.t.on ? '#3a3448' : '#8a7aa0') : stair && stair.cx === x && stair.cy === y ? '#9ae8ff' : fog.visible([x, y]) ? '#3a3448' : '#2a2436';\n      g.fillRect(x0 + x * s, y0 + y * s, s, s);\n      const f = foeAt(x, y); if (f && fog.visible([x, y])) { g.fillStyle = '#ff5a4a'; g.fillRect(x0 + x * s + (s >> 2), y0 + y * s + (s >> 2), Math.max(1, s >> 1), Math.max(1, s >> 1)); }\n    }\n    // the party: a dot and the way it faces\n    const px = x0 + S.cx * s + s / 2, py = y0 + S.cy * s + s / 2;\n    g.fillStyle = '#ffe08a'; g.fillRect(Math.round(px - 1), Math.round(py - 1), 2, 2); g.fillRect(Math.round(px + DX[S.dir] * s * .45 - .5), Math.round(py + DY[S.dir] * s * .45 - .5), 1, 1);\n    if (big) E.font.text(g, 'THE LANTERN VAULTS   ' + (keys.has('iron') ? 'IRON KEY' : ''), r.W / 2, y0 - 12, '#d8c890', { align: 'center', font: 'tiny', outline: '#000' });\n  }\n\n  /* ---- THE CONTROLS: keys, touch, and clicks on the cards and the map ---- */\n  const KEYS = { up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n    strafeL: ['KeyQ', 'Pad4'], strafeR: ['KeyE', 'Pad5'], act: ['KeyJ', 'Space', 'Pad0'], spell: ['KeyK', 'Pad2'], heal: ['KeyH', 'Pad3'], map: ['Tab', 'Pad8'],\n    m1: ['Digit1'], m2: ['Digit2'], m3: ['Digit3'], m4: ['Digit4'],\n    start: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'], confirm: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'Pad1'] };\n  const TOUCH = ['map', 'heal', 'spell', 'act'], TOUCH_LABELS = { map: 'MAP', heal: 'HEAL', spell: 'BOLT', act: 'ACT' };\n  const SETTING = { key: 'crawlTurns', label: 'Turns', group: 'Game', type: 'select', value: 'real', options: [['real', 'Real time'], ['turns', 'Turns']],\n    help: 'Real time: each one acts when its gauge fills, and the monsters do not wait. Turns: the vaults wait for you; each step, turn or blow is a turn' };\n  const ctl = { move: [0, 0], down: a => game.input.down(a), pressed: a => game.input.pressed(a), use: a => game.input.consume(a) };\n  function controls() {\n    const m = game.input.move(); ctl.move[0] = m[0]; ctl.move[1] = m[1];\n    const tap = game.input.clicked();\n    if (tap) {   // a portrait acts; the little map opens the big one; the view uses what is in front, or fights\n      const r = game.r || { W: game.W, H: game.H }, i = [0, 1, 2, 3].find(k => { const [x, y, w, h] = card(r, k); return tap[0] >= x && tap[0] < x + w && tap[1] >= y && tap[1] < y + h; });\n      if (i !== undefined) { if ((mode === 'real' || phase === 'party') && act(party[i]) && mode === 'turns') phase = 'world'; }\n      else if (tap[0] > r.W - MW * 3 - 8 && tap[1] >= below(r) - 2 && tap[1] < below(r) + MH * 3 + 6) showMap = !showMap;\n      else if (!touch()) { const t = { pressed: a => a === 'act', use() {}, down: () => false, move: [0, 0] }; if (mode === 'real' || phase === 'party') control(t); }\n    }\n    return ctl;\n  }\n\n  /** the proof: a scripted walk from the start (forward, a quarter turn to the lever, pull it, round to the gate it raised,\n   *  through it), in real time; n steps of 1/120 s. The world's hash with the party's cell and way, the gate's height and\n   *  the party's lives: the same on WebGPU, WebGL 2 and run again */\n  function run(n = 600) {\n    reset(3, 'real'); scripted = true;\n    const plan = ['up', 'left', 'up', 'up', 'act', 'right', 'up', 'right', 'up', 'up', 'left', 'up', 'up'], keys0 = new Set();\n    const c = { move: [0, 0], down: a => keys0.has(a), pressed: a => keys0.has(a), use: a => keys0.delete(a) };\n    let k = 0, wait = 0;\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      keys0.clear(); c.move[0] = c.move[1] = 0;\n      if (!busy() && S.bump === 0 && k < plan.length && (wait -= 1 / 120) <= 0) {\n        const a = plan[k++];\n        if (a === 'up') c.move[1] = -1; else if (a === 'left') c.move[0] = -1; else if (a === 'right') c.move[0] = 1; else keys0.add(a);\n        if (a === 'act') wait = 1.4;   // (the gate takes a while to rise)\n      }\n      step(1 / 120, c);\n    }\n    scripted = false; const g = gates['10,9'];\n    return world.hash([S.cx, S.cy, S.dir, g.t.open, levers[0].t.on ? 1 : 0, ...party.map(m => m.hp), k]);\n  }\n\n  /** the bot: plays the vaults by the game's own rules (a stick and buttons each step, as a player gives them): the\n   *  lever, the iron key in the slimes' hall, the locked gate, the plate, the Warden, the stair; it walks the grid's\n   *  paths, turns to face what attacks, fights (the front's blows, the mage's bolts down a line), heals when hurt. Then\n   *  the same start in TURNS: the vaults hold still while the party waits, and act once it steps.\n   *  Returns { lever, key, unlocked, plate, warden, won, alive, killed, steps, errors, turns: { waited, acted } } */\n  function bot(max = 120 * 60 * 10) {\n    reset(5, 'real'); scripted = true;\n    const keys0 = new Set(), c = { move: [0, 0], down: a => keys0.has(a), pressed: a => keys0.has(a), use: a => keys0.delete(a) };\n    const GOALS = [['use', 8, 11, 3], ['go', 12, 1], ['use', 17, 8, 0], ['go', 17, 5], ['go', 17, 3], ['go', 17, 1]];\n    let g = 0, steps = 0, errors = 0, waitT = 0;\n    const r = { lever: false, key: false, unlocked: false, plate: false, warden: false, won: false };\n    try {\n      for (; steps < max && !ended && alive().length; steps++) {\n        keys0.clear(); c.move[0] = c.move[1] = 0;\n        r.lever = r.lever || levers[0].t.on; r.key = r.key || keys.has('iron') || gates['17,7'].up; r.unlocked = gates['17,7'].up; r.plate = plates['17,5'].t.on;\n        if (busy() || S.bump > 0) { step(1 / 120, c); continue; }\n        // a foe beside the party: face it and fight; heal whoever is low; bolt what stands in line ahead\n        const near = foes.find(e => e.hp > 0 && Math.abs(e.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(e.cy - S.cy) === 1);\n        const low = alive().some(m => m.hp < m.max * .45) && party[2].hp > 0 && party[2].mp >= HEAL_MP && party[2]._turn >= 100;\n        if (low) keys0.add('heal');\n        else if (near) {\n          const want = [0, 1, 2, 3].find(d => S.cx + DX[d] === near.cx && S.cy + DY[d] === near.cy);\n          if (want !== S.dir) c.move[0] = ((want - S.dir + 4) % 4) === 3 ? -1 : 1; else keys0.add('act');\n        } else {\n          const lineFoe = foes.find(e => e.hp > 0 && e.awake && fog.visible([e.cx, e.cy]) && ((e.cx === S.cx && Math.sign(e.cy - S.cy) === DY[S.dir] && DY[S.dir]) || (e.cy === S.cy && Math.sign(e.cx - S.cx) === DX[S.dir] && DX[S.dir])));\n          if (lineFoe && party[3].hp > 0 && party[3].mp >= BOLT_MP && party[3]._turn >= 100) keys0.add('spell');\n          else if (lineFoe && Math.abs(lineFoe.cx - S.cx) + Math.abs(lineFoe.cy - S.cy) <= 3 && (waitT += 1 / 120) < 3) { /* wait for it to come (3 s at most) */ }\n          else if (g < GOALS.length) {\n            waitT = 0;\n            const [kind, gx, gy, gd] = GOALS[g];\n            if (S.cx === gx && S.cy === gy) {\n              if (kind === 'use') { if (S.dir !== gd) c.move[0] = ((gd - S.dir + 4) % 4) === 3 ? -1 : 1; else { keys0.add('act'); g++; } }\n              else g++;\n            } else {\n              const path = grid.path([S.cx, S.cy], [gx, gy], { blocked: (x, y) => !!foeAt(x, y) });\n              if (path.length > 1) {\n                const [nx, ny] = path[1], want = [0, 1, 2, 3].find(d => S.cx + DX[d] === nx && S.cy + DY[d] === ny);\n                if (want === S.dir) c.move[1] = -1; else c.move[0] = ((want - S.dir + 4) % 4) === 3 ? -1 : 1;\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n        step(1 / 120, c);\n        r.warden = r.warden || foes.every(e => e.type !== 'warden') || !!(stair && stair.t.on);\n      }\n    } catch (e) { errors++; console.error(e); }\n    Object.assign(r, { won: ended === 1, alive: alive().length, killed: total - foes.filter(e => e.hp > 0).length, steps, errors, goal: g });\n    // TURNS: the vaults hold still while the party waits (a second and a half), then a step: the wisps by the start's\n    // hall act (none are awake there yet: the dead in the hall beyond the gate are not seen), so the count is of turns had\n    reset(5, 'turns');\n    try {\n      const before = foes.map(e => [e.cx, e.cy, e._turn].join()).join('|');\n      for (let i = 0; i < 180; i++) { keys0.clear(); c.move[0] = c.move[1] = 0; step(1 / 120, c); }\n      const still = foes.map(e => [e.cx, e.cy, e._turn].join()).join('|') === before && phase === 'party';\n      c.move[1] = -1; step(1 / 120, c); c.move[1] = 0; const t0 = S.cy;\n      for (let i = 0; i < 120; i++) step(1 / 120, c);\n      r.turns = { waited: still, stepped: t0 !== MAP.findIndex(row => row.includes('@')), back: phase === 'party', rounds, energy: foes.some(e => e._turn > 0) };\n    } catch (e) { errors++; r.errors = errors; console.error(e); }\n    scripted = false; ended = 0; return r;\n  }\n\n  return {\n    view: 'iso', input: KEYS, pausable: true, touch: TOUCH,\n    enter(d) {\n      game.settings.define(SETTING); reset(1); active = world; game.input.touchButtons(TOUCH, { labels: TOUCH_LABELS });\n      if (d && d.part === 'warden') { for (const k of ['10,9', '17,7', '17,4']) { raise(gates[k]); gates[k].t.open = 1; world.setSolid(gates[k].t, false); } S.cx = 17; S.cy = 5; S.dir = 0; plates['17,5'].t.on = true; place(1); look(); }\n      say(d && d.part === 'warden' ? 'THE WARDEN\\'S HALL' : 'THE LANTERN VAULTS. FIND THE WAY DOWN', 3.5);\n    },\n    update(dt) {\n      if (game.input.pressed('map')) { game.input.consume('map'); showMap = !showMap; }\n      step(dt, controls());\n      const want = foes.some(e => e.type === 'warden' && e.awake && e.hp > 0) ? FIGHT : VAULT;\n      if (want !== song && !ended) { song = want; A.music(want); }\n    },\n    draw(r) {\n      world.draw(r);\n      r.overlay(g => hud(g, r));\n    },\n    get world() { return world; }, get hero() { return hero; }, get party() { return party; }, get foes() { return foes; }, get state() { return S; }, get mode() { return mode; },\n    get gates() { return gates; }, reset, run, bot, MAP\n  };\n})();\nscenes.crawler = CRAWLER;\n","numLines":562,"startLine":1,"totalLines":562}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NB9DWymqiesoVHuxe6kETj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
