{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ASjKHGq7KVR7rXXbTUN2K2","type":"tool_result","content":"791:     *  padLost: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses) */\n935:   * pausable scene into it (without the corner a START button there starts a title and pauses, as a gamepad's Start)\n1249:   touch START button, to start and pause in any layout: like Start, it starts on a title and pauses a pausable scene */\n2288:   * - autoPause: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\n2353:    /** paused: true while paused (a pausable scene toggles it on 'pause'; steps still run, scenes don't update);\n2491:  /** a pausable scene in play pauses when the page is hidden, the window loses focus or the controller is unplugged\n2493:  _autoPause(reason) { this.input.stopRumble(); return this.o.autoPause !== false && !!this.scene && !!this.scene.pausable && this.pause(reason); }\n2495:   * open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without\n2501:    const sh = this.shell, s = this.scene, play = !!s && (!!s.pausable || this.sceneName === 'main');\n2544:  _canBack() { const s = this.scene; return !!(this.shell && this.shell.screen) || !!s && (!!s.pausable || this.sceneName === 'main' || !!s.back); }\n2553:    if (!s || !(s.pausable || this.sceneName === 'main')) return false;\n2571:    const main = !!s && (!!s.pausable || this.sceneName === 'main'), play = main && !this.paused, near = performance.now() - (this._mouseTop || -1e9) < 2500;\n2660:   * A scene is { enter(data), exit(), update(dt), draw(r), back(), pausable, view, views, input, res, expand, touch, camera }\n2858:    if (s.pausable || name === 'main') this._fsAuto = this._autoFull();   // a game starting from a tap goes full screen again\n2883:    if (s && s.pausable && this.input.pressed('pause')) { this.paused = !this.paused; this.pauseReason = this.paused ? 'player' : null; this.audio.sfx('pause'); }\n2967: *    - pausing: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus, or the controller in use is unplugged,\n3757:    if (game.scene && game.scene.pausable && q.pressed('pause')) { game.paused = !game.paused; game.pauseReason = game.paused ? 'player' : null; game.pausedBy = q.player; game.audio.sfx('pause'); q.consumeAll(); }\n3910:HOOKS.step.push((game, dt) => { const s = game._saves, sc = game.scene; if (s && sc && (sc.pausable || game.sceneName === 'main')) s.played += dt; });   // time played: the game's scenes, not its titles\n9551:    const g = this._game, I = g.input, now = g.real, sc = g.scene, play = !!sc && (!!sc.pausable || g.sceneName === 'main');\n1250:const MENU_KEYS = {\nconst MENU_KEYS = {\n  start: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'],\n  confirm: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'KeyJ', 'KeyZ', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'KeyX', 'KeyK', 'Pad1']","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5572b217-8052-4a87-b3f3-49ea658fe605","uuid":"24e767e0-0dca-431e-8954-d9c6d79f606d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:20:04.340Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"791:     *  padLost: true for the step after the gamepad in use was unplugged (a pausable scene pauses) */\n935:   * pausable scene into it (without the corner a START button there starts a title and pauses, as a gamepad's Start)\n1249:   touch START button, to start and pause in any layout: like Start, it starts on a title and pauses a pausable scene */\n2288:   * - autoPause: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\n2353:    /** paused: true while paused (a pausable scene toggles it on 'pause'; steps still run, scenes don't update);\n2491:  /** a pausable scene in play pauses when the page is hidden, the window loses focus or the controller is unplugged\n2493:  _autoPause(reason) { this.input.stopRumble(); return this.o.autoPause !== false && !!this.scene && !!this.scene.pausable && this.pause(reason); }\n2495:   * open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without\n2501:    const sh = this.shell, s = this.scene, play = !!s && (!!s.pausable || this.sceneName === 'main');\n2544:  _canBack() { const s = this.scene; return !!(this.shell && this.shell.screen) || !!s && (!!s.pausable || this.sceneName === 'main' || !!s.back); }\n2553:    if (!s || !(s.pausable || this.sceneName === 'main')) return false;\n2571:    const main = !!s && (!!s.pausable || this.sceneName === 'main'), play = main && !this.paused, near = performance.now() - (this._mouseTop || -1e9) < 2500;\n2660:   * A scene is { enter(data), exit(), update(dt), draw(r), back(), pausable, view, views, input, res, expand, touch, camera }\n2858:    if (s.pausable || name === 'main') this._fsAuto = this._autoFull();   // a game starting from a tap goes full screen again\n2883:    if (s && s.pausable && this.input.pressed('pause')) { this.paused = !this.paused; this.pauseReason = this.paused ? 'player' : null; this.audio.sfx('pause'); }\n2967: *    - pausing: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus, or the controller in use is unplugged,\n3757:    if (game.scene && game.scene.pausable && q.pressed('pause')) { game.paused = !game.paused; game.pauseReason = game.paused ? 'player' : null; game.pausedBy = q.player; game.audio.sfx('pause'); q.consumeAll(); }\n3910:HOOKS.step.push((game, dt) => { const s = game._saves, sc = game.scene; if (s && sc && (sc.pausable || game.sceneName === 'main')) s.played += dt; });   // time played: the game's scenes, not its titles\n9551:    const g = this._game, I = g.input, now = g.real, sc = g.scene, play = !!sc && (!!sc.pausable || g.sceneName === 'main');\n1250:const MENU_KEYS = {\nconst MENU_KEYS = {\n  start: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'],\n  confirm: ['Enter', 'NumpadEnter', 'Space', 'KeyJ', 'KeyZ', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'KeyX', 'KeyK', 'Pad1']","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185013__xe162c9/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1069,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1069,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"972ca841-0540-4c71-85fe-204eae6bea61\",\"uuid\":\"e5fbe867-a2e4-46e5-8372-96eac57a1b9f\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":299,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":249,\"session_id\":\"972ca841-0540-4c71-85fe-204eae6bea61\",\"uuid\":\"1984fdcb-f871-45f3-840a-f3bf17ea33f5\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh64W3eg17kdrv7WoZVD\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7557,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":395831,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":7557},\"output_tokens\":6,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"972ca841-0540-4c71-85fe-204eae6bea61\",\"uuid\":\"1ed9b0dc-f2f2-4621-8d69-dec5db706926\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:20:03.430Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh64VkJ6UkfoK5P6fZ7X\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":1072,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh64W3eg17kdrv7WoZVD\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The harness runs several copies of a game in iframes, which is what I need to test two or more players locally. I'll write the networking module now: the host runs the battle from the seeded stage, clients send their inputs and draw from snapshots, and the host reports the result.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7557,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":395831,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":7557},\"output_tokens\":6,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"972ca841-0540-4c71-85fe-204eae6bea61\",\"uuid\":\"fed9d9c4-90ef-4614-b42f-336745404552\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:20:03.898Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh64VkJ6UkfoK5P6fZ7X\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183420__xf7f297/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":853,"oldLines":3,"newStart":853,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":550,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea\",\"uuid\":\"ab2e02d3-dcca-433d-8b52-22769d304b9c\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":700,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea\",\"uuid\":\"abe8890b-6dd5-40b0-b8b7-476c2d3e9a5b\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":800,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea\",\"uuid\":\"ae7eed48-23eb-468a-ab83-23ce648fa39f\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":900,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea\",\"uuid\":\"4b43ce2b-3782-41bb-9ff0-46d404b2d3a7\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/ho