42f0-ba91-458cd0dea4c5\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:36:42.571Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"1629293 Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-183420.html\\n6270 exit-interview.json\\nno TODO/placeholder in src\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01FZsrLwBcYTcGBYDCtriD29\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh7LNuLyBNUZXEXFsRCc\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I built **Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins** from PLAN.md. It's one HTML file in this folder, `Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-183420.html`, and it plays from `file://` with nothing else needed. `node tests/run.mjs` passes all 150 checks. That includes the browser checks of the bundle and the real AI Hub harness in three runs: 2 players; 4 players with 150 ms latency, jitter and 5% packet loss; and the host leaving.\\n\\n**What's in it:**\\n- **Story:** an opening crawl, a training mission and three story missions, each with a boss: Brother Ittetsu, Gonroku, Hotaru and Kurogane (who has a second phase).\\n- **Characters:** two playable ninja with different stats, combos and Silent Cut moves (Sojiro and Kaede).\\n- **Stealth:**\\n  - Light, shadow and noise decide detection, and the camera hides guards your ninja can't see (Shadow Sight).\\n  - A Ki gauge shows how near and how alert guards are.\\n  - Silent Cuts come in five kinds: back, side, front, from above, and from the water.\\n  - You also have a grappling hook, swimming and diving, wall-hugging with peeks, and body dragging and hiding.\\n- **Guards:** six guard types plus civilians and disguised ninja. Guards eat baits, find bodies, run to alarm bells and call reinforcements.\\n- **Tools and ranks:** 10 tools packed into an 8-compartment bento. Mission ranks unlock new tools, and the game autosaves.\\n- **Mission 2 and 3 extras:** an escort mission, and a moon timer in Mission 3.\\n- **Combat:** blocking, parrying, ripostes and dodge rolls.\\n- **Other modes:**\\n  - A mission editor (the Workshop) that edits the same level format the story uses.\\n  - Dev Mode from the pause menu, with live balance sliders and a reset.\\n  - Attract mode: seven demo scenes that start after 10 seconds idle.\\n  - The Shadow Trial, where you race your own best run's ghost.\\n  - AI Hub ghost-mode multiplayer for 1–4 players.\\n- **Controls and screens:** PlayStation button icons by default, with an Xbox option. A \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" notice on touch-only devices. An About screen with the four sections below.\\n\\n**What testing caught and I fixed:**\\n- Guards counted the hero's visibility twice, so they barely noticed anyone.\\n- Diving was impossible.\\n- Guards got stuck on solid props, which broke baits and some patrols.\\n- The attack-from-above check could never fire from a roof edge.\\n\\n**Things to know:**\\n- **Usage is unknown.** I couldn't measure tokens or cost.\\n- **Not tested in a real browser with a real gamepad.** Gamepad play was only checked through simulated input.\\n- **GPU lighting is off.** The plan wanted it when WebGPU is available; I left it off to keep the look consistent with the screenshots I checked.\\n- **Two tests are lighter than the plan's.** The full story isn't run in one go: each mission and the menu/ending flow are tested separately. The bosses are beaten by an automated player with invincibility on.\\n- **Disk space.** The machine's temp space is nearly full (about 4 MB free); keep that in mind for other runs.\\n- **Dev folder.** The source, tests and engine patches are in `Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-183420/`; its README lists the commands.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:34:20\\n- **Source:** Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins (Acquire / Activision, PlayStation, 2000)\\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Third-person ninja stealth-action with melee combat and boss duels. Isometric third person, rotatable in 45° steps and zoomable, with a high three-quarter camera option.\\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine with nine small patches (listed in `engine/PATCHES.md`), AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript in one HTML file. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 with Chromium.\\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1-era pixel art (320×240, expanded to fill the screen). Detailed character models with new masks, hats and weapons, canvas lighting, and Japanese props and materials written as shape data.\\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural character animation and paired actions. New: Silent Cut moves (5 kinds × 2 characters), grapple, riposte, ninja run, wall hug, swimming, eating, and a four-legged hound.\\n- **Audio:** The engine's chip synth. Layered Japanese-scale music (koto, shamisen, shakuhachi, fue, taiko), sound effects made in code, and a gibberish voice synth for every spoken line.\\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1–4 players, with the game's own pre-round card. Offline, the Shadow Trial against your own best ghost.\\n- **Testing:** Headless suites that drive the game in fixed steps behind one command (prints only failures and a one-line count). Missions completed through their real objectives, with an automated player fighting the bosses. Playwright checks of the bundle and the real AI Hub harness.\\n- **Research:** The engine's handoff docs and the AI Hub README; the planner's research (Wikipedia on Tenchu 2) carried in PLAN.md.\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** unknown\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 9, all fixed:\\n   - Guards counted the hero's visibility twice, so they barely noticed anyone.\\n   - The attack-from-above check could never fire from a roof edge.\\n   - Diving was impossible: the engine's movement code undid the crouch toggle.\\n   - Guards and bait-eaters got stuck on solid props.\\n   - A held button didn't reset the 10-second attract-mode timer.\\n   - Test teleports left the camera behind during slow motion.\\n   - The rest were test-setup mistakes: rice bales in a path, a hound that smelled the tester, and Python buffering the local server's port number.\\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 3: no diving, guards stuck on props, and the double-counted visibility.\\n3. **Most helpful test:** The missions suite. It completes all four missions through their real objectives and found the stuck-on-props bug.\\n4. **Least helpful test:** The headless smoke test with wandering input. It passed at once because headless runs skip all drawing.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n1. **What I liked most:** How much already works headless: parkour movement, sight/suspicion/hearing, paired actions, a standard pause/settings/rebinding interface, fixed-step tests, and character models that look good with little code.\\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes, a few times:\\n   - The movement code treats crouch as a held state, not a toggle.\\n   - Pathfinding ignores solid props.\\n   - The sight check already multiplies in the target's visibility, so I counted it twice.\\n   - A scripted one-step button press can be lost during hit-stop.\\n   - A custom input map has to restate the menu keys.\\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** The stealth layer: Shadow Sight and the Ki gauge, light maps baked with line of sight, the guard behaviour (baits, bodies, bells), Silent Cuts, the bosses, and the mission runtime with checkpoints.\\n4. **Hardest part:** Knowing how existing systems behave in a 1.2 MB engine. The docs give the names, but details like what a movement field means or which systems respect props are only in the source.\\n5. **What I changed:** Nine small patches:\\n   - PlayStation button symbols in the pixel font.\\n   - PlayStation/Xbox button-symbol setting.\\n   - Character gear: masks, two hat styles, spear, bow, club, offhand blade, back banner.\\n   - Settings sliders on custom menu screens.\\n   - Mouse hover moves menu focus.\\n   - TV-distance interface scaling.\\n   - Plucked-string music notes.\\n   - A volume channel for voices.\\n   - The hub's Create + Options guard on pause.\\n6. **One thing I'd change:** Make pathfinding respect solid props.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n1. **What I liked most:** It's concrete about the player: a TV at 10 feet, button icons, attract mode, touch-only handling, dev sliders and the hub. With the detailed plan, little was left to guess.\\n2. **What was confusing:** The plan's file names and suffix were written for a different run (max effort, different timestamp), so its names had to be swapped for mine. Also, how to weigh \\\"every feature\\\" when the plan is far larger than one session.\\n3. **Hardest thing:** The scope. A full stealth game with four bosses, an escort, an editor, attract mode, multiplayer and dev mode, all tested and with no stubs.\\n4. **What I'd change:** Mark which plan items are must-haves and which are stretch goals, give a session budget, and mention the temp-disk limit in TASK.md itself.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":698,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":630074,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":698},\"output_tokens\":796,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea\",\"uuid\":\"8cef33b8-308d-4439-bbc3-3ef92b2fc100\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:37:10.524Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh7LNMbz8ws78zEP4Nsz\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-185330/tests/dbg.mjs","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":7,"lines":["+import vm from 'node:vm'; import { readFileSync, readdirSync } from 'node:fs';","+const here = new URL('..', import.meta.url).pathname;","+const ctx = { console }; ctx.window = ctx; vm.createContext(ctx);","+vm.runInContext(readFileSync(here + 'engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'utf8'), ctx);","+const files = readdirSync(here + 'src').filter(f => f.endsWith('.js') && (f < '32' || f === '72-bot.js')).sort();","+vm.runInContext('(()=>{' + files.map(f => readFileSync(here + 'src/' + f, 'utf8')).join('\\n') + '\\n})()', ctx);","+export const B = ctx.B;"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1313,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1313,"newLines":6,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d\",\"uuid\":\"40dc76a2-c951-46b5-936b-a6e5820a5190\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d\",\"uuid\":\"98d19999-73e4-4ce4-b56c-0289553a89e1\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":250,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d\",\"uuid\":\"0f894d49-f317-4341-b22f-b9b2551875b3\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":400,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d\",\"uuid\":\"b67bdcfe-a362-400