7c666747077e\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:48:18.286Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"165/165 checks passed, 0 failed (93.6s)\\nexit-interview ok; About 12 real issues, all fixed: guards\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01K5HK4aZe1LrUiba5aQdeFS\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh8Df9aHCPqJ4555UTtP\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I re-checked each part of the goal directly. The game is finished, and all 165 checks pass on the final bundle.\\n\\n**File name.** `Bentou2BirthOfTheLunchboxAssassins-Tenchu2BirthOfTheStealthAssassins-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-183420.html` is in the folder root. It matches TASK.md's `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-183420].html` pattern, written in CamelCase like the other runs in this repo (e.g. `WireOnTheCorner-TheWire`).\\n\\n**exit-interview.json.** It parses as JSON. A script confirmed every source-information and AI Hub field is non-empty, there are 6 tags, and the 4/6/4 feedback answers are present. Its text matches the sections below.\\n\\n**No stubs.** I went beyond the keyword check (TODO, FIXME, placeholder) and also searched for empty functions and phrases like \\\"not implemented\\\". Only two empty bodies turned up, both deliberate:\\n- Bosses ignore noise, because they are always aware of you. I commented this.\\n- The empty clipboard-failure handler now shows a toast; the text-box fallback for export was already there.\\n\\n**Every TASK.md feature.** `FEATURES.md` lists each requirement with where it lives and which test covers it. I also looked at screenshots of the screens tests can't judge:\\n- **Attract mode:** the demo's labels sat under the corner menu buttons; I moved them down.\\n- **Hub card:** the four player names show in seat colors, and the countdown covered them; I moved it up.\\n- **Touch-only notice:** \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" with a Settings button.\\n- **Already shown earlier:** the Silent Cut splash, every mission, the bento screen, results, the Workshop, and About at 1080p.\\n\\nReal controller hardware is still untested; the controller was simulated by replacing the browser's gamepad API. Keyboard, mouse, a simulated DualSense, and touch emulation all pass in Chromium. The AI Hub test harness passes three ways: 2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter and packet loss; and the host leaving.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:34:20\\n- **Source:** Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins (Acquire / Activision, PlayStation, 2000)\\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Third-person ninja stealth-action with melee combat and boss duels. Isometric third person, turnable in 45° steps and zoomable, with a high three-quarter camera option.\\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine with nine small patches, AI Hub session client 1.4.0 (unmodified), plain JavaScript in one HTML file. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 with Chromium.\\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1-era pixel art (320×240, stretched to fill the screen). The characters have new masks, hats and weapons; scenes use canvas lighting, with Japanese props and materials written as shape data.\\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural character animation, plus new Silent Cut moves (5 kinds × 2 characters), grapple, riposte, ninja run, wall hug, swimming, eating, and a four-legged hound.\\n- **Audio:** The engine's chip synth. Layered Japanese-scale music (koto, shamisen, shakuhachi, fue, taiko), sound effects made in code, and a gibberish voice synth for every spoken line.\\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1–4 players, with the game's own pre-round card. Offline, the Shadow Trial lets you race your own best run.\\n- **Testing:** One command runs everything and prints only failures plus a one-line count; 165 checks pass.\\n  - Headless suites cover mechanics, all four missions completed through their objectives (an automated player fights each boss), menus, the story and ending, attract mode, Dev Mode, the Workshop, a mock AI Hub, and determinism.\\n  - Browser checks cover the bundle, an audit with a simulated DualSense, keyboard and mouse, and the real AI Hub harness.\\n- **Research:** The engine handoff docs and the AI Hub README, plus the planner's research (Wikipedia on Tenchu 2) carried in PLAN.md.\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** unknown\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 12 real issues, all fixed:\\n   - Guards counted the hero's visibility twice, so they barely noticed anyone.\\n   - The attack from above never triggered from a roof edge.\\n   - Diving was impossible: the engine's movement code undid the crouch toggle.\\n   - Guards got stuck on solid props.\\n   - A held button didn't count as activity, so attract mode could start while you held it.\\n   - Test teleports left the camera behind during slow motion.\\n   - The mouse never took over again after a gamepad was used.\\n   - The Workshop missed quick key taps.\\n   - The mouse wheel was ignored during an attack.\\n   - Plus three test-setup mistakes: rice bales in a path, a hound that smelled the tester, and Python buffering the local server's port number.\\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 3: no diving, guards stuck on props, and the double-counted visibility.\\n3. **Most helpful test:** The missions suite. It completes all four missions through their real objectives, with the automated player fighting each boss.\\n4. **Least helpful test:** The headless smoke test with random input. It passed at once because headless runs skip all drawing.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n1. **What I liked most:** How much already works headless: parkour movement, sight, suspicion and hearing, paired actions, the built-in pause and settings menus, fixed-step tests, and good-looking characters from little code.\\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes, a few times:\\n   - The movement code treats crouch as a held state, not a toggle.\\n   - Pathfinding ignores solid props.\\n   - The sight check already includes the target's visibility, so I counted it twice.\\n   - A one-step scripted press can be lost during hit-stop.\\n   - A custom input map has to restate the menu keys.\\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** The stealth layer: Shadow Sight and the Ki gauge, light maps, guard behaviour, Silent Cuts, the bosses, and the mission runtime.\\n4. **Hardest part:** Knowing how existing systems behave in a 1.2 MB engine; those details live only in the source.\\n5. **What I changed:** Nine small patches:\\n   - PlayStation button symbols in the pixel font.\\n   - A PlayStation/Xbox setting for button symbols.\\n   - Character gear: masks, two hat styles, spear, bow, club, an off-hand blade and a back banner.\\n   - Settings rows on custom menu screens.\\n   - Mouse hover moves the focus.\\n   - Interface scaling for viewing from 10 feet.\\n   - Plucked-string music notes.\\n   - A volume channel for voices.\\n   - Leaving the hub's Create + Options shortcut to the hub instead of pausing the game.\\n6. **One thing I'd change:** Make pathfinding respect solid props.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n1. **What I liked most:** It's concrete about the player: a TV at 10 feet, button symbols, attract mode, touch-only devices, dev sliders and the hub. With the detailed plan, little was left to guess.\\n2. **What was confusing:** The bracketed file-name pattern versus the plan's own names, and how to weigh \\\"every feature\\\" against a plan far larger than one session.\\n3. **Hardest thing:** The scope. A full stealth game with four bosses, an escort, a mission editor, attract mode, multiplayer and a dev mode, all tested with no stubs.\\n4. **What I'd change:** Mark which plan items are must-haves and which are stretch goals, give a session budget, give one worked example of the file name, and mention the temp-disk limit in TASK.md itself.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":530,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":663154,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":530},\"output_tokens\":753,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"65d0dba4-d8b1-427b-bda2-f14280ca26ea\",\"uuid\":\"dedbf3a8-bf0e-4428-9513-458de2b17333\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:48:39.488Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh8DepUYebsB8BqvxJyy\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184337__xe162c9/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1266,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1266,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh8Ea1YBDwFXMHo4nEB6\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2428,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":565658,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2428},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"c87f55d5-27de-4595-aefb-732ca102ecfb\",\"uuid\":\"971ca