{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghAdkkLBD3KuwKg5wEU7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Beards render on Cobb and Durgan. Fixing the prompts row overlapping the BACK label, then writing the dev-folder docs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1365,"cache_read_input_tokens":703848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1365},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5572b217-8052-4a87-b3f3-49ea658fe605","uuid":"a69fa121-dbd3-41f2-8918-b0065f6488e5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:20:05.272Z","request_id":"req_011CghAdkSDxp7cfGMiDq3JY"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghAdkkLBD3KuwKg5wEU7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019Pef8Cfg4C82s7ZkMyyGsv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-185330; sed -i \"s/if (dev !== 'mouse' \\&\\& !S.talk) B.prompts(g, game, this.prompts(game), W - 6, H - 62, 'right');/if (dev !== 'mouse' \\&\\& !S.talk) B.prompts(g, game, this.prompts(game), W - 6, H - 67, 'right');/\" src/62-ui-hud.js; grep -c \"H - 67\" src/62-ui-hud.js\ncat > PATCHES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2)\n\nEvery change to the engine copies in `engine/`, what it does and why. Each is marked `(patch)` in the source.\n\n## engine/my-3d2dge.js (2D engine)\n\n1. **Voice bus.** `ChipAudio._init` makes a third gain bus, `_voiceBus`, beside the sfx and music buses; `applyVolume`\n   sets it from `audio.voiceVolume` (0.8 by default). A new `audio.bus(name)` returns the `'sfx'`, `'music'` or `'voice'`\n   gain node. Why: the babble voice synth (50-audio.js) needs its own route and its own volume setting (Settings,\n   Sound, Voices volume).\n2. **Panned sound effects.** `audio.sfx(name, { pan })` routes the voices through a StereoPannerNode. Why: hits from the\n   flanks, monster sounds and doors are placed by their bearing from the party.\n3. **Button symbols.** The Controller setting *Button symbols* offers PlayStation (the default) and Xbox only. Why: the\n   game is designed around a DualSense; the Xbox letters are the one alternative the brief asks for.\n4. **Beards.** `E.Humanoid` takes `beard: 'full' | 'braided'`, drawn in the hair colour over the jaw before the mouth (a\n   braid hangs from the chin). Why: dwarves need beards, in the portraits and on the cards.\n\n## engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js (3D engine)\n\nNo changes. Secret and illusory walls are `world.box` blocks given the level's own wall style and colours (the box\nmaterial and the wall material are baked by the same function, at the same 16 pixels a metre), so they match the walls.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Eye of the Bolt-Holder (dev folder)\n\nA real-time, first-person party dungeon crawler inspired by Eye of the Beholder (1991), on my-3D2dge v0.85.2.\n\n- **Build:** `node tools/build.mjs` writes the single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` into the folder above.\n- **Test:** `node tests/run.mjs` (all suites; `--fast` skips the browser, harness and playthrough suites; name suites to\n  run only those). It prints only failures and one line of counts.\n- **Play:** open the built HTML file in a browser (three.js and Rapier load from jsDelivr). Controller, or keyboard and\n  mouse. Add `?backend=webgl` to force WebGL 2.\n- **Look:** `node tests/browser/look.mjs \"key=Enter;wait=800;shot=name\"` takes screenshots into `shots/`.\n\nLayout: `src/` (the game, concatenated in file order), `engine/` (the two engine files, patched: PATCHES.md), `hub/`\n(the AI Hub client, unmodified, and its harness), `tests/` (the Node harness, suites, browser checks), `tools/`.\nThe sim (files 20-31) is pure and deterministic: it never touches the view, the DOM, sound or `Math.random`.\nEOF\ncat > CONTENT.md <<'EOF'\n# Content formats (for designers)\n\nAll content is data in `src/1x-data-*.js`. The lint suite checks every id and coordinate.\n\n## Floors (`15-data-floors.js`)\n- `map`: one character a cell. `#` wall, `.` floor, `@` start, `<` `>` stairs, `+` door, `=` gate, `L` `K` locked door,\n  `M` magic seal, `H` secret wall, `I` illusory wall, `P` plate, `T` dart trap, `O` pit, `o` trapdoor, `^` teleporter,\n  `S` spinner, `U` the Undergate, `*` pit landing, `B` the boss.\n- `doors: { id: { at: [x, y], key, kind: 'simple' | 'warded', seal, undergate } }`, `plates: { id: { at, mode: 'hold' |\n  'latch' } }`, `pits`, `teleports: { id: { at, to: [x, y, dir], silent } }`, `secrets`, `illusions`, `traps`,\n  `stairs: { 'x,y': { to, at: [x, y, dir] } | { sealed } | { exit } }`, `fall: { to, at }`, `safe: [[x, y]]`.\n- `features: [[id, kind, x, y, face, options]]`: the feature on the wall `face` (N E S W) of the open cell (x, y).\n  Kinds: lever, button, catch, alcove (`holds`, `accepts`, `shrine`, `riddle`), inscription (`text`), torch, candle,\n  greatLock, gearNiche, clockFace, shrine, undergate, altarSlab, and decor (pipe, grate, chain, cage, gearWall, eyeRelief).\n- `items: [[x, y, itemId, count]]`, `mons: [[type, x, y, count, { id, asleep, patrol, drop }]]`,\n  `wanderers: { budget, types: [[type, n]], at: [[x, y]] }`.\n- `wires: [{ when, mode, once, do, fail, undo }]`. Triggers: `lever`, `levers` + `is`, `catch`, `buttons` + `within`,\n  `plate`, `plates`, `alcove` + `accepts` | `kind`, `killed`, `hurt` + `below`, `flag`, `opened`, `gears`, `wards`,\n  `sequence`. Actions: `open` `close` `toggle` (door), `story`, `take`, `special`, `give`, `place`, `msg`, `secret`,\n  `reveal`, `hint`, `hintAfter`, `spawn`, `teleporter`, `xpSecret`, `sfx`, `bridge`, `return`, `clock`, `candlesOut`,\n  `music`, `race`, `bossWake`, `flag`, `join`, `quest`, `veilHelp`.\n- `events: [{ at: [x, y] | area: [x0, y0, x1, y1], once, do }]`, `hints`, `waypoints` (Dev Mode's warps).\n- `look`: ground and wall colours, side style, fog, ambient light.\n\n## Items, monsters, spells (`10-data-items.js`, `11-data-rules.js`)\nAn item is `IT(id, name, kind, { dmg, speed, hit, cls, two, reach, throw, blunt, ammo, stack, def, icon, color, desc })`;\nicons are 12x12 strings in `61-ui-kit.js` (`B.ICON_ART`). Monsters list size, HP, Defense, attack, damage, interval,\nmove time, sight, XP, specials and drops. Spells give level, target and description; their effects are in 27-sim-magic.js.\n\n## Text and stories (`14-data-text.js`)\nStories are `{ lines: [[speaker, text]], choices: [{ label, reply, do }], do, bark }`. Speakers carry a rig for the\nportrait and a voice profile (`B.VOICES` in 50-audio.js). Hints may name actions in braces, `{strike}`, which show as the\nplayer's own buttons.\n\n## The walkthrough (`69-bot.js`)\n`B.WALK[floor]` is the bot's plan: `go`, `use`, `openDoor`, `grabAt`, `loot`, `hold`, `stow`, `put`, `throw`, `zap`,\n`wait`, `clear`, `rest`, `rest4`, `retry`, `branch`, `boss`. The playthrough test and the attract mode use it.\nEOF\nls","description":"Move prompts up; write PATCHES, README, CONTENT docs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1365,"cache_read_input_tokens":703848,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1365},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5572b217-8052-4a87-b3f3-49ea658fe605","uuid":"3eb67150-f7d3-4c3f-8411-775798394361","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:20:29.921Z","request_id":"req_011CghAdkSDxp7cfGMiDq3JY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019Pef8Cfg4C82s7ZkMyyGsv":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-185330; sed -i \"s/if (dev !== 'mouse' \\&\\& !S.talk) B.prompts(g, game, this.prompts(game), W - 6, H - 62, 'right');/if (dev !== 'mouse' \\&\\& !S.talk) B.prompts(g, game, this.prompts(game), W - 6, H - 67, 'right');/\" src/62-ui-hud.js; grep -c \"H - 67\" src/62-ui-hud.js\ncat > PATCHES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2)\n\nEvery change to the engine copies in `engine/`, what it does and why. Each is marked `(patch)` in the source.\n\n## engine/my-3d2dge.js (2D engine)\n\n1. **Voice bus.** `ChipAudio._init` makes a third gain bus, `_voiceBus`, beside the sfx and music buses; `applyVolume`\n   sets it from `audio.voiceVolume` (0.8 by default). A new `audio.bus(name)` returns the `'sfx'`, `'music'` or `'voice'`\n   gain node. Why: the babble voice synth (50-audio.js) needs its own route and its own volume setting (Settings,\n   Sound, Voices volume).\n2. **Panned sound effects.** `audio.sfx(name, { pan })` routes the voices through a StereoPannerNode. Why: hits from the\n   flanks, monster sounds and doors are placed by their bearing from the party.\n3. **Button symbols.** The Controller setting *Button symbols* offers PlayStation (the default) and Xbox only. Why: the\n   game is designed around a DualSense; the Xbox letters are the one alternative the brief asks for.\n4. **Beards.** `E.Humanoid` takes `beard: 'full' | 'braided'`, drawn in the hair colour over the jaw before the mouth (a\n   braid hangs from the chin). Why: dwarves need beards, in the portraits and on the cards.\n\n## engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js (3D engine)\n\nNo changes. Secret and illusory walls are `world.box` blocks given the level's own wall style and colours (the box\nmaterial and the wall material are baked by the same function, at the same 16 pixels a metre), so they match the walls.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Eye of the Bolt-Holder (dev folder)\n\nA real-time, first-person party dungeon crawler inspired by Eye of the Beholder (1991), on my-3D2dge v0.85.2.\n\n- **Build:** `node tools/build.mjs` writes the single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` into the folder above.\n- **Test:** `node tests/run.mjs` (all suites; `--fast` skips the browser, harness and playthrough suites; name suites to\n  run only those). It prints only failures and one line of counts.\n- **Play:** open the built HTML file in a browser (three.js and Rapier load from jsDelivr). Controller, or keyboard and\n  mouse. Add `?backend=webgl` to force WebGL 2.\n- **Look:** `node tests/browser/look.mjs \"key=Enter;wait=800;shot=name\"` takes screenshots into `shots/`.\n\nLayout: `src/` (the game, concatenated in file order), `engine/` (the two engine files, patched: PATCHES.md), `hub/`\n(the AI Hub client, unmodified, and its harness), `tests/` (the Node harness, suites, browser checks), `tools/`.\nThe sim (files 20-31) is pure and deterministic: it never touches the view, the DOM, sound or `Math.random`.\nEOF\ncat > CONTENT.md <<'EOF'\n# Content formats (for designers)\n\nAll content is data in `src/1x-data-*.js`. The lint suite checks every id and coordinate.\n\n## Floors (`15-data-floors.js`)\n- `map`: one character a cell. `#` wall, `.` floor, `@` start, `<` `>` stairs, `+` door, `=` gate, `L` `K` locked door,\n  `M` magic seal, `H` secret wall, `I` illusory wall, `P` plate, `T` dart trap, `O` pit, `o` trapdoor, `^` teleporter,\n  `S` spinner, `U` the Undergate, `*` pit landing, `B` the boss.\n- `doors: { id: { at: [x, y], key, kind: 'simple' | 'warded', seal, undergate } }`, `plates: { id: { at, mode: 'hold' |\n  'latch' } }`, `pits`, `teleports: { id: { at, to: [x, y, dir], silent } }`, `secrets`, `illusions`, `traps`,\n  `stairs: { 'x,y': { to, at: [x, y, dir] } | { sealed } | { exit } }`, `fall: { to, at }`, `safe: [[x, y]]`.\n- `features: [[id, kind, x, y, face, options]]`: the feature on the wall `face` (N E S W) of the open cell (x, y).\n  Kinds: lever, button, catch, alcove (`holds`, `accepts`, `shrine`, `riddle`), inscription (`text`), torch, candle,\n  greatLock, gearNiche, clockFace, shrine, undergate, altarSlab, and decor (pipe, grate, chain, cage, gearWall, eyeRelief).\n- `items: [[x, y, itemId, count]]`, `mons: [[type, x, y, count, { id, asleep, patrol, drop }]]`,\n  `wanderers: { budget, types: [[type, n]], at: [[x, y]] }`.\n- `wires: [{ when, mode, once, do, fail, undo }]`. Triggers: `lever`, `levers` + `is`, `catch`, `buttons` + `within`,\n  `plate`, `plates`, `alcove` + `accepts` | `kind`, `killed`, `hurt` + `below`, `flag`, `opened`, `gears`, `wards`,\n  `sequence`. Actions: `open` `close` `toggle` (door), `story`, `take`, `special`, `give`, `place`, `msg`, `secret`,\n  `reveal`, `hint`, `hintAfter`, `spawn`, `teleporter`, `xpSecret`, `sfx`, `bridge`, `return`, `clock`, `candlesOut`,\n  `music`, `race`, `bossWake`, `flag`, `join`, `quest`, `veilHelp`.\n- `events: [{ at: [x, y] | area: [x0, y0, x1, y1], once, do }]`, `hints`, `waypoints` (Dev Mode's warps).\n- `look`: ground and wall colours, side style, fog, ambient light.\n\n## Items, monsters, spells (`10-data-items.js`, `11-data-rules.js`)\nAn item is `IT(id, name, kind, { dmg, speed, hit, cls, two, reach, throw, blunt, ammo, stack, def, icon, color, desc })`;\nicons are 12x12 strings in `61-ui-kit.js` (`B.ICON_ART`). Monsters list size, HP, Defense, attack, damage, interval,\nmove time, sight, XP, specials and drops. Spells give level, target and description; their effects are in 27-sim-magic.js.\n\n## Text and stories (`14-data-text.js`)\nStories are `{ lines: [[speaker, text]], choices: [{ label, reply, do }], do, bark }`. Speakers carry a rig for the\nportrait and a voice profile (`B.VOICES` in 50-audio.js). Hints may name actions in braces, `{strike}`, which show as the\nplayer's own buttons.\n\n## The walkthrough (`69-bot.js`)\n`B.WALK[floor]` is the bot's plan: `go`, `use`, `openDoor`, `grabAt`, `loot`, `hold`, `stow`, `put`, `throw`, `zap`,\n`wait`, `clear`, `rest`, `rest4`, `retry`, `branch`, `boss`. The playthrough test and the attract mode use it.\nEOF\nls","description":"Move prompts up; write PATCHES, README, CONTENT docs"}}}
