{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML, exit-interview.json (valid JSON with all required fields) and the four required sections are present, and no TODO/placeholder hits remain. But the transcript does not show every TASK.md feature implemented: the final reply still calls the cutscenes 'simple' earlier in the session and the Art Direction and Animation sections say the creatures and mechanisms are built 'from simple shapes', and the Testing Feedback claims 'every failure it found was a real game bug' and that the game 'now wins all 32 seeds', while the 32-seed sweep was run on a mix of seeds that were tuned against during the same session. Several TASK.md items remain unverified in the transcript: the Xbox setting's ✕-to-A mapping was only tested in Node, the touch-only checks run on a stub, and the plan's 1920x1080 filmstrip review and drag-and-drop for all items are only partly covered. The condition's 'no stubs' requirement is therefore not clearly satisfied by transcript evidence."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5572b217-8052-4a87-b3f3-49ea658fe605","uuid":"1388dd85-7362-424f-aa40-91266ad5cf55","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:08:39.652Z","isSynthetic":true}
