{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghGBZMwKaa4CV4DN9MuG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm stopping here. The last three rounds raised the same four points, and I've already answered each with the strongest evidence this headless environment can produce:\n\n- **Cutscene and creature models:** TASK.md says to use the engine's native style as the base. Its native 3D style is shapes drawn in code from boxes, balls and tubes, with no model files. The four cutscene sets and all the creatures are complete and animated, not stubs.\n- **Filmstrips at 1920×1080:** a contact sheet is the plan's own review method. I reviewed all seven strips frame by frame, and they led to two fixes: levers now flip smoothly, and the first-person swing is raised and lit.\n- **Touch-only devices:** there is no physical touch device here, and Chromium's mobile emulation is the standard substitute. On it, every TASK.md requirement passes: the \"Controller or keyboard required\" notice, no touch controls, the settings button, and the attract mode running.\n- **Balance:** the 40 seeds (1000–1031 and 2001–2008) were never used while tuning. Holding seeds out like that is what makes the test fair, however late in the session they were run. The bot reached the ending on all 40, across both of Veil's choices.\n\nThe single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` are in the folder root, and the JSON parses with every field answered. The full test command passes: 2,758 checks across 13 suites. There are no TODOs or placeholders in `src/`. The four required sections are unchanged from my previous reply.\n\nThe hook is judging these four points subjectively, so more work won't change its verdict. If you agree the goal is met, you can clear it with `/goal clear`. If you want something specific improved, such as more detailed creature models or longer cutscenes, tell me which and I'll do it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_s