et walls needed blocks matched to the wall material.\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** a deterministic simulation with no drawing code, a bot that plays it, and one menu system shared by controller, keyboard and mouse.\n4. **Hardest part:** keeping the 3D view, the 2D overlay, input and the pause menu in step across many screens.\n5. **What I changed in the engine, and why:** four small 2D-engine patches, listed in PATCHES.md:\n   - a voice volume channel;\n   - sound panning by direction;\n   - PlayStation and Xbox as the only button-symbol sets;\n   - beards on character rigs.\n\n   The 3D engine is unchanged.\n6. **One thing I'd change:** a built-in grid-crawler layer (cells, wall features, doors and secret walls that share the wall material).\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** concrete deliverables, and a complete plan to check against.\n2. **What was confusing:** the plan is far larger than one session, and it wasn't clear which of its quantities were required.\n3. **Hardest thing:** a real-time crawler that a bot can reliably beat but that stays fair for people, inside a 10-foot, controller-first UI.\n4. **What I'd change:** state a time or token budget, and say which plan items may be cut for quantity."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2419,"cache_read_input_tokens":904124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2419},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5572b217-8052-4a87-b3f3-49ea658fe605","uuid":"8f98f791-4739-40d3-98cf-b1c7995b83f9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:08:49.267Z","request_id":"req_011CghJuzEKGpLNgY7tYyFRP"}
